{"data":[{"slug":"manager-agent-architecture-452885","company_name":"parloa","title":"Manager, Agent Architecture","description":"&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Parloa&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Parloa&#39;s mission is to make every customer conversation feel effortless for both customers and the companies serving them. As agentic AI accelerates, Parloans are shaping the foundation of a new era in customer experience, one where customer support is no longer transactions, but meaningful exchanges. It is not just a vision; Parloa has powered over ONE BILLION interactions between global enterprise brands and their customers, with companies like Booking.com, HealthEquity, Allianz, SAP, BarmeniaGothaer, and TUI already deploying Parloa at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As &lt;strong&gt;Manager, Agent Architecture&lt;/strong&gt;, you will build and lead the team that transforms customer service with AI Agents, while staying in the build yourself. You run a team of Agent Architects: you hire them, coach them, set their goals, and own the quality of every AI Agent they ship, with a significant portion of your capacity on live customer engagements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is your opportunity to lead at the front line of enterprise AI, where your credibility comes from doing the work alongside your team, not just directing it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Areas of ownership:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Own hiring for Agent Architect roles, run weekly 1:1s, performance reviews, and career conversations, and build development plans that help each person grow. Set ramp expectations for new hires and coach Associate and mid-level Agent Architects on prompt engineering, conversation design, and customer-facing judgment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Capacity and Stakeholder Alignment:&lt;/strong&gt; Set team goals and OKRs aligned with Professional Services priorities, manage capacity and workload across concurrent engagements, and surface resourcing tradeoffs early. Represent the Agent Architecture team to Sales, Product, Engineering, customers, and partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on Agent Delivery:&lt;/strong&gt; Personally guide customers through AI Agent implementations, from strategic advice to scoping to end-to-end delivery. Serve as the escalation point when agent performance degrades.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quality and Best Practices:&lt;/strong&gt; Define what good looks like for agent quality, enforce it through review, and make it repeatable across every live project. Document best practices for internal and external audiences, and turn recurring field problems into structured feedback for Product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading people, whether as a formal manager, team lead, or through sustained mentorship where you owned a group&#39;s growth and output. First-time managers with a strong coaching track record are welcome.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of conversation design and AI agent development experience, with a track record of building scalable solution architecture and conversational experiences grounded in real user needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled in advanced prompt engineering, comfortable integrating REST APIs and working with Javascript.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project and stakeholder management skills, with significant experience working with enterprise customers, including in escalated or high-pressure situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment on capacity and prioritization: you can say what your team can and cannot absorb, and back it up with reasoning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our recruiting process:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Talent Acquisition → Hiring Manager → Technical Interview(s) → Bar Raiser&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Parloa?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re at the beginning of a new era in customer experience, one where AI doesn&#39;t just respond, but understands, reasons, and takes action. We&#39;re building agentic AI that enterprises trust with their most important customer moments: complex questions, high volumes, real stakes. When millions of people reach out to a brand, those interactions aren&#39;t just support tickets; they&#39;re defining experiences. We&#39;re here to raise the standard: making every conversation seamless, intelligent, and genuinely helpful. If you care about shaping how businesses and customers connect at scale and want your work to matter in real, everyday moments, this is where you do it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Parloa, ownership isn&#39;t a buzzword; it means being accountable for outcomes, not just tasks. We operate in a category that&#39;s evolving fast, where the bar is high, and the problems are complex. We hire people who think in solutions, communicate with clarity, and follow through. People who are comfortable making decisions, taking responsibility, and raising the standard for themselves and those around them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;ve grown beyond the earliest startup phase, but we&#39;ve kept the intensity: fast execution, direct feedback, and a strong expectation to contribute meaningfully from day one.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Backed by leading global investors like General Catalyst, EQT Ventures, and Altimeter Capital, we&#39;re scaling with a clear ambition: to become the global category leader in enterprise-grade conversational AI.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;iframe style=&quot;display: table; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/embed/P4d-iyx7RQM&quot; width=&quot;560&quot; height=&quot;314&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Parloa is committed to upholding the highest data protection standards for our clients&#39; and employees&#39; data. All our employees are instrumental in ensuring the utmost care, GDPR, and ISO compliance, including ISO 27001, in handling sensitive information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Parloa is an e-verify employer in the USA. &lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.e-verify.gov/about-e-verify/what-is-e-verify&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.e-verify.gov/about-e-verify/what-is-e-verify&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Please click here to learn more&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;* &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We provide equal opportunities to all qualified applicants regardless race, gender, sexual orientation, age, religion, national origin, disability status, socioeconomic background and other characteristics.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/parloa/manager-agent-architecture-452885","tags":["Professional Services"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1792486520},{"slug":"staff-site-reliability-engineer-wiesbaden-germany-relocation-provided-197778","company_name":"Onebrief","title":"Staff Site Reliability Engineer (Wiesbaden, Germany) - Relocation Provided","description":"<h2><em>Consequential Work. Dedicated People.</em></h2><h2><br /><strong>About Onebrief</strong><br /></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Onebrief builds collaboration and AI-powered workflow software for military planning and operational coordination.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Military planning is complex by nature, requiring teams to coordinate information, people, and decisions across systems and locations. Onebrief brings planning, collaboration, simulation, and AI into one connected environment, helping teams test strategies, adapt to changing conditions, and make decisions with greater clarity when the stakes are real.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a distributed team of builders from military, operational, and technology backgrounds who care deeply about improving how important work gets done. Some team members work remotely, while others work directly alongside customers in operational environments around the world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in 2019, Onebrief is backed by leading investors including General Catalyst, Battery Ventures, Insight Partners, Sapphire Ventures, and Human Capital. Valued at more than $2 billion, we continue to invest in product innovation, AI capabilities, and team growth.</p><h1><strong>About the Role</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are hiring a Site Reliability Engineer to support Onebrief deployments across on-premises hardware, virtualized systems, and cloud environments.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on infrastructure role focused on Linux administration, hardware maintenance, and application reliability. You will manage Linux servers, NVIDIA DGX Spark or similar AI computing systems, rack-mounted equipment, and the applications running on them. You will also support workloads deployed on virtual machines, Kubernetes, and cloud infrastructure.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your primary responsibility is keeping these environments operational and maintaining a <strong>99.5% application availability target</strong>. You will troubleshoot production issues, perform routine maintenance, and work with engineering teams to improve system reliability.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will work primarily on-site with military customers in Wiesbaden, Germany, alongside Onebrief Outcome Engineers, Mission Success, GRC, and Infrastructure teams. Some environments have limited connectivity or operate on air-gapped networks, requiring practical troubleshooting skills and careful planning for maintenance and deployments.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Security Clearance, Location, and Onsite Requirements</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role requires regular on-site work at customer locations in and around Wiesbaden, Germany. Relocation assistance is available.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">An active Top Secret clearance is required, with the ability to obtain SCI eligibility. Active Security+ (or another DoD 8570.01-approved credential) is required, or the ability to obtain one within 30 days of hire.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>About You</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have a strong background in Linux systems administration and experience supporting production applications. You are comfortable working directly with server hardware, troubleshooting operating system issues, and diagnosing application failures. You understand how infrastructure problems affect the software running on it and know how to narrow down the cause of an outage.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You take responsibility for the systems you maintain and communicate clearly when problems arise. You can work independently at a customer site while collaborating with remote engineering teams. You value good documentation, practical automation, and fixing recurring problems.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Maintain Linux systems and hardware:</strong> Install, configure, patch, and troubleshoot Linux servers, NVIDIA DGX Spark or similar GPU systems, rack-mounted equipment, and virtual machines. Handle hardware diagnostics, firmware updates, and routine maintenance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Operate production applications:</strong> Deploy, monitor, upgrade, and troubleshoot applications running on Linux, virtual machines, Kubernetes, and cloud infrastructure. Work with software engineers to resolve application issues and improve deployment processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Maintain application availability:</strong> Work toward a 99.5% uptime target across assigned environments. Monitor application and system health, respond to alerts, investigate performance issues, and address problems before they cause extended outages.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Respond to incidents:</strong> Diagnose hardware, operating system, network, and application failures. Restore service, coordinate escalations, and document root causes and corrective actions through After Action Reviews (AARs).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Improve operations through automation:</strong> Use scripting and configuration management tools to simplify deployments, patching, monitoring, and recovery. Support secure operations in cloud, on-premises, and air-gapped environments.</p></li></ul><h1><strong>What We Look For</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Active Top Secret clearance, with the ability to obtain SCI eligibility.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years of experience in Linux systems administration, SRE, infrastructure engineering, or a related role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong Linux administration and troubleshooting skills, including networking, storage, system performance, and security configuration.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience maintaining physical servers and troubleshooting hardware failures.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience supporting production applications on Linux servers, virtual machines, or containers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with Docker and Kubernetes, including application deployments and basic troubleshooting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understanding of networking fundamentals, including TCP/IP, DNS, routing, and firewalls.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with monitoring, incident response, and root cause analysis.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to automate routine administration tasks using Bash or Python.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have qualifications</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of at least one cloud platform, preferably AWS or Oracle Cloud Infrastructure (OCI).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with NVIDIA DGX Spark, GPU servers, or similar AI computing hardware.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with virtualization platforms such as VMware, Proxmox, or Nutanix.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with infrastructure automation tools such as Terraform or Ansible.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with Prometheus, Grafana, Loki, or similar monitoring tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience supporting systems in DoD, classified, or air-gapped environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with DoD security requirements, including STIGs and RMF.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with CI/CD pipelines, GitOps, or Kubernetes administration.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Relevant certifications such as RHCSA, RHCE, CKA, or AWS certifications.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><br />Notice to Third Party Recruitment Agencies</strong><br />Please note that Onebrief does not accept unsolicited resumes from recruiters or employment agencies. In the absence of an executed Recruitment Services Agreement, there will be no obligation to any referral compensation or recruiter fee. In the event a recruiter or agency submits a resume or candidate without an agreement Onebrief explicitly reserves the right to pursue and hire those candidate(s) without any financial obligation to the recruiter or agency. Any unsolicited resumes, including those submitted to hiring managers, shall be deemed the property of Onebrief.</p><hr><p>Compensation: $205K – $250K • Offers Equity</p><ul><li> • $205K – $250K • Offers Equity</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/onebrief/staff-site-reliability-engineer-wiesbaden-germany-relocation-provided-197778","tags":["Infrastructure & Security"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Wiesbaden, Germany","created_at":1792485617},{"slug":"sales-customer-support-specialist-emea-munich-germany-354150","company_name":"Zello","title":"Sales & Customer Support Specialist EMEA (m/w/d)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>IMPORTANT: Please be aware, scammers may try to impersonate Zello by reaching out regarding job opportunities. We will never ask you for bank account information, checks, or other sensitive information as part of our hiring process. All correspondence will come from the zello.com email domain. If you’re unsure, please email ----- with questions. </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About Zello</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Zello is a voice-first communication platform, powered by our industry-leading push-to-talk technology, to improve collaboration and productivity for desk-less workers. With over 175+ million users, we’re the #1 rated push-to-talk app in the world, delivering 9 billion (yes, with a B) messages a month. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Zello, our company values are at the heart of what we do everyday. We’re proud to serve the frontline, we’re privileged to connect people in times of crisis across the globe, and we’re honored to support first responders.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">And this is where you come in.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Zello keeps frontline teams connected with instant push-to-talk voice. Our customer base across Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and Asia-Pacific is growing faster than separate sales and support queues can keep up with. This role owns the inbound experience for those customers end to end, from the first pricing question to the first support ticket, so new customers buy faster and stay longer. You'll be based in Munich, report to our Sales Leader EMEA, and work closely with our Account Executives, Support, and Customer Success teams.</p><h2><strong>After a successful first year, you will</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have owned inbound EMEA and APAC leads end to end, responding to every new inquiry within one business day and converting at least 20% of qualified leads into paying customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have closed a steady monthly run-rate of new SMB deals and plan upgrades, with every opportunity tracked accurately in HubSpot.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have resolved at least 80% of support tickets on first contact, with customer satisfaction at or above team target.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have built a library of macros, setup guides, and FAQ answers that measurably reduced repeat tickets on the most common topics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have handed off at least 10 qualified expansion opportunities to Account Executives, becoming a reliable source of enterprise pipeline.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What you'll do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Respond to inbound inquiries, demo requests, and trial sign-ups from across EMEA and APAC, qualify them, and close SMB deals and plan upgrades.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run demos and onboarding calls in English, showing frontline teams how Zello fits the way they already work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work the support queue in HubSpot: troubleshoot account, channel, and device issues across Android, iOS, rugged handsets, and PTT accessories.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Escalate what you can't solve to Tier 2 and Engineering with clean reproduction steps, and close the loop with the customer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep HubSpot accurate, with every contact, deal, and ticket logged and a clear next step.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Spot customers outgrowing self-serve and hand them to Account Executives with the context they need to win.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn recurring questions into help content and macros, and feed customer feedback back to Product.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Who you are</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've spent 2+ years in a role that combined selling and supporting customers, such as inside sales, SaaS support, or customer success, and can point to deals you closed and customers you kept.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You speak and write fluent English. Another language is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're based in Munich, or ready to be.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You troubleshoot hands-on: you're comfortable setting up Android and iOS devices, two-way radios or rugged handsets, and working through Wi-Fi, LTE, or Bluetooth issues until it works.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've worked in HubSpot or a comparable CRM and ticketing tool, and you keep your records clean without being chased.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You explain technical things in plain language to people who aren't technical, like a warehouse supervisor or a dispatcher mid-shift.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You follow through: when you tell a customer you'll get back to them, you do, and they remember it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You raise problems early and share what you learn, so the next ticket or deal goes faster for the whole team.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>This Role Is Not</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A pure support role measured only on ticket volume. Sales outcomes are half the job.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An enterprise Account Executive role. Large, multi-stakeholder deals go to the AE team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A Tier 3 engineering role. You diagnose and escalate; you don't fix code.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A people management role.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We hire for potential, passion for our mission, and a knack for solving difficult problems over checking every qualification box. We have competitive pay, equity with significant upside, and intentionally design our benefits to encourage healthy and well-balanced employees, flexible schedules and time off. We even offer a sabbatical after every five years of service so you’re able to pursue and enjoy what matters most to you. And of course, we wouldn’t be a technology company without a ping-pong table and free snacks in our break room. Join us!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Zello provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws.</em><br /><br />All Zello personnel are required to comply with defined security, privacy, and compliance requirements applicable to their role along with requirements that are applicable to all Zello personnel.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/zello/sales-customer-support-specialist-emea-munich-germany-354150","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Munich, Germany","created_at":1792485617},{"slug":"senior-talent-partner-space-tech-scale-up-germany-194440","company_name":"pplwise","title":"Senior Talent Partner - Space-Tech scale-up","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About pplwise</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">pplwise helps leading, fast-growing companies reach their growth goals. Our services include Recruiting as a Service and Executive Search, and we specialise in technology companies in their growth phases.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work with publicly listed companies such as Uber and Just Eat Takeaway, unicorns such as Clark, TIER and Taxfix, and many startups and scale-ups backed by top venture capital firms like Sequoia Capital, HV Capital and Cherry Ventures.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in 2021, pplwise operates in more than 20 countries and has a team of over 40 Talent Partners who help ambitious tech companies through their growth stages.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Senior Talent Partner (m/f/d)</strong><br /><strong>Location:</strong> Remote, Germany<br /><strong>Engagement:</strong> Freelance or full-time. The initial project runs about 6 months, with a follow-up project likely.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The project</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll be embedded in the recruiting team of a fast-growing space-tech company, helping them build out their organisation. You'll hire for the functions you know best: technical, go-to-market or general business roles.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Getting started</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In your first two weeks, you'll check in daily with your pplwise lead and teammates. That way you'll quickly get comfortable working independently with pplwise's principles, frameworks and methods, and you'll get to know the team. Part of your onboarding happens with pplwise and part with the client.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">By the end of those two weeks, you'll have a solid grasp of the client's vision, strategy and culture. You'll also know the goals of the teams and the roles you'll be hiring for. You'll have built relationships with the hiring managers and their teams, and you'll have put together a delivery forecast using the pplwise methodology.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">From there you'll take ownership of your roles, build pipelines and proactively share insights with key stakeholders so bottlenecks are spotted and dealt with early.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the client's hiring goals end to end, in tech roles or in go-to-market and business roles.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Source and engage candidates across the German market, using your network and market knowledge.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage stakeholders proactively, acting as a strategic partner who spots bottlenecks and solves them through clear communication and critical thinking.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and run hiring forecasts. Choose the right channels and strategies, with a clear sense of urgency and backward planning.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use recruiting systems and data to drive decisions before and during each search.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver an excellent candidate experience from first contact to offer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with the wider pplwise team, giving and getting support on sourcing or delivery bottlenecks.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Several years of full-cycle recruiting in startups, scale-ups or other high-growth environments. Agency experience is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong knowledge of the German talent market.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An understanding of how tech organisations are structured at different growth stages, and the ability to help hiring managers define roles.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort working independently in a fast-paced, ambiguous environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Decisions based on data and facts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High standards for stakeholder satisfaction.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An ambitious, collaborative mindset.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent German and very good English, written and spoken.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we offer</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A dynamic, high-impact project helping a fast-growing space-tech company scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fully remote work with flexibility and autonomy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive pay, either an hourly rate (freelance) or a salary (full-time).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A talented, ambitious and collaborative team of Talent Partners to work alongside.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The pplwise playbook, frameworks and training to help you deliver at a consistently high standard.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">pplwise actively fosters a diverse and inclusive environment that values every candidate's individuality. We are committed to equal opportunity throughout our hiring process, regardless of nationality, ethnic or national origin, colour, religion, disability, sex, sexual orientation or gender identity.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Don't tick every box? We'd still love to hear from you 🚀</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/pplwise/senior-talent-partner-space-tech-scale-up-germany-194440","tags":["🏡 work with us"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Germany","created_at":1792485616},{"slug":"senior-hr-business-partner-focus-rd-gilching-471536","company_name":"Quantum-Systems GmbH","title":"Senior HR Business Partner (m/f/d) – Focus R&D","description":"<p><strong>Quantum Systems is a leading European deep-tech company for unmanned systems across air, land and maritime domains.</strong> We develop and scale integrated hardware, software and AI-powered solutions for mission-critical operations.</p><p>At Quantum Systems, you’ll work alongside experts across disciplines, take ownership from day one and help turn ambitious ideas into technology with real-world impact. We move fast, think beyond boundaries and give our teams the space to shape what comes next.</p><p><strong>The Future is Unmanned - But the responsibi