wth-manager-berlin-200241","company_name":"Platform Engineering Masters","title":"Senior Events Growth Manager","description":"<h2>About Platform Engineering</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Platform Engineering (<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://platformengineering.org">platformengineering.org</a>) is home to the world's largest community of platform engineers. Through PlatformCon and AgenticCon, one of the world's largest conferences dedicated to platform engineering, we bring together thousands of platform engineers, platform leaders every year. Alongside our events, we run a university, a newsletter read by hundreds of thousands of engineers, and Weave Intelligence, our research arm.<br /></p><h2>About the Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for an Events Growth Marketing Manager to own registration and attendance growth across our entire events portfolio. That starts with our flagship conferences, PlatformCon and AgenticCon, the biggest conferences in the platform engineering world, which travel to San Francisco, London, Sydney, New York and Berlin, and extends to our roadshows, roundtables, workshops, House of Kube (the largest party in the cloud native world) and the satellite events we run in cities around major conferences such as AWS re:Invent, KubeCon and Google Cloud Next. Your goal is to bring platform engineering leaders into the room and keep them coming back. This is a systems and relationships role, not a one off campaign role. You’ll build the growth loops, the audience, and the repeatable playbook needed to fill these events and drive high attendance every time. You’ll report to the Head of Growth.<br /></p><h2>What you'll do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own registration and attendance growth for PlatformCon and AgenticCon ticket sales, and for every other event we run, across San Francisco, London, Sydney, New York, Berlin and Amsterdam.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build growth loops and long term relationships with the platform engineering community, its practitioners and its leaders, so we have an audience to pull from in every city.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own our event pages on Luma and the end to end campaigns that fill them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plan campaigns designed for a high attendance rate, so the right people do not just register but actually show up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use HubSpot and Luma to build and target the right audience segments for each event.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with design team to ensure high quality event pages and with content for strong copy and assets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Brief and work with our performance marketing and lifecycle managers to get paid and email support behind each event.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the systems and the playbook that let us fill these events repeatedly, so the approach compounds instead of starting from scratch each time.</p></li></ul><h2>What success looks like</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Within your first 90 days, we want you to come back to us with a proposed playbook: how we should run our in person events, and the exact workflow you would follow every time a new event brief lands, from audience to event page to campaigns to attendance. By 180 days, we want that playbook proven on live events, with a rising attendance rate and a reusable audience building in each city.<br /></p><h2>What you'll bring</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A systems thinker who works in growth loops, not one off tactics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in B2B SaaS marketing. Even better if you have worked somewhere whose core business is running events.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of building and growing audiences and driving real attendance at in person events, not just registrations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong hands on experience with CRM tools such as HubSpot for segmentation and targeting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort running social campaigns and briefing paid campaigns.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to work independently with complete ownership, and to build a repeatable system rather than firefighting each event.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with the design team to produce strong event visuals, both for our Luma pages and website pages, so every event looks as good as it performs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable with occasional travel to our event cities when an event calls for it.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to have</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with Luma as an event platform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience marketing events for a company whose primary business is events.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">You do not need experience with data or automation tooling such as zapier, n8n or similar data flow systems. Our ops team supports all of that.<br /></p><h2>Why join us?</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We run the biggest and most influential events in the platform engineering world. PlatformCon and AgenticCon are the flagship conferences of the entire space, and they travel to San Francisco, London, Sydney, New York and Berlin, alongside a full calendar of roadshows, executive roundtables, AI Platform Leaders events and House of Kube, the largest party in the cloud native world. These rooms bring together senior platform and engineering leaders from some of the biggest companies on the planet, including many from the S&amp;P 500. You would own the growth of all of it end to end, with the mandate to build the audience and the playbook that make these events repeatable, and direct access to the Head of Growth and the wider leadership team.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/platform-engineering-masters/senior-events-growth-manager-berlin-200241","tags":["Growth Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1792474819},{"slug":"strategy-lead-acquisition-berlin-72070","company_name":"iwoca Deutschland","title":"Strategy Lead - Acquisition","description":"<h2>The company</h2><p>Small businesses move fast. Opportunities often don’t wait, and cash flow pressures can appear overnight. To keep going, and growing, SMEs need finance that’s as flexible and responsive as they are.</p><p>That's why we built iwoca. Our smart technology, data science and five-star customer service ensures business owners can act with the speed, confidence and control they need, exactly when it's needed.</p><p>We’ve already cleared the way for 100,000 businesses with more than £4 billion in funding. Our passionate team is driven to help even more SMEs succeed, through access to better finance and other services that make running a business easier. Our ultimate mission is to support one million SMEs in their defining moments, creating lasting impact for the communities and economies they drive.</p><h2>The team</h2><p>The Acquisition Strategy and Tech team is the integrated growth engine for iwoca in Germany. We bridge the gap between high-level commercial strategy and the technical systems that power our customer journey. By combining growth analytics, performance modeling, and full-stack engineering, we own the end-to-end acquisition funnel – from the very first touchpoint to a completed loan application. Our Core Focus:</p><p>Strategic Growth & Analytics: We serve as the central hub for our Direct Marketing and Sales channels. We translate complex data into actionable strategies, ensuring our outreach is both scalable and profitably managed.</p><p>Technical Infrastructure: We build and maintain the proprietary systems and models that drive our German operations. This includes optimizing the "User Experience" (UX) to ensure a frictionless onboarding process for small businesses.</p><p>Operational Excellence: We connect the dots between data-driven decision-making and real-world commercial impact. Our mission is to ensure every potential customer receives a clear, relevant, and rapid understanding of how iwoca can fund their business.</p><p>We are a fast-moving, cross-functional unit designed to turn strategic hypotheses into measurable results. Whether it’s refining a marketing model or shipping a new feature in the application journey, we ensure that iwoca’s expansion in the German market is backed by robust tech and a clear commercial North Star.</p><h2>The role</h2><p>This role sits at the intersection of commercial strategy, data, and technology. Reporting into the Head of Direct Acquisition, you will lead a high-performing, interdisciplinary team of three and own acquisition and activation outcomes for the German market. Your primary objective is to co-define the growth strategy and partner closely with engineering and data teams to build the systems, onboarding journeys, and experiments that bring that strategy to life.</p><p>The scope of this role is broad and we're not looking for someone with deep expertise in every domain the team covers – spanning strategy, analytics, product development, and data science – but rather someone intellectually curious, and skilled at asking the right questions.</p><p>You'll define hypotheses, lead cross-functional initiatives, and own the roadmap for how iwoca engages with German businesses. You will be accountable for measurable impact on acquisition and conversion, bringing ideas to life through rigorous commercial insight, strong customer empathy, and practical delivery. As a Lead, you will also be responsible for coaching your team and establishing the operating rhythm for this new unit.</p><h3>Market and problem understanding</h3><ul><li>Deeply understand the German SME lending landscape, customer needs, and competitive context to sharpen our go-to-market strategy.</li><li>Translate market and customer insight into clearly defined product problems and prioritised commercial opportunities.</li><li>Inform targeting and segmentation strategies to help Marketing and Sales reach the right customers.</li></ul><h3>Product build and optimisation</h3><ul><li>Own the roadmap for acquisition and onboarding, working with engineers and data scientists to develop tools such as lead scoring systems, eligibility checkers, and onboarding journeys.</li><li>Work with marketing and sales to evolve website content, sign-up flows, and decisioning logic to increase conversion.</li><li>Influence future team capability by helping define priorities, roles, and processes as we scale.</li></ul><h3>Experimentation and insight</h3><ul><li>Design, run, and interpret A/B tests across messaging, targeting, onboarding tools, and product flows.</li><li>Identify opportunities using first-principle reasoning supported by data, customer research, and funnel analysis.</li></ul><h3>Cross-functional collaboration</h3><ul><li>Manage, coach, and develop a team of at the beginning two commercial strategy analysts and a data scientist focused on acquisition strategy and operational excellence.</li><li>Lead cross-functional initiatives, aligning engineering, data, marketing, and commercial stakeholders around clear goals, hypotheses, and success metrics.</li><li>Translate high-level business goals into testable hypotheses and actionable briefs for our technical teams.</li><li>Help establish the operating rhythm, rituals, and roadmap processes for this new team.</li></ul><h2>The requirements</h2><p>Essential:</p><ul><li>Strong commercial mindset with proven experience driving go-to-market strategy and measurable acquisition growth.</li><li>Experience in growth strategy, revenue operations, or a highly analytical commercial role with a track record of driving tech-enabled or product-led growth.</li><li>Proven people management or team leadership experience, with the ability to build culture and establish operating rhythms in a newly formed team.</li><li>Fluency in German and strong written communication skills tailored to customer-facing environments.</li><li>Strong analytical capability and experience with experimentation frameworks and A/B testing tools.</li><li>Experience working with (or a strong desire to learn about) technical models such as lead scoring, predictive targeting, or qualification logic.</li><li>Ability to work from first principles and thrive in ambiguity with curiosity and autonomy.</li></ul><p>Bonus:</p><ul><li>Experience in fintech, lending, B2B SaaS, or regulated products.</li><li>Experience working closely with engineering, product, or data science teams to ship features or models.</li><li>Knowledge of the German SME ecosystem or B2B financial products.</li></ul><h2>The culture</h2><p>At iwoca, the best idea wins. We model our culture on independent thinking, challenging untested logic, and evidence-based decisions. We prioritise learning and growth, and give people the autonomy to develop in the direction that makes them most effective.</p><p>We're a tech company and believe in the power of AI to help us work faster and better. We provide the infrastructure where every iwocan always has access to the best models and where those models have access to all of our data. We will help our people to learn how to use and grow with the new tools available to them.</p><h2>The offices</h2><p>We put a lot of effort into making iwoca a great place to work:</p><ul><li>Offices in London, Leeds, Berlin, and Frankfurt with plenty of drinks and snacks.</li><li>Events and community-led groups, including running groups, padel, and monthly ping-pong and pool competitions.</li></ul><h2>The benefits</h2><p>A smart, motivated and international team (we represent over 35 different nationalities) with ridiculous growth-mindset.</p><p>26 days of vacation a year plus a free day for your birthday.</p><p>One-month fully paid sabbatical after 4 years.</p><p>Mental health support with direct access to certified psychologists via our partner OpenUp.</p><p>iwoca takes over a ski chalet in winter so that you and your team can ski or snowboard (and work) for a week. During summer we are drawn to the sun. We’ve been to France, Italy, Spain, and further afield.</p><p>Access to the gym membership program, €25 for either Fit711 or Urban Sports Club.</p><p>€30 contribution towards the Deutschlandticket.</p><p>Company Pension with Canada Life.</p><p>Great office locations. In Frankfurt in the middle of the city, our Berlin office is located in Prenzlauer Berg.</p><p>A paid volunteer day that gives you the opportunity to invest time to support a charity of your choice.</p><p>Corporate Benefits discounts.</p><p>’iwocans’ also benefit from fully stocked fridges in our offices with whatever is needed to strengthen them. There are snacks (both healthy and less healthy) for the whole day.</p><p>And to make sure we all keep learning, we offer:</p><ul><li>A learning and development budget for everyone, including a book budget.</li><li>Learning German budget.</li><li>Company-wide talks with internal and external speakers.</li><li>Access to learning platforms like Treehouse.</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/iwoca-deutschland/strategy-lead-acquisition-berlin-72070","tags":["Business Development"],"job_types":["Permanent employment (unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag)","manager"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1792474237},{"slug":"senior-partner-acquisition-manager-frankfurt-am-main-376547","company_name":"iwoca Deutschland","title":"Senior Partner Acquisition Manager (m/f/d)","description":"<h2>We're looking for a Senior Partner Acquisition Manager (m/f/d)</h2><p>You'll own iwoca's most strategic partnerships in Germany, from the first conversation with a bank, payment provider or business software platform to a live integration that funds small businesses. Your mission is to bring fast, flexible finance to the places where SMEs already run their business.</p><h3>The company</h3><p>Small businesses move fast. Opportunities often don’t wait, and cash flow pressures can appear overnight. To keep going, and growing, SMEs need finance that’s as flexible and responsive as they are.</p><p>That's why we built iwoca. Our smart technology, data science and five-star customer service ensures business owners can act with the speed, confidence and control they need, exactly when it's needed.</p><p>We’ve already cleared the way for 100,000 businesses with more than £4.5 billion in funding. Our passionate team is driven to help even more SMEs succeed, through access to better finance and other services that make running a business easier. Our ultimate mission is to support one million SMEs in their defining moments, creating lasting impact for the communities and economies they drive.</p><h3>The team</h3><p>The Partner Acquisition Germany team builds the partner channel through which iwoca reaches small businesses in Germany: comparison platforms and brokers, banks, payment providers, business software providers and financial advisors who offer iwoca's finance to their customers at the moment it is needed. The team works with three partnership models, from a co-branded referral link and a partner portal to a full API integration, and measures its success by partners that are live and funding customers.</p><p>The team is small and works closely together: the Head of Partner Acquisition Germany, a Strategy & Data Manager who owns market analysis, business cases and the CRM, and the partner managers who own the relationships. The team prioritises partners by strategic fit, works through warm introductions and existing networks wherever possible, and stays close to every new partner until the first customers are funded. It works hand in hand with Relationship Management and the product and engineering teams in London / Berlin / Frankfurt that build the integrations.</p><h3>The role</h3><p>This is a senior role with full ownership of the partners you pursue. Three things matter more than anything else: You will qualify before you sell, because the best partnerships begin with a genuine customer need. You know how to activate networks and create warm introductions rather than relying solely on cold outreach. And you consider a deal complete only when the partnership is live, working well and funding its first customers. You'll travel across Germany one to two days a week for face-to-face partner meetings, industry events and trade fairs.</p><h3>Ownership and impact</h3><ul><li><p>Own a portfolio of the highest-value partnership prospects in Germany, from first conversation to signed contract and live integration.</p></li><li><p>Lead negotiations with founders, managing directors and heads of product or partnerships at banks, payment providers, business software platforms and financial intermediaries.</p></li><li><p>Design the cooperation model and commercial terms for each partner so that the partnership works for both sides over years, not quarters.</p></li><li><p>Bring every partner to go-live with a committed internal promoter and a first concrete use case, so that your work turns into funded customers and long-term value.</p></li></ul><h3>Autonomy, backed by a dedicated strategy and data function</h3><ul><li><p>Spend your time on relationships and deals, with a Strategy & Data Manager who builds target models, business cases and CRM automation alongside you for your prospects and partners.</p></li><li><p>Own your pipeline end to end and keep it transparent, so that forecasts and decisions rest on input and numbers everyone trusts.</p></li><li><p>Decide together with the Head of Partner Acquisition which segments and partners you pursue and where you say no.</p></li></ul><h3>Influence on product and strategy</h3><ul><li><p>Feed what you learn from partners directly into our partnership models, the integration roadmap and the go-to-market plan for Germany.</p></li><li><p>Shape the activation playbook for new partners and the handover to Key Account Management together with the Head of Business Development.</p></li><li><p>Represent iwoca at the industry events, trade fairs and partner roundtables that matter for SME finance in Germany.</p></li></ul><h3>The requirements</h3><p><strong>Essential:</strong></p><ul><li><p>At least five years of experience in B2B partnerships, business development or key account management in fintech, banking, payments or business software. You can show a proven track record of closing complex deals with six to twelve month sales cycles at C-Level, founder, board or head-of-department level.</p></li><li><p>A working understanding of how a financing product is integrated into a partner's platform: APIs, embedded finance and how a partner's customer data can be used in the application journey. You won't build integrations yourself (our engineering teams do that), but you need to lead that conversation credibly.</p></li><li><p>Professional fluency in German and English.</p></li><li><p>Demonstrates curiosity to use and learn more about AI tools. You’ll already be comfortable using AI tools in practical ways to help solve problems, increase productivity and improve quality of work, showing good judgement about when to use them and the ability to explain the reasoning behind that use.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Bonus:</strong></p><ul><li><p>An existing network among German banks, payment providers, brokers or business software platforms.</p></li><li><p>Experience with lending, working capital or other financial products for small businesses.</p></li><li><p>Experience managing a partner pipeline in HubSpot and using data to prioritise targets.</p></li></ul><p>Don’t take this list as prescriptive: it’s just to give you a sense of who might do well at the job. We’d still love to hear from you if you don’t hit every point on the list, or if you have other experience.</p><h3>The salary</h3><p>We expect to pay from €70,000 - €85,000 base salary plus a performance-related bonus for this role. But, we’re open-minded, so definitely include your salary goals with your application. We routinely benchmark salaries against market rates, and run quarterly performance and salary reviews.</p><h3>The culture</h3><p>At iwoca, the best idea wins. We model our culture on independent thinking, challenging untested logic, and evidence-based decisions. We prioritise learning and growth, and give people the autonomy to develop in the direction that makes them most effective.</p><p>We're a tech company and believe in the power of AI to help us work faster and better. We provide the infrastructure where every iwocan always has access to the best models and where those models have access to all of our data. We will help our people to learn how to use and grow with the new tools available to them.</p><h3>The offices</h3><p>We put a lot of effort into making iwoca a great place to work:</p><ul><li><p>Offices in London, Leeds, Berlin, and Frankfurt with plenty of drinks and snacks.</p></li><li><p>Events and community-led groups, including running groups, padel, and monthly ping-pong and pool competitions.</p></li></ul><h3>The benefits</h3><ul><li><p>A smart, motivated and international team (we represent over 35 different nationalities) with a ridiculous growth-mindset.</p></li><li><p>26 days of vacation a year plus a free day for your birthday.</p></li><li><p>One-month fully paid sabbatical after 4 years.</p></li><li><p>Mental health support with direct access to certified psychologists via our partner OpenUp.</p></li><li><p>iwoca takes over a ski chalet in winter so that you and your team can ski o