ung: Du baust den Entsorgungsfachbetrieb PFASuiki von Grund auf mit auf und bist die zentrale Ansprechperson für alle Entsorgungsfragen</p></li><li><p>Breites Aufgabenfeld: Abfallrecht, Zertifizierung, Behördenarbeit, Einsätze bei Kunden und die Markteinführung einer neuen Zerstörungstechnologie</p></li><li><p>Startup-Kultur: Ein dynamisches, kollegiales Umfeld, in dem deine Ideen unsere Technologie und Strategie direkt prägen</p></li><li><p>Weiterbildung: Fachkunde- und Fortbildungslehrgänge sind bei uns fest eingeplant</p></li><li><p>Attraktives Paket: Fixgehalt plus leistungsabhängige variable Vergütung</p></li><li><p>Weitere Benefits wie Zuschüsse zu ÖPNV und Mittagessen</p></li></ul><p></p><p>Bereit, mit deinem Entsorgungs-Know-how dafür zu sorgen, dass „Ewigkeitschemikalien“ der Vergangenheit angehören?</p><p>Werde Teil von PFASuiki und schaffe die regulatorische Grundlage, mit der unsere Technologie vom Pilotbetrieb in den kommerziellen Einsatz geht.</p><p>Wenn du fundiertes Abfallrecht mit einer praktischen, lösungsorientierten Arbeitsweise verbindest und gern Verantwortung übernimmst, freuen wir uns auf deine Bewerbung.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/pfasuiki-gmbh/environmental-compliance-manager-pfas-kreislaufwirtschaft-oberhaching-377347","tags":["Power Engineering and Environmental Engineering"],"job_types":["Unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag","berufserfahren"],"location":"Oberhaching","created_at":1792474236},{"slug":"technical-product-manager-ai-finance-app-london-216078","company_name":"Bjak","title":"Technical Product Manager - AI Finance App","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About KIRA</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our mission is to make money smart, reliable and within reach for everyone.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">In 2019, we built the first mobile-first, insurance platform, enabling insurance to be accessible online by millions in the region. Today, it's the leading insurance platform in Southeast Asia.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, we are expanding ways to help people in Asia and it includes spending, saving, investing, exchanging, travelling, and more. Our objective is to build tools that will help people get more from their money and at ease and self reliance, become an expert. We believe AI will help us achieve this in our generation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for the most talented and driven people we can find. We are looking for people who work for their passion, not counting hours. Who loves building great next-generation products, not status quo. Who cares about redefining how everyone around us can get the best financial applications, not for an exclusive few.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We have teams working around the world, with over 20 nationalities and growing from our offices and remotely. Join us and build a better future.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you're this person, we'd love to talk to you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">KIRA is building a AI Finance Superapp for Southeast Asia across payments, remittance, insurance, wealth, and trading.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">These products move real money. Reliability, regulatory requirements, and third-party financial rails are fundamental to the product - not considerations around the edges.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Technical Product Manager owns a product vertical <strong>end-to-end</strong>, from strategy and outcomes through technical design, delivery, and launch.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are AI-native by default, but AI is a means, not the goal. The bar is knowing where AI genuinely improves an outcome, where deterministic systems must remain in control, and how to build products that are reliable, auditable, and trusted.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>What You'll Own</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Owning a product vertical end-to-end, including strategy, metrics, roadmap, priorities and delivery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shaping technical design with engineering across APIs, data flows, ledgering, reconciliation, failure handling, security and scalability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Driving trade-offs across correctness, speed, cost, reliability, regulatory requirements and user experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Building regulatory requirements into the product across KYC, transaction monitoring, limits, privacy and licensing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Applying AI where it improves outcomes, with clear evaluation, safeguards, human oversight and failure handling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shipping products around external dependencies, including regulatory approvals, financial rails and third-party partners.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Aligning Engineering, Design, Compliance, Operations, Treasury and Finance around clear product decisions and launch requirements.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div></li></ul><h2><strong>What We're Looking For</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years of product management experience, including ownership of complex technical products from strategy through production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong technical foundation across system architecture, APIs, databases, workflows, failure modes and distributed systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working closely with engineers and ability to review, challenge and contribute to technical designs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in payments, banking, remittance, insurance, trading or another regulated, high-consequence product domain.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong product judgment and ability to make difficult trade-offs under technical, regulatory and operational constraints.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building with LLMs or AI products, including evaluation, reliability and understanding when AI should not be used.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div></li></ul><h2><strong>Nice to have</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Engineering or highly technical product background.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building zero-to-one fintech or consumer products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience defining evaluation frameworks for ML or LLM-powered products.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div></li></ul><h2><strong>Outcome</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear vertical strategy and legible roadmap</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ships fast and clears the gates that actually block launch</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Money is correct and users are never misled about the state of their funds</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI features are valuable, predictable and trusted</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Trade-offs made deliberately under uncertainty and hold up when challenged</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Engineering, design, compliance, and operations are aligned with minimal friction</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>Location</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a <strong>hybrid role</strong>. You are expected to work from our local office at least <strong>3 days per week</strong>, with the remaining days offering flexibility to work remotely.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Candidates should be based in, or able to work from, the location where the role is advertised..</p><h2></h2><h2>Language</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">English is our main working language across global teams. Strong English communication is required.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Interview Process</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our process is designed to move fast:</p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Online assessment or practical task</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical interview</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">CEO / final round</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em">For strong candidates, we aim to complete the process and make an offer within <strong>1 week</strong> from the start of the interview process. Candidates who complete assessments quickly will be prioritized.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/bjak/technical-product-manager-ai-finance-app-london-216078","tags":["Product"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"United Kingdom","created_at":1792474822},{"slug":"growth-associate-ma-platform-london-173222","company_name":"iwoca","title":"Growth Associate - M&A Platform","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re joining manda, iwoca’s M&amp;A platform, at a pivotal moment. After early success working with existing iwoca customers, we’re now turning to the open market to help more business owners exit.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">That’s why we’re looking for a Growth Associate to join the team. This is a 6-month fixed-term role for someone smart, hungry and entrepreneurial. With the right traction the role will convert into a permanent role at the forefront of manda’s growth efforts.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The company</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Selling a small business is hard. Only <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.iwoca.co.uk/news/iwoca-launches-m-a-marketplace"><u>one in five UK SME owners</u></a> has a formal exit plan, yet half are counting on their business to fund their retirement. Below £10m in enterprise value, most M&amp;A advisers can't make the economics work, so a generation of owner-managers is getting ready to step back with no realistic route to a sale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">manda exists to fix that. We match owners with serious buyers, from search funds to private equity, and handle the whole process in one place, including financial due diligence and acquisition finance. Our first sale is done, and we're now opening manda up beyond iwoca's own customers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">manda is part of iwoca, one of Europe's leading fintech lenders, which has provided more than £4 billion in funding to over 150,000 businesses since 2012. That gives us what a traditional adviser doesn't have: a deep footprint in the SME economy, a lender's data and infrastructure, and deals run on clean, automated processes rather than spreadsheets.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The team</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll report to manda's Venture Lead and work day to day with our Transaction Managers, the dealmakers who run each sale, and our Partnerships Manager, who builds our referral network with accountants, solicitors and wealth managers. You'll also work with iwoca's marketing &amp; sales team and have access to their tools and know-how.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your mission is to grow the number of businesses manda takes to market, by finding owners who are serious about selling and bringing them into a first meeting with one of our Transaction Managers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With an ethos of smarter, not louder, you’ll build on iwoca’s existing models to work out which owners are getting ready to sell and which businesses will attract a buyer, then reach them personally by email, LinkedIn and phone. We'd rather approach the right few hundred owners well than the wrong ten thousand badly.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Decide who we contact.</strong> Own the target lists and the logic behind them, and keep sharpening them on what actually predicts a seller and a strong business.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Convert interest.</strong> Write and send the outreach yourself, follow up with owners who respond, and book them in with a Transaction Manager.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Find what works.</strong> Run several experiments at once, back what produces meetings and drop what doesn't. Letters, events and ideas of your own can all earn a place.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Make manda credible.</strong> Owners look us up before they reply. Help make sure what they find, from our website to LinkedIn, gives them a reason to get in touch.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Who you are</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You don't need to be a marketer or have years of experience. You need to be smart, resourceful and quick to learn from what isn't working, and to want ownership of something real.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You're entrepreneurial.</strong> You've started, sold or built something, even if it was small, and you don't wait for a plan before getting going.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You write well.</strong> Your messages are short, clear and human, the kind a busy owner actually answers, and you're just as at ease on the phone with someone who has spent thirty years building their business.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You follow through.</strong> A reply that never becomes a meeting is a lead lost.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You're honest about results.</strong> You'd rather report a bad week than dress it up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You're AI-savvy.</strong> You use AI to research, personalise and write at a scale one person couldn't otherwise reach, and you automate whatever you find yourself doing twice.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The requirements</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Essential:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Some experience in outreach, sales or growth, whether in an SDR or BDR role, marketing, a startup or a project of your own. Evidence of initiative matters more than a polished CV.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Numerate and analytical. Working out who to contact is as much of this job as contacting them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable with rejection. Most owners won't reply, and plenty who do won't be ready yet.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A genuine interest in SMEs, M&amp;A or how businesses change hands.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Based in London and available full-time.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bonus:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on with outbound tools such as HubSpot or LinkedIn Sales Navigator.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've worked to a meetings or pipeline target, and hit it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building a targeting or lead-scoring model.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>The salary &amp; contract</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is initially a 6-month fixed-term contract, with a salary of £30,000–£40,000 per annum (pro rata), depending on experience.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">While we're starting with a fixed-term contract, our intention is for this to develop into a permanent position. At the end of the six months, we'll review how things have gone, with the opportunity to make the role permanent, expand its responsibilities and revisit the salary to reflect the longer-term scope.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Please include your salary expectations with your application.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The culture</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At iwoca, we prioritise a culture of learning, growth, and support, and invest in the development of our team members. We value thought and skill diversity, and encourage people to explore new areas of interest, adopt better tools – including AI – and apply sound judgement so our products and decisions improve over time.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The offices</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We put a lot of effort into making iwoca a great place to work:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Offices in London, Leeds, Berlin, and Frankfurt with plenty of drinks and snacks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Events and community-led groups, including running groups, padel, and monthly ping-pong and pool competitions.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The benefits</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible working hours.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Medical insurance from Vitality, including discounted gym membership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A choice between a dedicated dental plan or a health cash plan that reimburses everyday medical expenses.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A private GP service (separate from Vitality) for you, your partner, and your dependents.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">25 days’ holiday per year, an extra day off for your birthday, the option to buy or sell an additional five days of annual leave, and unlimited unpaid leave.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A one-month, fully paid sabbatical after four years.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Instant access to external counselling and therapy sessions for team members that need emotional or mental health support.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3% Pension contributions on total earnings.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An employee equity incentive scheme.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Generous parental leave and a nursery tax benefit scheme to help you save money.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Electric car scheme and cycle to work scheme.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Two company retreats a year: we’ve been to France, Italy, Spain, and further afield.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">And to make sure we all keep learning, we offer:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A learning and development budget for everyone.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Company-wide talks with internal and external speakers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to learning platforms like Treehouse.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Useful links:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://coda.io/@iwocauk/iwoca-benefits-policies-uk"><u>iwoca benefits &amp; policies</u></a></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://coda.io/@iwocauk/interview-welcome-pack-tap"><u>Interview welcome pack</u></a></p></li></ul><hr><p>Compensation: £30K – £40K</p><ul><li> • £30K – £40K</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/iwoca/growth-associate-ma-platform-london-173222","tags":["Strategy and Product"],"job_type