rting and executing Delinea's communications strategy across EMEA and APAC, reporting directly to the Corporate Communications Director. Based in London or surrounding areas, you will help drive initiatives that strengthen the company's brand awareness, amplify its thought leadership in the cybersecurity space, and engage internal and external audiences across the region. This role involves hands-on execution across media relations, executive communications, content creation, internal communications, and social media. The ideal candidate is a proactive, detail-oriented communicator with experience in technology or cybersecurity and a strong ability to translate complex topics into clear, engaging narratives.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">External communications &amp; media relations</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the execution of public relations campaigns across EMEA and APAC to elevate Delinea's brand visibility and reputation in the cybersecurity industry.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Draft, edit, and coordinate press releases, media pitches, and briefing documents for company announcements, product launches, partnerships, and other milestones.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help maintain relationships with journalists, analysts, and media outlets, ensuring timely responses to inquiries and consistent engagement with key stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track media coverage and develop regular reporting dashboards to assess performance and sentiment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage the day-to-day of our regional agency partners (PR, content, etc.) across the UK, France, Germany, Middle East, India, Singapore, and Australia.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner regularly with regional marketing leads to align PR priorities with local business objectives.</p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Executive &amp; thought leadership support</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with the Director to build and maintain executive platforms, including drafting thought leadership content (blogs, op-eds, bylines, speeches, social media posts) and supporting event participation (webinars, panels, keynotes).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Research industry trends and competitor communications to identify white space opportunities for Delinea's executives to stand out.</p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Internal communications</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support internal messaging initiatives, including All Hands meetings, employee newsletters, and intranet updates to ensure alignment with company priorities and culture.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with HR, IT, and other departments to create clear, engaging internal content that enhances employee engagement and awareness.</p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Content creation &amp; management</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Draft and edit a range of communications materials, including Q&amp;As, FAQs, and messaging frameworks aligned with brand voice and tone.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the development of high-impact cybersecurity thought leadership assets such as whitepapers, customer stories, and strategic reports</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage content calendars and coordinate with marketing and product teams to ensure timely execution.</p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Crisis communications</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assist the Director in preparing and executing response plans during critical situations, including developing holding statements, FAQs, and internal and external messaging.</