&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For Australia &amp;amp; Singapore&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Your personal data will be retained by Baringa for up to two years, in accordance with our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.baringa.com/globalassets/careers/dp-007-nerpn-amer--apac-recruitment-privacy-notice-word.pdf&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice (AMER &amp;amp; APAC)&lt;/a&gt;, to assess your application and meet applicable reporting and legal obligations. In line with the Australian Privacy Act and Singapore’s Personal Data Protection Act (PDPA), you may have rights to access, correct, or request limited deletion of your personal data. For more information, please contact us at &lt;a ----------<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/baringa/banking-markets-consultant-senior-consultant-london-457843","tags":["Banking and Markets"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1792464925},{"slug":"staff-mechanical-product-engineer-production-sydney-australia-28370","company_name":"Andurilindustries","title":"Staff Mechanical Product Engineer (Production)","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Staff Product Engineer serves as the primary design engineering presence on the production floor, bridging the gap between design intent and production execution. Embedded within the Global Head of Production organization with a dotted-line relationship to Platform and Payload Engineering Teams, this role owns the day-to-day engineering interface between design engineering teams and manufacturing operations across multiple production sites.&lt;br&gt;This is a senior individual contributor role requiring deep technical judgement, the ability to operate autonomously in a fast-paced production environment, and the credibility to influence both design engineers and production leadership. The Staff Product Engineer is expected to drive systemic improvements — not just resolve individual issues — and to develop process and tooling solutions that scale across product versions, variations, and manufacturing sites.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Production Floor Engineering Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary design engineering point of contact on the production floor for assigned programs and product lines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Triage and disposition Material Review Board (MRB) actions day-to-day; participate in MRB meetings and drive resolution timelines to minimize production hold time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resolve production process-blockers, design ambiguities, and drawing interpretation issues in real time, exercising engineering judgement within defined authority boundaries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide rapid-response engineering support to Production, Quality, and Test teams for nonconformance resolution, use-as-is/rework/scrap decisions, and repair dispositions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and escalate systemic design issues to core Design Engineering teams with clear problem statements, data, and recommended corrective actions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform and review mechanical design analyses — including structural stress, fatigue life, thermal, and tolerance stackup calculations — to support MRB dispositions, deviation requests, and use-as-is justifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilize 3D CAD tools (e.g., SolidWorks, NX, or CATIA) to evaluate proposed rework paths, model design modifications, and generate or revise engineering drawings as needed to support production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply knowledge of materials and manufacturing processes — including metals, composites, adhesive bonding, welding, brazing, and surface treatments — to assess nonconformances and recommend technically sound repair or rework methods&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design Intent Translation &amp;amp; Multi-Site Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bridge the translation of design intent into production-executable work across multiple product versions, configurations, and manufacturing sites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain Standard Repair Manuals and engineering disposition guides that give Production autonomy to resolve high-frequency, low-complexity MRB items without engineering hold&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the stand-up and ramp of production at new or expanding manufacturing sites, ensuring design engineering knowledge transfers effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Manufacturing Engineering on work instruction development, tooling validation, and First Article Inspection (FAI) activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flow production observations, failure mode data, and process improvement opportunities back to Design Engineering through structured feedback mechanisms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage mechanical modeling and simulation capabilities to rapidly evaluate design change proposals, ensuring form-fit-function integrity before releasing changes to the production floor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply materials engineering knowledge to assess the suitability of alternate materials or processes during supply chain disruptions, ensuring equivalent mechanical performance and environmental compatibility for maritime applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process &amp;amp; Tooling Improvement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and drive process/tool-based solutions to reduce manual translation of engineering intent into production across product variants and sites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and improve key tool and functional interfaces (PLM workflows, digital work instructions, BOM reconciliation) that impact design-to-production efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop scalable frameworks for multi-site production: configuration management alignment, site-specific work instruction adaptation, and cross-site lesson-learned sharing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build repeatable playbooks for standing up production of new product variants, reducing ramp time and first-unit defects at each additional site&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration &amp;amp; Metrics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain strong working relationships with Quality, Supply Chain, Manufacturing Engineering, and Program Management to ensure aligned priorities and rapid issue resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and report key metrics: MRB disposition cycle time, repeat-discrepancy rate, first-pass yield trends, and engineering response SLA adherence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collate and drive corrective actions on design-originated production issues, providing data-backed prioritization to core Design Engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in Production readiness reviews, design reviews (DFM/DFA/DFT), and engineering change assessments as the production voice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Competencies &amp;amp; Attributes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering Judgement:&lt;/strong&gt; Technical depth combined with production pragmatism — able to make sound engineering decisions under time pressure without over-engineering solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Influence:&lt;/strong&gt; Credibility with both design engineers and production operators; able to speak both languages and bridge communication gaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mechanical Design Acumen: &lt;/strong&gt;Broad mechanical engineering foundation spanning 3D CAD modeling, structural and thermal analysis, materials selection, and manufacturing process knowledge — able to apply design engineering skills directly to solve production problems rather than relying solely on escalation to design teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Autonomy &amp;amp; Initiative:&lt;/strong&gt; Comfort with ambiguity and competing priorities in a fast-moving production environment; able to self-direct and prioritize without constant direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems Thinking:&lt;/strong&gt; Thinks beyond individual issue resolution to identify patterns, root causes, and scalable solutions that prevent recurrence across sites and variants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Clear, concise technical communication — written dispositions, engineering reports, and presentations to leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Mechanical Engineering, Aerospace Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering, or a related engineering discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of engineering experience in a manufacturing or production environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience working on or directly supporting a production floor in a hands-on engineering capacity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of MRB processes, nonconformance management, and engineering disposition (use-as-is, rework, scrap, return to vendor)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AS9100 / ISO 9001 quality management systems and associated production quality processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with GD&amp;amp;T, engineering drawings, specifications, and the ability to interpret design intent for production personnel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting multi-site manufacturing operations or production transfers between facilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of configuration management, engineering change order (ECO) processes, and product lifecycle management (PLM) tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to obtain an Austrailian Security Clearance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience should span mechanical design engineering and production/manufacturing engineering roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4 years in aerospace and/or defense&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with NX, FEMAP and Teamcenter or similar CAD, FEA and PLM systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with the design, analysis, testing, implementation and support of mechanical parts and assemblies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with welding, machining, sheet metal, injection molding, composites and/or additive manufacturing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with drawings, GD&amp;amp;T (AS1100, ASME Y14.5), tolerance stack-up analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the maritime domain (sealing, pressure vessels, corrosion and material compatibility, pressure testing).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience as a Liaison Engineer, Sustaining Engineer, Product Engineer, or Production Support Engineer in an aerospace or defense environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing Standard Repair Manuals, engineering disposition guides, or similar production-autonomy documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Lean Manufacturing, Six Sigma, or similar continuous improvement methodologies applied in a production setting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of driving process improvements that resulted in measurable cycle time reduction or yield improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with digital work instruction platforms, MES systems, or PLM-to-shop-floor integration tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The salary range for this role is an estimate based on a wide range of compensation factors, inclusive of base salary only. Actual salary offer may vary based on (but not limited to) work experience, education and/or training, critical skills, and/or business considerations. Highly competitive equity grants are included in the majority of full time offers; and are considered part of Anduril&#39;s total compensation package. Additionally, Anduril offers top-tier benefits for full-time employees, including:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;At Anduril, we invest in our people. Our comprehensive, competitive benefits package (available at little to no cost to employees) ensures you’re supported in health, recovery, and whatever comes next.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;For more information, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.anduril.com/careers&quot;&gt;Explore Our Benefits&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;RichText column1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Protecting Yourself from Recruitment Scams&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;Anduril is committed to maintaining the integrity of our Talent acquisition process and the security of our candidates. We&#39;ve observed a rise in sophisticated phishing and fraudulent schemes where individuals impersonate Anduril representatives, luring job seekers with false interviews or job offers. These scammers often attempt to extract payment or sensitive personal information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;RichText column2&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;To ensure your safety and help you navigate your job search with confidence, please keep the following critical points in mind:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No Financial Requests:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Anduril will never solicit payment or demand personal financial details (such as banking information, credit card numbers, or social security numbers) at any stage of our hiring process. Our legitimate recruitment is entirely free for candidates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please always verify communications:&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct from Anduril: If you receive an email from one of our recruiters, it will &lt;em&gt;only&lt;/em&gt; come from an ----- address.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Via Agency Partner: If contacted by a recruiting agency for an Anduril role, their email will clearly identify their agency. If you suspect any suspicious activity, please verify the agency&#39;s authenticity by reaching out to &lt;a ----------
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exercise Caution with Unsolicited Outreach:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;If you receive any communication that appears suspicious, contains grammatical errors, or makes unusual requests, do not engage. Always confirm the sender&#39;s email domain is ----- before providing any personal information or clicking on links.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What to Do If You Suspect Fraud:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Should you encounter any questionable or fraudulent outreach claiming to be from Anduril, please report it immediately to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a ---------- Your proactive caution is invaluable in protecting your personal information and upholding the security and trustworthiness of our recruitment efforts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Privacy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;To view Anduril&#39;s candidate data privacy policy, please visit &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/&quot;&gt;https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;By submitting your application, you consent to Anduril Industries using a third-party service provider to conduct pre-employment risk, integrity, and due diligence screening and assessing potential risks as part of your application process. This third-party service provider provides risk-intelligence services that may include analysis of sanctions and watchlists, adverse media, public-record information, and other lawful open-source or commercial data sources. This third-party service provider does not act as a consumer reporting agency. Use of this provider helps to ensure compliance with applicable laws and protect technology, intellectual property, and organizational security.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/andurilindustries/staff-mechanical-product-engineer-production-sydney-australia-28370","tags":["Maritime & Maneuver Dominance : Undersea Dominance - Engineering & Operations : Systems Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"Sydney, Australia","created_at":1792464924},{"slug":"staff-mechanical-product-engineer-platform-sydney-australia-180860","company_name":"Andurilindustries","title":"Staff Mechanical Product Engineer (Platform)","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Staff Product Engineer serves as the primary design engineering presence on the production floor, bridging the gap between design intent and production execution. The role sits within Platform Engineering organisation and dispositions nonconformances and Material Review Board (MRB) actions, resolves design questions in real time, and closes the loop between production and design so that issues get root caused and fixed at the source. This is a senior individual contributor role requiring deep technical judgement, the ability to operate autonomously in a fast-paced production environment, and the credibility to influence both design engineers and production teams. You will be expected to drive systemic improvements, cutting repeat nonconformances through changes to the design and documentation, as well as resolving individual issues.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Production Floor Engineering Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary design engineering point of contact on the production floor for assigned programs and product lines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the design authority at Material Review Board (MRB), working with Quality and Manufacturing to minimise production hold time without compromising product safety and integrity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resolve production process-blockers, design ambiguities, and drawing interpretation issues in real time, exercising engineering judgement within defined authority boundaries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide rapid-response engineering support and Root Cause Analysis (RCA) to Production, Quality, and Test teams for part and sub-assembly nonconformance resolution, use-as-is/rework/scrap decisions, and repair dispositions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and escalate systemic design issues to core Design Engineering teams with clear problem statements, data, and recommended corrective actions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design Intent Translation &amp;amp; Multi-Site Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the translation of design intent into production-executable work across multiple product versions, configurations, and manufacturing sites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the stand-up and ramp of production at new or expanding manufacturing sites, ensuring design engineering knowledge transfers effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise and implement engineering changes to correct production issues that originate in the design, through the Anduril configuration management and change process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feed production observations, failure modes and DFM/DFA opportunities back into Platform Mechanical design work through structured feedback, prioritised using data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design to Production Interface&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Manufacturing Engineering on work instruction (WI) development, tooling validation, and First Article Inspection (FAI) activities, communicating the design intent and acceptance criteria&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the resolution of EBOM discrepancies found in production, and give engineering input to Configuration Management and Manufacturing Engineering on PLM workflows, BOM reconciliation and work instruction tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify patterns across nonconformances, test failures and build issues, and lead engineering root cause analysis and design corrective action implementation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate on the improvement of key tool and functional interfaces (PLM workflows, digital work instructions, BOM reconciliation) that impact design-to-production efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the development of scalable frameworks for multi-site production: configuration management alignment, site-specific work instruction adaptation, and cross-site lesson-learned sharing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build repeatable playbooks for standing up production of new product variants, reducing ramp time and first-unit defects at each additional site&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration &amp;amp; Metrics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain strong working relationships with Quality, Supply Chain, Manufacturing Engineering, and Program Management to ensure aligned priorities and rapid issue resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and report key metrics: disposition turnaround, repeat-discrepancy rate on owned hardware, nonconformances closed by design change, and how many nonconformance types are covered by repair and disposition guides&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collate and drive corrective actions on design-originated production issues, providing data-backed prioritisation to core Design Engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in Production readiness reviews, design reviews (P&amp;amp;DFMEA, DFM/A/T) and engineering change assessments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Competencies &amp;amp; Attributes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering Judgement:&lt;/strong&gt; Technical depth combined with production pragmatism — able to make sound engineering decisions under time pressure without over-engineering solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design Authority Integrity:&lt;/strong&gt; You protect product safety and integrity under schedule pressure, understand the limits of your delegated authority and escalate when you should.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Influence:&lt;/strong&gt; Credibility with both design engineers and production operators; able to speak both languages and bridge communication gaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Autonomy &amp;amp; Initiative:&lt;/strong&gt; Comfort with ambiguity and competing priorities in a fast-moving production environment; able to self-direct and prioritise without constant direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems Thinking:&lt;/strong&gt; Thinks beyond individual issue resolution to identify patterns, root causes, and scalable solutions that prevent recurrence across sites and variants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Clear, concise technical communication — written dispositions, engineering reports, and presentations to leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Mechanical Engineering, Aerospace Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering, or a related engineering discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of engineering experience in a manufacturing or production environment, with at least 4 years in defense, aerospace or automotive&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mechanical design and analysis capability to justify use-as-is and repair dispositions (hand calculations, tolerance analysis, FEA)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience working on or directly supporting a production floor in a hands-on engineering capacity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of Material Review Board (MRB) processes, nonconformance management, and engineering disposition (use-as-is, rework, scrap, return to vendor)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ISO 9001 quality management systems and associated production quality processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to interpret engineering GD&amp;amp;T drawings, specifications and to explain design intent to production personnel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting multi-site manufacturing operations or production transfers between facilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of configuration management, engineering change order (ECO) processes, and product lifecycle management (PLM) tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to obtain and maintain an Australian Government security clearance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the defence, maritime, automotive or aerospace industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience as a Product, Sustaining, Liaison or Production Support Engineer with delegated design or disposition authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with NX, FEMAP and Teamcenter, or similar CAD, FEA and PLM systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with the design, analysis, testing, implementation and support of mechanical parts and assemblies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with welding, machining, sheet metal, injection moulding, composites and/or additive manufacturing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with engineering drawings, GD&amp;amp;T (AS 1100, ASME Y14.5) and tolerance stack-up analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the maritime domain (sealing, pressure vessels, corrosion and material compatibility, pressure testing)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering under Australian Defence contracts, including working with Defence quality assurance, acceptance and seaworthiness representatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with First Article Inspection and production readiness reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing engineering disposition guides or similar documentation that lets production resolve issues without engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting multi-site production or production transfers, including international sites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Root Cause Analysis (RCA) and continuous improvement methods (e.g. 8D, 5 Whys, Red X. Lean, Six Sigma)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of reducing repeat nonconformances or disposition cycle time through design or documentation changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The salary range for this role is an estimate based on a wide range of compensation factors, inclusive of base salary only. Actual salary offer may vary based on (but not limited to) work experience, education and/or training, critical skills, and/or business considerations. Highly competitive equity grants are included in the majority of full time offers; and are considered part of Anduril&#39;s total compensation package. Additionally, Anduril offers top-tier benefits for full-time employees, including:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;At Anduril, we invest in our people. Our comprehensive, competitive benefits package (available at little to no cost to employees) ensures you’re supported in health, recovery, and whatever comes next.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;For more information, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.anduril.com/careers&quot;&gt;Explore Our Benefits&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;RichText column1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Protecting Yourself from Recruitment Scams&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;Anduril is committed to maintaining the integrity of our Talent acquisition process and the security of our candidates. We&#39;ve observed a rise in sophisticated phishing and fraudulent schemes where individuals impersonate Anduril representatives, luring job seekers with false interviews or job offers. These scammers often attempt to extract payment or sensitive personal information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;RichText column2&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;To ensure your safety and help you navigate your job search with confidence, please keep the following critical points in mind:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No Financial Requests:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Anduril will never solicit payment or demand personal financial details (such as banking information, credit card numbers, or social security numbers) at any stage of our hiring process. Our legitimate recruitment is entirely free for candidates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please always verify communications:&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct from Anduril: If you receive an email from one of our recruiters, it will &lt;em&gt;only&lt;/em&gt; come from an ----- address.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Via Agency Partner: If contacted by a recruiting agency for an Anduril role, their email will clearly identify their agency. If you suspect any suspicious activity, please verify the agency&#39;s authenticity by reaching out to &lt;a ----------
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exercise Caution with Unsolicited Outreach:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;If you receive any communication that appears suspicious, contains grammatical errors, or makes unusual requests, do not engage. Always confirm the sender&#39;s email domain is ----- before providing any personal information or clicking on links.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What to Do If You Suspect Fraud:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Should you encounter any questionable or fraudulent outreach claiming to be from Anduril, please report it immediately to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a ---------- Your proactive caution is invaluable in protecting your personal information and upholding the security and trustworthiness of our recruitment efforts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Privacy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;To view Anduril&#39;s candidate data privacy policy, please visit &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/&quot;&gt;https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;By submitting your application, you consent to Anduril Industries using a third-party service provider to conduct pre-employment risk, integrity, and due diligence screening and assessing potential risks as part of your application process. This third-party service provider provides risk-intelligence services that may include analysis of sanctions and watchlists, adverse media, public-record information, and other lawful open-source or commercial data sources. This third-party service provider does not act as a consumer reporting agency. Use of this provider helps to ensure compliance with applicable laws and protect technology, intellectual property, and organizational security.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/andurilindustries/staff-mechanical-product-engineer-platform-sydney-australia-180860","tags":["Maritime & Maneuver Dominance : Undersea Dominance - Engineering & Operations : Systems Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"Sydney, Australia","created_at":1792464924},{"slug":"channel-solutions-engineer-london-198065","company_name":"Algolia","title":"Channel Solutions Engineer","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;m_8220454926977230902gmail-docs-internal-guid-9a9f34f4-7fff-014a-c97c-98ca90610a47&quot;&gt;Algolia is the retrieval intelligence layer that turns intent into trusted, decision-grade outcomes. Powering more than 1.7 trillion queries a year for over 18,000 customers with millisecond latency and 99.999% reliability, we are the recognized leader for Search and Product Discovery by top industry analyst firms. The Algolia platform turns a company&#39;s products, content, and business rules into data that humans, applications and AI agents can act upon. The result is trusted customer experiences with stronger conversions for measurable business impact.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;uil-fw-normal uil-ff-hind uil-fsz-16 lg:uil-fsz-18 uil-lh-bigger uil-color-grey-700&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Algolia, we&#39;re passionate about helping organisations create fast, relevant, and intuitive digital experiences. Algolia AI search powers millions of experiences across ecommerce, financial services, travel and hospitality, media, marketplaces, SaaS, and other enterprise applications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Partner Solutions Engineer (EMEA), you&#39;ll play a critical role in expanding the impact of our partner ecosystem. You&#39;ll serve as the primary technical advisor across all of our partner categories including: Systems Integrators (SIs), Independent Software Vendors (ISVs), Cloud Partners, OEM partners, and Resellers across the EMEA region, enabling them to build, sell, and deliver exceptional experiences powered by Algolia.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role combines technical consulting, partner enablement, solution validation, and relationship management. You&#39;ll work closely with Partner Managers, Product, Engineering, Marketing, and the global Partner Solutions Engineering team to help partners become trusted experts on the Algolia platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While reporting into the global Solutions Engineering team, this role is dedicated to our Global Partner Team which covers our partners in EMEA, AMER, LATAM and APAC.&amp;nbsp; This is a chance to join a mature Partner Team which has delivered consistent results and value to the business for the past 5 years.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enable and Empower Partners&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver technical onboarding and enablement programs for SI, ISV, and Cloud partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary technical point of contact for strategic partners throughout their lifecycle with Algolia&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide ongoing technical guidance and best practices to ensure partners successfully implement and innovate using Algolia solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop scalable enablement materials, workshops, demos, and technical documentation for our partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Technical Excellence Across the Partner Ecosystem&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate, validate, and certify partner-built accelerators, integrations, and solutions&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Product and Engineering teams to ensure partner solutions align with platform best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring partner insight to Product and Engineering teams through our Partner Advisory Board or other mechanism&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor the health and quality of partner technical assets and recommend improvements over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Evangelize New Capabilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become an expert on new Algolia features and product releases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate technical capabilities into compelling business value for both technical and executive audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare partners to confidently position, demonstrate, and sell new Algolia capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver engaging technical demonstrations, webinars, workshops, and enablement sessions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support Partner-Led Sales Opportunities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide presales technical expertise for opportunities coming from our partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist partners with architecture discussions, solution design, demonstrations, proof-of-concepts, and technical discovery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales and Partner Managers to help accelerate partner-sourced and partner-influenced revenue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build Strategic Relationships&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop trusted relationships with technical leaders and solution architects at strategic partner organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the voice of partners internally by communicating technical feedback and identifying opportunities for improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with the global Partner Solutions Engineering organisation, particularly the EMEA team, to develop annual technical engagement initiatives and share best practices across regions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Might Be a Great Fit If You Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years experience as a Solutions Engineer, Sales Engineer, Solutions Architect, Partner Engineer, or Technical Consultant.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with Systems Integrators and ISV Partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of APIs, cloud technologies, web architectures, and modern software development practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to explain complex technical concepts in a way that resonates with both technical and non-technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding presentation, storytelling, and technical demonstration skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for educating others and helping technical teams become successful&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organisational skills with the ability to independently manage multiple partner initiatives and deliverables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating across globally distributed teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable balancing strategic relationship management with hands-on technical work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with search, ecommerce, content management, personalization, digital experience technologies or other AI technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;uil-fw-normal uil-ff-hind uil-fsz-16 lg:uil-fsz-18 uil-lh-bigger uil-color-grey-700&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Hybrid&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Algolia does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, military status, veteran status, disability status, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, or any other characteristic protected by law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The annual total cash compensation range (base salary and commission) for this role reflects market pay data within this location. The exact compensation offered for this role may vary depending on specific location and job-related knowledge, technical skills, and experience; and is only one part of our Total Rewards philosophy to compensate and recognize employees for their work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;On-Target Earnings Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;£77,500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;£90,000 GBP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FLEXIBLE WORKPLACE STRATEGY:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Algolia’s flexible workplace model is designed to empower all Algolians to fulfill our mission to power search and discovery with ease. We place an emphasis on an individual’s impact, contribution, and output, over their physical location. Algolia is a high-trust environment and many of our team members have the autonomy to choose where they want to work and when.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a global presence with offices in Paris, NYC, London, Sydney and Bucharest, however we also offer many of our team members the option to work remotely either as fully remote or hybrid-remote employees.&lt;strong&gt; Positions listed as &quot;Remote&quot; are only available for remote work within the specified country. Positions listed within a specific city are only available in that location - depending on the role it may be available with either a hybrid-remote or in-office schedule.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WE’RE LOOKING FOR SOMEONE WHO CAN LIVE OUR VALUES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GRIT&lt;/strong&gt; - Problem-solving and perseverance capability in an ever-changing and growing environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TRUST &lt;/strong&gt;- Willingness to trust our co-workers and to take ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CANDOR&lt;/strong&gt; - Ability to receive and give constructive feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CARE&lt;/strong&gt; - Genuine care about other team members, our clients and the decisions we make in the company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HUMILITY&lt;/strong&gt; - Aptitude for learning from others, putting ego aside.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for talented, passionate people to help build the world’s best search and discovery technology. We value autonomy, diversity, and collaboration. We’re committed to creating an inclusive workplace where everyone is respected and supported—regardless of race, age, ancestry, religion, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, marital status, color, veteran status, disability, or socioeconomic background.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;IMPORTANT NOTICE FOR CANDIDATES - Recruitment Fraud Notice&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’ve recently seen an increase in recruitment scams targeting job seekers. To help protect yourself, please keep the following in mind:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our open positions may appear on third-party job boards, but the &lt;strong&gt;best way to apply safely&lt;/strong&gt; is directly through our &lt;strong&gt;careers page&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;All genuine communication from Algolia will come from an ----- email address. If you receive an email from someone claiming to work at Algolia who does not have an ----- email address, please do not respond or share any personal information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We’ll &lt;strong&gt;never ask for payments, purchases, or financial details&lt;/strong&gt; during the hiring process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;READY TO APPLY?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you share our values and our enthusiasm for building the world’s best search &amp;amp; discovery technology, we’d love to review your application!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/algolia/channel-solutions-engineer-london-198065","tags":["Field Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1792464920},{"slug":"remote-team-lead-customer-success-southern-europe-131358","company_name":"Constructor","title":"Team Lead Customer Success - Southern Europe","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">About You</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />You're a jack-of-all-trades with a passion for cool technology and interacting with people and making them happy. You're a self-starter who's good at triaging problems and working on the most important one. You've worked directly with customers for a long time and are comfortable being the face of the company to them. One of the things that pleases you most in life is customers successfully using your product, being thrilled with its value, and telling you they're happy they partnered with you. Further, you're a curious person, and you'd love the opportunity to work with a technology team that includes data scientists, algorithm experts, back-end and front-end engineers to expand your knowledge.<br /><br />About Us<br /><br /><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Constructor.io">Constructor.io</a> powers product search and discovery for some of the largest retailers in the world. We serve billions of requests every week, and you've probably seen our results somewhere and used our product without knowing it. We differentiate ourselves by focusing on metrics over features, and reinventing search and discovery from the ground up as a machine learning challenge with the specific goal of improving metrics like revenue. We're approximately doubling year over year despite the market slow down and have customers in every eCommerce vertical.<br /><br />We're a passionate team of technologists who love solving problems and want to make our customers' and coworkers' lives better. We value empathy, openness, curiosity, continuous improvement, and are excited by metrics that matter. We believe that empowering everyone in a company to do what they think is best can lead to great things.<br /><br />About The Position<br /><br />As a Team Lead Customer Success Southern Europe, you'll be joining a rapidly growing team that helps our customers increase their revenue by improving the search and product discovery experiences of their websites and mobile apps through integrating with our services.<br /><br />Your responsibilities will include:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leading, coaching, and developing a team of Customer Success Managers across Southern Europe, with a focus on the main markets of France and Spain (and other Southern European countries)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensuring customers successfully go live and continue to see measurable value from Constructor's product.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Building and enabling your team to build trusted relationships across complex enterprise organizations: from engineers, data, and product teams to Heads and Directors of Ecommerce, Digital, Product, and Technology, up to VP and C-level executives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translating technical concepts, product capabilities, and performance data into clear business value connecting Constructor's work to outcomes like conversion, revenue, customer experience, and operational efficiency.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Implementing and iterating on scalable processes and best practices to support team growth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Acting as an escalation point for complex customer challenges and leading from the front when hands-on engagement is required.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Requirements</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">French is a must for this role; and additional languages are welcome bonuses.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Based in EMEA, ideally in Southern Europe.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least three years leading teams, with a minimum of three direct reports.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least five years managing enterprise customer relationships in Customer Success, Account Management, Solutions Consulting, or a similar customer-facing role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building trusted relationships with stakeholders ranging from technical teams and product leaders to Ecommerce Directors, VPs, and C-level executives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong executive presence and the confidence to lead strategic customer conversations, including QBRs and EBRs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong influencing and stakeholder-management skills, including the ability to create momentum without direct authority.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong problem-solving skills, intellectual curiosity, and the ability to learn quickly in a fast-moving, technically sophisticated environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in ecommerce, digital commerce, search, product discovery, or a related field is highly valued.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Benefits</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A competitive compensation package including stock options</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fully remote team - choose where you live</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work from home stipend! We want you to have the resources you need to set up your home office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Apple laptops provided for new employees</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Training and development budget for every employee, refreshed each year</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Parental leave for qualified employees</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with smart people who will help you grow and make a meaningful impact</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion at Constructor<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">At <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Constructor.io">Constructor.io</a> we are committed to cultivating a work environment that is diverse, equitable, and inclusive. As an equal opportunity employer, we welcome individuals of all backgrounds and provide equal opportunities to all applicants regardless of their education, diversity of opinion, race, color, religion, gender, gender expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, veteran status or affiliation in any other protected group.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How we handle your data.</strong> By submitting this application, you acknowledge that Constructor will collect and process the personal data you provide for the purpose of evaluating your candidacy for this role. If you are not selected, we will retain your data for a limited period as described in our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://constructor.com/recruitment-privacy-notice">Recruitment Privacy Notice</a>. After that period your data will be deleted or anonymized.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/constructor/remote-team-lead-customer-success-southern-europe-131358","tags":["Customer Success"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Remote - EMEA","created_at":1792464018},{"slug":"senior-director-infrastructure-engineering-london-306227","company_name":"Volta","title":"Senior Director Infrastructure Engineering","description":"<h2><strong>About Volta</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Volta is the category-defining, fully vertically integrated AI infrastructure platform – from capital to clusters to software, under a founder-led enterprise. Our mission is The Utility of Compute™: AI infrastructure as dependable and available as electricity, for every organization that needs it. Launched with a $10B strategic partnership with one of the leading frontier AI labs, a Series A led by Andreessen Horowitz, and a $5B AI Infrastructure Fund, Volta is building the infrastructure layer of the AI era from the ground up. We are 100+ people across London, Palo Alto, and New York, with rapid growth expectations to hundreds.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a Senior Director, Infrastructure Engineering to lead engineering across Volta's global portfolio of AI factories. You will report directly to the VP, Development and Design within the Delivery organisation and lead a team of subject matter experts spanning every infrastructure architecture and engineering discipline, from power and cooling to structures, controls and network infrastructure.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will own Volta's engineering design standards, developing and deploying them across our projects in EMEA and AMER. You will work day to day with your peers in the Design organisation to support live projects and shape Volta's Reference Design for AI factory infrastructure, and partner with the CTO and CPO organisations so that every site turns up compute consistently. You will build the engineering function, its standards and its ways of working as Volta scales.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You Will Do</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">› Lead, develop and grow a team of infrastructure engineering SMEs across architecture, electrical, mechanical, cooling, structural, civil, controls and network infrastructure disciplines, building the capability to support a fast growing global pipeline</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">› Develop and deploy Volta's engineering design standards and specifications for AI factories, making sure they are applied consistently across every project and region</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">› Work with peers in the Design organisation to provide engineering input into Volta's Reference Design for AI factory infrastructure, balancing performance, cost, speed of delivery and scalability</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">› Support live projects with engineering expertise from concept through detailed design, construction and commissioning, resolving technical issues quickly so delivery is never held up</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">› Partner with the CTO and CPO organisations to align facility design with compute, rack and network requirements, enabling consistent turn up of compute across the portfolio</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">› Track the evolution of AI hardware, including rack densities, liquid cooling and power architectures, and translate it into design standards that keep Volta's AI factories ready for next generation compute</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">› Own engineering governance, including design reviews, technical assurance and design authority for any departure from standard</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">› Work with Procurement to standardise specifications for long lead equipment, enabling framework agreements, prefabrication and modular delivery at scale</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">› Champion safety in design, reliability, maintainability and energy and water efficiency, working with Operations to design for how our facilities will be run</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">› Embed lessons learned from delivery and operations back into the standards, so every AI factory builds faster, safer and more efficiently than the last</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">› Provide engineering status, risk and decision reporting to the VP, Development and Design and the executive team</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You Will Bring</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">› A degree in electrical, mechanical, civil or building services engineering, with chartered or professional engineer status (for example CEng or PE) preferred</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">› Significant experience in data centre or mission critical infrastructure engineering, including senior leadership of multidisciplinary engineering teams</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">› Deep technical expertise in at least one core discipline, such as power distribution or cooling, and a strong working knowledge across all infrastructure disciplines</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">› A track record developing and deploying design standards, reference designs or basis of design documents for a hyperscale, colocation or large scale data centre developer</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">› Hands on experience with high density and liquid cooled environments for AI and HPC workloads, and an understanding of how GPU cluster requirements drive facility design</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">› Strong commercial judgement, balancing capex, schedule, reliability and operability in design decisions</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">› Confident executive level communication, able to explain complex technical trade offs clearly to technical and non-technical stakeholders</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">› A collaborative leadership style that builds trust with peers across partner teams, and the conviction to hold the line on standards</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">› Exposure to both North American and European projects, or to utility scale power, onsite generation or energy storage, would be an advantage</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What We Offer</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Volta, we believe people do their best work when they feel supported, trusted and able to grow. We're building a company where you can make an impact, keep a healthy balance between work and life, and build a career you're proud of. <br />As a global team, we do our best to provide great benefits wherever you're based. While some benefits vary by country due to local regulations, we believe looking after our people is simply the right thing to do.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive salary based on the work you do here, not your previous salary</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Equity in Volta, giving you the opportunity to share in the company's long-term success</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Retirement/pension contributions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comprehensive health, wellbeing and insurance benefits</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Generous number of vacation days each year</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Additional Information</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Background Checks</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">All offers of employment at Volta are conditional on the satisfactory completion of pre-employment screening, which includes confirmation of your right to work, verification of your employment history and a criminal record check, where this is permitted by local law. Screening is carried out by Zinc, an accredited third-party provider, after an offer is made and all information is handled confidentially and in accordance with applicable data protection law.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Equal Opportunity</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Volta is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive team and make employment decisions based on skills, qualifications, experience and business needs. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, veteran status or any other legally protected characteristic.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Accessibility</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Volta is committed to providing an accessible recruitment experience for all candidates. If you require accommodations or adjustments at any stage of the application or interview process, please contact us at <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="Hyperlink SCXW200826348 BCX0" ---------- We will work with you to identify reasonable accommodations that enable you to participate fully in the hiring process.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Candidate Privacy Notice</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">By applying, you consent to the processing of your personal data for recruitment purposes in accordance with applicable data protection laws, including the UK GDPR, EU GDPR and relevant US state privacy regulations. Your data will be shared only with those involved in the hiring process and will not be used for unrelated purposes. For details, see our Recruitment &amp; Candidate Privacy Notice.<br /></p><h3><strong>Note to Recruitment Agencies</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Volta does not accept unsolicited CVs or candidate profiles from recruitment agencies. Any unsolicited submissions, including those sent directly to hiring managers or employees, will be treated as the property of Volta. No agency fees will be payable unless a valid, signed recruitment agreement is in place, and the agency has been specifically engaged for the relevant vacancy.</p><hr><p>Compensation: £200K – £240K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus • Multiple Ranges</p><ul><li>United Kingdom • £200K – £240K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus</li><li>USA • $260K – $320K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/volta/senior-director-infrastructure-engineering-london-306227","tags":["Delivery"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"United Kingdom - Remote","created_at":1792464018},{"slug":"junior-account-executive-uk-market-london-425232","company_name":"Mollie","title":"Junior Account Executive - UK market","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build with us</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Businesses deserve better from finance. Less friction, more freedom. Since 2004, Mollie has been on a mission to make payments and money management effortless for every business in Europe.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, more than 250,000 companies trust our all-in-one platform to get paid, manage money and grow on their terms. Simple, scalable and built with real businesses in mind.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're one of Europe's fastest-growing fintechs, with 950+ Mollies across 14+ locations. Our people make this growth possible. We move fast, build with purpose and care deeply about our customers. Whether you're solving problems, building market-leading products or exploring how AI can make work smarter, you'll have the freedom to create and the trust to deliver.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you're ready to grow, shape the future of fintech and join an ambitious, high-performing team, this is the place for you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your impact<br /></strong>The United Kingdom is a critical frontier for Mollie’s mission. As a Junior Account Executive, you aren't just making calls; you are the engine driving our expansion in the UK market. By identifying and connecting with high-potential businesses, you directly contribute to our goal of eliminating financial bureaucracy for merchants across the region.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will join a high-velocity team of 7, working closely with other Account Executives to build a robust, high-quality pipeline. This is a role for an ambitious contributor who wants to own their territory, influence business strategy, and see the immediate results of their work in our growth metrics.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll ship<br /></strong>Own the full sales cycle from prospecting to close, building our pipeline in the UK market and hitting your revenue targets</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive high-impact outbound prospecting campaigns through a multi-channel approach (email, phone, social selling) to identify and engage high-potential businesses.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Conduct in-depth discovery calls to understand prospect challenges, qualify opportunities, and demonstrate the value of the Mollie solution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead commercial and contractual negotiations from proposal to signature, converting qualified prospects into new Mollie customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate closely with Marketing, Product, and Onboarding teams to refine our strategy and ensure the long-term success of your customers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience in full-cycle outbound sales, specifically within the UK market.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of hitting and exceeding targets in a fast-paced environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mastery of multi-channel prospecting, including cold calling, emailing, and social selling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with CRM systems and sales tools like Salesforce, Bigmind, or LinkedIn Sales Navigator.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A natural curiosity and a passion for continuous learning, essential for thriving in a fast-paced, ever-evolving tech industry.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Grow your way</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Mollie, growth is personal. We believe everyone should have the chance to develop their skills, explore new challenges and shape their career on their own terms.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll get regular feedback and performance reviews to support your development, with fair and transparent salary reviews along the way. Many Mollies move into new roles or take on new projects to stretch themselves, and we actively hire from within to help you take the next step.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">No matter if you're aiming for promotion, exploring a different career path or building new skills, you'll be supported with the tools, trust and opportunities to grow your way.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Unlock your full potential and join us to eliminate financial bureaucracy</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you're excited by the idea of building what's next, for yourself and for thousands of businesses across Europe, we'd love to hear from you. Apply with your CV (in English) using the form below.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Want a peek behind the scenes? Check out what life at Mollie is really like.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI at Mollie</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe in Always Be Shipping, and AI brings that philosophy to life across every team, every role, every day</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI is core to how we build. It helps us move faster, simplify work and make smarter decisions, creating real impact for the businesses we serve. We're looking for people who are excited to use AI to shape the future of finance with us.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/mollie/junior-account-executive-uk-market-london-425232","tags":["Go To Market"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792464017},{"slug":"executive-assistant-london-493217","company_name":"Monday.com","title":"Executive Assistant","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://monday.com">monday.com</a> is the AI work platform powering the most ambitious teams. 250,000+ customers across departments use us to bring people, workflows, and AI agents together on one flexible platform where AI doesn't just assist, it executes. We move fast, build things that matter, and foster an ownership-driven culture where you're empowered to shape how organizations work and outpace their competition.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://monday.com"><u>monday.com</u></a> is hiring an <strong>Executive Assistant</strong> to serve as the right-hand person to the <strong>GM of our EMEA Region</strong> as well as the <strong>Global VP of Partnerships</strong>. In this role, you will provide strategic administrative and project management support, handling calendar management and travel planning while serving as a full partner on projects, initiatives, and events.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The chosen candidate can build this role independently; with the right passion, the sky is the limit. You will join our <strong>Operations Team</strong>, based in our <strong>London office</strong>.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About The Role</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage all administrative aspects of the GM EMEA and the VP of Partnerships in an efficient, effective, and professional manner.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Point of contact for internal and external interfaces.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Oversee meeting coordination from sending invites, scheduling catering, securing meeting spaces, and follow-up correspondence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Oversee executive-level hospitality and event logistics, ensuring flawless coordination for C-suite office visits, town halls, and internal forums.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage travel coordination, including booking flights, hotels, and local transportation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Handle the VP’s matters with the highest confidentiality and time sensitivity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Responsibility for special projects that are relevant to the work of the VPs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be part of the company's EA guild, contributing to a collaborative network of executive assistants and providing admin support and assistance across the business and senior leadership when needed.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid experience as an Executive Assistant in a fast-paced environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in Saas/Tech environment is a must.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are a self-starter with strong organisational and time-management skills.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have excellent written and verbal communication skills.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can multitask while remaining detail-oriented.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are proactive, resourceful, and self-driven; you can anticipate needs before we know they exist.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are willing to accept and embrace change in a fast-paced environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency in English.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://monday.com"><strong>monday.com</strong></a><strong> can offer you:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join a customer-obsessed team where transparency and ownership are how we actually operate - not just things we put on a wall.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive salary, benefits, bonus potential, and equity eligibility for many roles — we believe people should share in our success.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A collaborative, global culture backed by Employee Resource Groups and workplace teams across New York, Tel Aviv, London, Munich, Warsaw, Tokyo, Sydney, and more.</p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/mondaycom/executive-assistant-london-493217","tags":["Consulting"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792464017},{"slug":"senior-gtm-onboarding-manager-london-49076","company_name":"Zoominfo","title":"Senior GTM Onboarding Manager","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;ZoomInfo is where careers accelerate. We move fast, think boldly, and empower you to do the best work of your life. You’ll be surrounded by teammates who care deeply, challenge each other, and celebrate wins. With tools that amplify your impact and a culture that backs your ambition, you won’t just contribute. You’ll make things happen–fast.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the &lt;strong&gt;Senior Customer Onboarding Manager&lt;/strong&gt;, you will be responsible for ensuring the successful execution of ZoomInfo&#39;s customer onboarding strategy and accelerating customer adoption of ZoomInfo&#39;s products and solutions. This role combines go-to-market (GTM) expertise, solution development, and project management to help customers translate business objectives into actionable use cases and measurable outcomes. The Senior GTM Onboarding Manager partners with Customer Success, Customer Training, and Customer Integrations teams to develop and execute effective onboarding plans, including goals, timelines, solution deployment, and resource coordination to accelerate value for ZoomInfo customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage comprehensive onboarding programs for a portfolio of ZoomInfo customers, ensuring a highly organized experience with clearly defined goals, timelines, deliverables, and success metrics. Serve as a primary point of contact throughout onboarding and implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead strategic discovery conversations to understand customers&#39; GTM objectives, business challenges, existing workflows, and technology environments, translating insights into actionable onboarding strategies and prioritized use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute implementation strategies that align customer business objectives with ZoomInfo&#39;s products and capabilities, ensuring successful onboarding within defined SLAs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with customers to assist with design, build, and deploy GTM solutions and workflows, demonstrating a hands-on approach to translating business requirements into practical, scalable solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with customers to establish expectations, define project milestones, manage dependencies, coordinate customer tasks, and provide regular updates throughout the onboarding lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally with Customer Success, Training, Integrations, and Solutions Engineering teams to deliver a cohesive implementation experience that drives product adoption and measurable business value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage multiple simultaneous onboarding projects, balancing strategic priorities, customer satisfaction, technical requirements, and execution timelines while proactively identifying risks and removing obstacles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a strategic advisor to customers, applying GTM best practices and product expertise to recommend solutions that improve sales and marketing processes, operational efficiency, and business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure a seamless transition to Customer Success and Account Management teams through standardized handoff documentation that captures customer objectives, deployed use cases, implementation milestones, wins, challenges, and opportunities for continued growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply creativity, critical thinking, and strong business acumen to solve complex customer challenges, continuously improve onboarding processes, and identify opportunities to accelerate customer value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in customer onboarding, customer success, GTM consulting, solutions implementation, and/or project management, ideally within a SaaS environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of B2B go-to-market strategies, including sales prospecting, pipeline generation, account prioritization, territory planning, marketing operations, and revenue workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A consultative mindset with the ability to translate business challenges into actionable strategies, use cases, and technical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working hands-on to build, configure, and deploy solutions, with an ability to move seamlessly between strategic planning and tactical execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent project management skills, including the ability to manage multiple complex implementations, coordinate cross-functional stakeholders, maintain timelines, and deliver high-quality outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage competing priorities, rapidly adapt to changing customer needs, and proactively address project risks and dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to assess customer requirements, identify gaps, and recommend practical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing, implementing, training, and/or supporting B2B SaaS solutions (previous experience with ZoomInfo and/or ZoomInfo certification strongly preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong familiarity with Salesforce CRM and an understanding of common GTM technology ecosystems, integrations, and workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly collaborative, organized, and execution-oriented, with excellent presentation and stakeholder management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to confidently facilitate strategic customer conversations, communicate technical concepts to business audiences, and influence stakeholders at various levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated, adaptable, and comfortable operating in a fast-paced environment that values ownership, innovation, and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superior relationship-building and communication skills, both verbal and written.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a &lt;strong&gt;hybrid&lt;/strong&gt; position, working a minimum of &lt;strong&gt;three days per week&lt;/strong&gt; from our London England office&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ZoomInfo (NASDAQ: GTM) is the Go-To-Market Intelligence Platform that empowers businesses to grow faster with AI-ready insights, trusted data, and advanced automation. Its solutions provide more than 35,000 companies worldwide with a complete view of their customers, making every seller their best seller.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ZoomInfo is committed to protecting your privacy when you apply for jobs with us. Please review our Job Applicant &lt;a href=&quot;https://drive.google.com/file/d/1yiG-k0YX_sW10PiJk_xliDc3W-veJCrK/view?usp=drive_link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; for more details on how we handle your personal information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ZoomInfo may use a software-based assessment as part of the recruitment process. More information about this tool, including the results of the most recent bias audit, is available &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoominfo.com/legal/nyc-local-law-144-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ZoomInfo is proud to be an equal opportunity employer, hiring based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, and does not discriminate based on protected status. We welcome all applicants and are committed to providing equal employment opportunities regardless of sex, race, age, color, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, disability status, religion, protected military or veteran status, medical condition, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. We also consider qualified candidates with criminal histories in accordance with legal requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For Massachusetts Applicants: It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment. An employer who violates this law shall be subject to criminal penalties and civil liability. ZoomInfo does not administer lie detector tests to applicants in any location.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/zoominfo/senior-gtm-onboarding-manager-london-49076","tags":["864 Client Services - Onboarding"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1792454114},{"slug":"senior-software-engineer-london-229334","company_name":"Chaosindustries","title":"Senior Software Engineer","description":"&lt;p&gt;CHAOS Industries is redefining modern defense with a multi-product portfolio that gives the ultimate advantage—domain dominance. The company&#39;s products are powered by Coherent Distributed Networks (CDN™), empowering warfighters, commercial air operators, and border protection teams to act faster, adapt rapidly, and stay ahead of evolving threats.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CHAOS Industries was founded in 2022 and has raised a total of $1 billion in funding from leading investors, including 8VC, Accel, and Valor Equity Partners. The company is headquartered in Los Angeles, with offices in Washington, D.C., San Francisco, San Diego, Seattle, and London. For more information, please visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.chaosinc.com&quot;&gt;www.chaosinc.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll join a small, highly collaborative team working across London and San Francisco, building the software behind some of the world’s most advanced radar systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working alongside software, hardware, and systems engineers, and the teams who take these systems into the field, you’ll design the backend services, data pipelines, and operator-facing applications that turn raw sensor data into decisions people can act on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The systems you build must be reliable, resilient, secure, and performant - enabling operators to depend on them in the environments where they matter most.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-ownership role where you’ll influence architecture and help define the engineering foundations of a rapidly evolving platform. We’re looking for engineers who enjoy scaling distributed systems and solving hard data problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You’ll Build&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backend Services&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- develop high-performance Python services that ingest, process, and distribute real-time sensor data with low latency, high reliability, and security at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operator Interfaces&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- build and evolve the web applications operators use to monitor live missions and investigate what the sensors saw (TypeScript and React).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cloud Platform&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- design and build secure, scalable Azure services that power distributed radar systems, defining the infrastructure as code and instrumentation for the systems you own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platform Architecture&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- help shape the technical direction of the platform, making architectural decisions that support new capabilities, increasing scale, and long-term maintainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for exceptional software engineers who are excited by solving hard technical problems and building systems that matter. You don’t need experience with every technology we use - we value strong engineering fundamentals, curiosity, and the ability to learn quickly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll thrive in this role if you:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoy building scalable backend systems and taking ownership of production services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoy solving complex distributed systems and real-time data challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are eager to learn new technologies and adapt to new technical domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Care deeply about reliability, security, and scalability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get real leverage from AI coding tools, with a considered view on what to delegate to them and what not to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate well and enjoy collaborating across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are motivated by building technology with meaningful real-world impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Requirements&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Right to work in the UK.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Willingness to travel.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;You’ll be based in our Soho office in London, but most of the team is in San Francisco - expect to co-locate there for around a week each quarter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Why CHAOS?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Health Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt; private medical, dental and vision benefits (for employees &amp;amp; dependents) will be 100% paid for by the company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional benefits&lt;/strong&gt;: 5% pension match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation Components:&lt;/strong&gt; competitive base salaries, generous pre-IPO stock option grants, relocation assistance + (coming soon!) annual bonuses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Growth: &lt;/strong&gt;350 employees and counting across 5 global offices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The stated compensation range reflects only the targeted base compensation range and excludes additional earnings such as bonus, equity, and benefits. If your compensation requirements fall outside of the range, we still encourage you to apply. The salary range for this role is an estimate based on a range of compensation factors, inclusive of base salary only. Actual salary offer may vary based on (but not limited to) work experience, education and/or training, critical skills, and/or business considerations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Recruiting Agencies: CHAOS Industries does not accept unsolicited resumes or outreach. Unsolicited submissions will not be reviewed or compensated.&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
