&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/riverlane/software-engineering-internship-2027-cambridge-68713","tags":["Internships"],"job_types":[],"location":"Cambridge","created_at":1792454113},{"slug":"2027-nextgen-finance-degree-apprenticeship-london-130196","company_name":"Checkout.com","title":"2027 NextGen Finance Degree Apprenticeship","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Company Description</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We’re</em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="http://checkout.com"><em> </em></a><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com"><em>Checkout.com</em></a><em>. You might not know our name, but companies like eBay, Spotify, Klarna, Uber, and Sony do, because we’re behind many of the digital experiences you use every day. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><em>We are where the world checks out, enabling over 10 billion transactions yearly for more than one billion global shoppers. </em><br /><br /><em>Whether you want to book a holiday, order food, renew a subscription, or check out online, there’s a good chance our tech powers the payments behind the scenes. Our platform helps the most ambitious businesses deliver effortless digital experiences, at scale. </em><br /><br /><em>If you want to do career-defining work, you’ve come to the right place. We move fast, think globally, and believe great teams are built by hiring exceptional people with conviction, curiosity, and the desire to make an impact. </em><br /><br /><em>With 20 offices across six continents and London as our HQ, we’re shaping the future of fintech – and we’re just getting started.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As part of Checkout.com’s #NextGen Early Careers Program, we are looking for an ambitious Finance Analyst Apprentice to join our fast-paced EU Finance department. Reporting directly to the Regional Finance Director, you will work alongside experienced professionals, gain hands-on experience, and join a global community with technical training, mentorship, and regular networking opportunities to accelerate your growth.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Through a structured three-year program, you will balance real team deliverables with study towards your ACCA (Association of Chartered Certified Accountants) qualification, dedicating 20% of your time (around six hours per week) to your professional studies. Each placement will be supported by a dedicated Rotation Manager alongside guidance from senior Finance leadership.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will gain broad exposure across six core finance pillars: Financial Control and Revenue &amp; Billing in year one; Tax and Treasury in year two; and Strategic Finance and Finance Transformation in year three. Depending on business and ACCA requirements, you may also gain exposure to adjacent areas such as Product Control, Procurement, or Internal Audit.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How You’ll Make An Impact</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support accurate, timely finance operations across your rotations, contributing to processes such as month-end close, reconciliations, journals and variance analysis.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help teams deliver invoicing, settlement, revenue recognition, tax compliance, cash management, budgeting and reporting activities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare and review information carefully, including supporting audit, compliance and management reporting requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with colleagues across Finance to respond to queries, share information and deliver tasks to agreed deadlines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Look for practical ways to improve processes, documentation and the use of finance systems and data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Apply what you learn through ACCA study to real finance work, building technical, analytical and communication skills over time.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Eligibility Requirements</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is offered as a government-funded Level 7 ACCA apprenticeship. Appointment is conditional on the successful candidate meeting the government’s apprenticeship funding and eligibility requirements at the start of training, as confirmed by our approved training provider. Under current England funding rules, Level 7 funding is generally available to applicants aged 16–21, with limited exceptions for eligible applicants aged 22–24 who have an EHCP or have been, or are, in care.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is offered as an early-careers opportunity and we are not able to offer this role on a privately funded basis. Further information about the Apprenticeship funding can be found here.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Academic Qualifications: </strong>You will have either:</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A degree qualification</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">OR</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have completed a Level 4 AAT qualification before the September start date</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">+ 2 A Levels (or equivalent) and 3 GCSEs including a pass in English and Maths </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Visa sponsorship: </strong>We are unable to offer visa sponsorship for this role.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What We’re Looking For</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Academic Ambition: You are eager to begin your journey toward becoming a Chartered Accountant via the ACCA pathway.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Analytical Mindset: You have a natural comfort with numbers and a high attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Resilience: The ability to work toward tight deadlines in a fast-paced, high-growth work environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tech Savvy: Proficiency in Excel or Google Sheets. Any prior exposure to accounting systems (like Workday) is a huge plus, but not a dealbreaker—we will train you!</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communication: Excellent verbal and written communication skills and a "team player" attitude.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency with Excel or Google Sheets; familiarity with finance systems such as Workday is helpful, but not essential.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Additional Information</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bring all of you to work</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We create the conditions for high performers to thrive, through real ownership, fewer blockers, and work that makes a difference from day one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Here, you’ll move fast, take on meaningful challenges, and be recognized for the impact you deliver. It’s a place where ambition gets met with opportunity, and where your growth is in your hands.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work as one team, and we back each other to succeed. So whatever your background or identity, if you’re ready to grow and make a difference, you’ll be right at home here.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It’s important we set you up for success and make our process as accessible as possible. So let us know in your application, or tell your recruiter directly, if you need anything to make your experience or working environment more comfortable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Life at </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://