calable, high-performing systems using best practices in a microservices architecture.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write clean, testable, and maintainable code for some of Checkout’s most impactful platforms.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with cross-functional teams, including product management, to solve real-world business challenges.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stay up to date with emerging technologies and share your knowledge across the engineering community.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Operate and own the resilience and performance of the systems you develop.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mentor and support peers while growing your own technical expertise.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we’re looking for</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re a curious, motivated, and innovative future engineer, either due to graduate in summer 2027 or having graduated within the last 12 months, who is excited to dive into the world of digital payments and technology. Here’s what you’ll bring to the team:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field or relevant work experience in these fields.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency in one or more programming languages (e.g. .NET C#, Java, Python, or Go), with an understanding of core software engineering principles.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong communication skills and the ability to collaborate with diverse teams and stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with or enthusiasm for working in agile environments and delivering high-quality code on tight deadlines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A passion for solving complex technical problems—independently and as part of a team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Payments or financial knowledge is a bonus, but not required.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why Join Us?</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work on impactful projects alongside industry experts, tackling some of the most exciting challenges in fintech.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Grow your skills in a dynamic, fast-paced environment where learning and development are a top priority.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join a diverse and supportive team that values innovation, collaboration, and excellence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be part of a company shaping the future of digital payments on a global scale.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Additional Information</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bring all of you to work</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We create the conditions for high performers to thrive, through real ownership, fewer blockers, and work that makes a difference from day one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Here, you’ll move fast, take on meaningful challenges, and be recognized for the impact you deliver. It’s a place where ambition gets met with opportunity, and where your growth is in your hands.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work as one team, and we back each other to succeed. So whatever your background or identity, if you’re ready to grow and make a difference, you’ll be right at home here.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It’s important we set you up for success and make our process as accessible as possible. So let us know in your application, or tell your recruiter directly, if you need anything to make your experience or working environment more comfortable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Life at </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com"><strong>Checkout.com</strong></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We understand that work is just one part of your life. Our hybrid working model offers flexibility, with three days per week in the office to support collaboration and connection.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curious about what it’s like to be part of our team? Visit our<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.checkout.com/careers"> <u>Careers Page</u></a> to learn more about our culture, open roles, and what drives us.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For a closer look at daily life at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com">Checkout.com</a>, follow us on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/checkout/life/"><u>LinkedIn</u></a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.instagram.com/checkout_com/"><u>Instagram</u></a></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/checkoutcom/2027-nextgen-technology-programme-london-390540","tags":["All Departments"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792453217},{"slug":"real-estate-analyst-london-94122","company_name":"Checkout.com","title":"Real Estate Analyst","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Company Description</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We’re</em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="http://checkout.com"><em> </em></a><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com"><em>Checkout.com</em></a><em>. You might not know our name, but companies like eBay, Spotify, Klarna, Uber, and Sony do, because we’re behind many of the digital experiences you use every day. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><em>We are where the world checks out, enabling over 10 billion transactions yearly for more than one billion global shoppers. </em><br /><br /><em>Whether you want to book a holiday, order food, renew a subscription, or check out online, there’s a good chance our tech powers the payments behind the scenes. Our platform helps the most ambitious businesses deliver effortless digital experiences, at scale. </em><br /><br /><em>If you want to do career-defining work, you’ve come to the right place. We move fast, think globally, and believe great teams are built by hiring exceptional people with conviction, curiosity, and the desire to make an impact. </em><br /><br /><em>With 20 offices across six continents and London as our HQ, we’re shaping the future of fintech – and we’re just getting started.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Role Description</strong><br />As a Real Estate Analyst at Checkout.com, you will provide dedicated administrative, data management, and operational support to the Head of Real Estate, focusing on mitigating risk and increasing efficiency across the global portfolio. This role is essential for managing high-risk operational tasks, such as lease event tracking, lease administration, budgeting and data reporting to ensure a structured approach and prevent critical errors.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>1. Lease Administration &amp; Governance</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proactively track, monitor, and manage critical dates for all lease events, including renewals and break clauses, acting as the primary conduit for populating and managing the tools that host our Real Estate data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the execution of Real Estate contracts by coordinating with Brokers, Procurement, Legal etc. to finalise signing, updating project budgets, and archiving completed agreements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage operational risk by ensuring all key details related to lease obligations are accurately recorded, tracked and action is taken.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">For business case generation, gather comparable evidence, property valuations, and market data to drive strategic negotiations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Liaise with regional, business and central teams to capture the justification and data necessary for business case approval.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage subleasing activities, including monitoring sub-tenant compliance, tracking sublease income and key milestones, and coordinating with legal and property management teams.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>2. Financial and Procurement Reporting</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate with Finance, Tax and Procurement teams for Real Estate budgets, including updating and managing the Real Estate OPEX and CAPEX budget tracking tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the central point of contact for all property-related budget reporting, preparing quarterly reviews in a clear, digestible format that includes Real Estate and Workplace costs - giving an all inclusive cost per desk / square foot / head.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assist in reporting refurbishment or new office delivery costs, against business as usual spend for operational office locations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the coordination of financial and legal documentation required for transactions, such as preparing group structure charts and financials for external parties (e.g., landlords).</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>3. Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) Data Collation</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead the coordination and collection of energy, water, and utility consumption data across the global portfolio to support future CSR reporting requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage the challenge of obtaining utility data in co-working and serviced spaces where direct meter readings are complex, including liaising with local teams, operators and landlords to gather the necessary information.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the conduit between the CEO Office and ESG/CSR teams to ensure our portfolio meets the needs of Sustainability policies and or regulatory requirements.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>4. Departmental Administrative Support</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assist in due diligence and preparation of business cases by researching and reporting on regional office statistics (e.g., desk counts, utilisation, attendance, capacity &amp; commercials).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as a key liaison for business case presentation and refinement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain dynamic headcount forecasts to ensure space planning aligns with evolving business needs, particularly for high-growth regions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor and document team shift patterns to inform workspace strategy (e.g., HVAC service requirements, after-hours access, and desk rotation models).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor and manage utilisation reports for Serviced Offices, along with onboard and offboard leaves to locations where we do not directly manage access control.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain the central digital repository for all property documentation (leases, contracts, floor plans, and insurance certificates), ensuring strict naming conventions, accessibility, and version control are met to ensure 100% audit-readiness.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Schedule and prepare agendas, collate pre-read materials, and document meeting minutes for key real estate governance forums, proactively tracking action items to ensure timely closure by stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Managing the administrative aspects of the "joiner/leaver" process for office access where no assigned Workplace / People person is assigned.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the primary administrator for processing property-related invoices, performing the initial "first-pass" review to flag discrepancies against purchase orders (POs) and ensuring all costs are accurately coded before final submission to Finance.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>5. Health, Safety &amp; Physical Security Management</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate the global H&amp;S audit schedule in partnership with SMEs, managing the central audit database, evidence library, action log, and training records to track progress and compliance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the weekly, monthly, quarterly, and annual reporting framework to surface risk trends and audit completion status, allocating audits to regional teams for execution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the scheduling, chasing, and evidence trail for the audit lifecycle, acting as the primary administrative point of contact to ensure smooth execution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive the audit lifecycle by ensuring all actions are identified, triaged, and managed to resolution, proactively identifying blockers and managing overdue items.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure regional teams interpret and apply the central H&amp;S framework in accordance with local laws while maintaining the global baseline standards.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage the integration of the H&amp;S framework with wider Real Estate RACI to ensure clear accountability and prevent overlaps in responsibilities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Implement and maintain physical security policies and standards across all global office locations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Instruct periodic physical security risk assessments and audits to identify vulnerabilities and ensure compliance with security protocols.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Oversee visitor management processes and physical security measures to safeguard personnel and assets.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Additional Information</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bring all of you to work</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We create the conditions for high performers to thrive, through real ownership, fewer blockers, and work that makes a difference from day one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Here, you’ll move fast, take on meaningful challenges, and be recognized for the impact you deliver. It’s a place where ambition gets met with opportunity, and where your growth is in your hands.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work as one team, and we back each other to succeed. So whatever your background or identity, if you’re ready to grow and make a difference, you’ll be right at home here.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It’s important we set you up for success and make our process as accessible as possible. So let us know in your application, or tell your recruiter directly, if you need anything to make your experience or working environment more comfortable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Life at </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com"><strong>Checkout.com</strong></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We understand that work is just one part of your life. Our hybrid working model offers flexibility, with three days per week in the office to support collaboration and connection.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curious about what it’s like to be part of our team? Visit our<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.checkout.com/careers"> <u>Careers Page</u></a> to learn more about our culture, open roles, and what drives us.</p>