al people with conviction, curiosity, and the desire to make an impact. </em><br /><br /><em>With 20 offices across six continents and London as our HQ, we’re shaping the future of fintech – and we’re just getting started.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are seeking an exceptionally organized, tech-forward <strong>Talent Operations Associate</strong> to join our Global Talent Acquisition team. As our Talent Operations Associate in <strong>London</strong>, you will bridge the gap between ensuring our recruiters, and interviewer community are able to find the best talent, through  cutting-edge Talent Operations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are seeking a proactive AI and automation expert to transform our hiring operations. In this role, you will leverage emerging tools to streamline scheduling, resolve logistics challenges, and build data-driven dashboards. If you thrive on solving complex problems, engaging consultatively with senior stakeholders, and redefining talent operations, we want to hear from you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Data reporting:</strong> handle regional and departmental data reporting, and produce reports and dashboards for the talent acquisition team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI, automation &amp; workflow optimisation:</strong> use AI tools and automation to remove manual bottlenecks, hunt for friction points in daily operations, and redesign workflows toward an admin-zero environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>TA Ops projects:</strong>Work on a range of strategic projects as needed for example interviewer training, implementing new tooling or designing refined TA processes.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Additional Responsibilities</strong><