&lt;p&gt;The hospitality industry is uniquely human, and it deserves technology that’s just as inspiring as the people behind it. At Mews, we’re transforming the industry with a platform that helps hotels run smarter, move faster and create better guest experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work with smart, curious people who care deeply about what they do. You’ll have autonomy and the trust to make good decisions and move quickly. And you’ll enjoy a real sense of purpose as you see the impact of what we’re building.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re motivated by ownership, curiosity and meaningful impact, and are driven to deliver consistent high performance, you’ll feel at home here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Let&#39;s get into the specifics. It’s impossible to capture every nuance of a role – especially at a rapidly growing company like Mews – but if we had to distil it into a job description (which we do because this is a job description), it would be this:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Sales Manager at Mews, you will own a territory—and own it at scale. You have 3+ years of proven quota attainment, and you&#39;ve demonstrated ambition to grow and take on increasingly complex challenges. You will close larger deals, build scalable playbooks, and serve as an ambassador for sales excellence across the team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mews powers 15,000+ properties across 85 countries. In 2025, we processed nearly $20 billion in transactions. In 2026, we raised $300 million in Series D funding at a $2.5 billion valuation. We are approaching IPO. The market is global, the product is unmatched, and the territories are genuinely winnable at scale. The question is whether you are the person to own a territory and lift the entire team&#39;s standard.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;351&quot; data-local-id=&quot;215fb90a5af3&quot;&gt;&lt;mark id=&quot;a22f7726-560b-4c94-9d38-27bcfc998281&quot; class=&quot;css-100s7ye&quot; data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot; data-mark-type=&quot;annotation&quot; data-mark-annotation-type=&quot;inlineComment&quot; data-id=&quot;a22f7726-560b-4c94-9d38-27bcfc998281&quot; data-mark-annotation-state=&quot;resolved&quot; data-has-focus=&quot;false&quot; data-is-hovered=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/mark&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;_3iDTPbvLZJ renderer-heading-wrapper&quot; data-testid=&quot;renderer-heading-wrapper&quot; data-level=&quot;2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;What-you-would-do&quot; data-local-id=&quot;974c86851289&quot; data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;768&quot;&gt;What you would do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-local-id=&quot;974c86851289&quot; data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;768&quot;&gt;Full ownership of a territory with quota targets, closing deals (€5,000+)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-local-id=&quot;974c86851289&quot; data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;768&quot;&gt;Strategic territory growth planning: building 2-3 year plans, not just quarterly targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-local-id=&quot;974c86851289&quot; data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;768&quot;&gt;Working with Multi-stakeholder deals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-local-id=&quot;974c86851289&quot; data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;768&quot;&gt;A pipeline built from outbound prospecting, with strategic account planning and targeted expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-local-id=&quot;974c86851289&quot; data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;768&quot;&gt;Mentoring and coaching of Sales Managers—not just your own discipline, but their development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-local-id=&quot;974c86851289&quot; data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;768&quot;&gt;Thought partnership with commercial leadership on scaling motions, team development, and market strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-local-id=&quot;974c86851289&quot; data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;768&quot;&gt;Representation of the sales team across cross-functional initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-local-id=&quot;974c86851289&quot; data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;768&quot;&gt;Use AI to redesign how your territory and team work, not just how you personally work. Build an AI-powered territory analysis framework your team follows. Create deal-coaching workflows that scale your mentoring. Actively question what AI gives you and know when to abandon an output.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1664&quot; data-local-id=&quot;4180db2f048a&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;AI Fluency Level 3:&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ve redesigned how your territory and team work using AI, not just how you personally work. You&#39;ve built approaches other Sales Managers follow—whether it&#39;s an AI-powered territory analysis framework, a prospecting workflow that uses AI to prioritize accounts, or a deal-coaching process that scales your mentoring. You actively question what AI gives you, push back when it&#39;s wrong, and know when to abandon an output entirely. At &lt;span data-highlighted=&quot;true&quot; data-vc=&quot;highlighted-text&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;_1mT5xdRAKS&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;_0nmozVaHVx _2V7sgO2M4S _3BoeIDwZ7G _30zrXRyxdf _0ReiIH7zJH&quot; data-testid=&quot;definition-highlighter&quot;&gt;IC3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;, you&#39;re thinking about how to multiply yourself through AI and through your team, not just how it speeds up your own work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2247&quot; data-local-id=&quot;87a5f0f2b3c3&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;For more information on AI fluency at Mews, please refer to &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;_2hGPVj98eZ _2i3C1kYbGa _2kH23qT6kp _1ubuxonXvL _34b3D2vc3e _1NDpvb6wH8 _2wtOC9vc3e _3e11vU6wH8 _0hSAgbHZdu _00uqCY98eZ _3xtjKN0Rl6 _0H9qDF6wH8 _24h04i2Njc _1mT5xdRAKS _0bjKvDcjp5 _0WKd3G4z3T _23rrnHo10F _1UtDYzM7Tp _32C2rk98eZ _0i9AWA0Rl6 _0mm6KQ6wH8 _10n1R5M7Tp _0DCa9DjOvk _3932vv0Rl6 _02cRtH6wH8 _1B4rbIo10F _0clgaMM7Tp _3WzCGijOvk _0NqVRt0Rl6 _3BKYwu6wH8 _3sFUREDdj4 _0CMRbkAwSC _2nTuUYWfPD _3ADzdEWfPD _1warJ9WfPD _4scvAwWyeI&quot; href=&quot;https://mews.atlassian.net/wiki/x/XQOskg&quot; data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot; data-is-router-link=&quot;false&quot; data-testid=&quot;link-with-safety&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;AI Fluency at Mews: A Comprehensive Guide for Candidates&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt; on Confluence.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;_3iDTPbvLZJ renderer-heading-wrapper&quot; data-testid=&quot;renderer-heading-wrapper&quot; data-level=&quot;2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;What-you-would-bring&quot; data-local-id=&quot;22b546661822&quot; data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2381&quot;&gt;What you would bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-local-id=&quot;22b546661822&quot; data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2381&quot;&gt;You have 3–5+ years of quota-carrying sales experience, with 3+ years of full-cycle closing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-local-id=&quot;22b546661822&quot; data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2381&quot;&gt;You have achieved 100%+ of quota in at least 2 consecutive years, proving sustained performance at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-local-id=&quot;22b546661822&quot; data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2381&quot;&gt;You have diagnosed and fixed market-level problems—not just closed deals, but rebuilt territories or built new motions from scratch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-local-id=&quot;22b546661822&quot; data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2381&quot;&gt;You know your numbers—ARR targets, attainment rates, deal progression, pipeline metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-local-id=&quot;22b546661822&quot; data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2381&quot;&gt;You can map your growth across roles: where you started, where you peaked, and why you moved on. You&#39;re ambitious about your own growth and you seek out bigger challenges and higher complexity. You move strategically to environments where there&#39;s genuine room to expand and where you can keep leveling up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-local-id=&quot;22b546661822&quot; data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2381&quot;&gt;You build scalable playbooks and mentor others—Sales Managers come to you for advice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-local-id=&quot;22b546661822&quot; data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2381&quot;&gt;You have a 2-3 year territory vision and can break it into actionable strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-local-id=&quot;22b546661822&quot; data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2381&quot;&gt;Track record of territory turnarounds or market expansion from zero&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-local-id=&quot;22b546661822&quot; data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2381&quot;&gt;You understand what drives you. You tie compensation to personal earnings ambitions and growth opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-local-id=&quot;22b546661822&quot; data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2381&quot;&gt;AI Fluency Level 3 or equivalent: you&#39;ve redesigned how work gets done using AI, built approaches others follow, and actively question AI output&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;UK&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;£52,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;£65,000 GBP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency at Mews&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salary ranges are provided in good faith and reflect current market conditions and internal pay structures. Final compensation may be adjusted based on funding, budget constraints, or exceptional candidate qualifications, but will remain within reasonable proximity to the stated range.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This salary disclosure is provided in compliance with applicable pay transparency legislation. We are committed to equal pay practices and prohibit salary history inquiries during our recruitment process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If the location you&#39;re applying from wasn&#39;t originally advertised for this role, salary range information is available upon request at any point during the application/interview process - your recruiter will be able to help.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What’s in it for you?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our success is powered by our incredible people, supported by benefits that help them thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;No matter where you’re based, you’ll enjoy:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unlimited paid holiday (yes, really)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participation in our company share program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid parental leave (6 months fully paid for primary caregivers, 2 months for secondary, available after one year of service)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An annual Learning budget of €300 (and more for high performers) to support your development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly &quot;EDGE&quot; time to Explore, Develop, Grow, and Elevate yourself&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A work from anywhere policy with flexibility to work abroad for a few weeks each year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relocation options, available after one year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible, hybrid working options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A home office setup budget to make your workspace your own and a monthly work-from-home allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Claude tokens, so you can automate workflows and build smarter, more efficient ways of working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Local benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll receive additional benefits that vary by location, from healthcare and retirement plans to team events, socials and other perks. Ask us about it during your interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Life at Mews&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re an equal opportunities employer. We value teams that reflect the diversity of the customers and communities we serve. Different perspectives make better ideas, stronger products and a more welcoming company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We also believe transparency is important when deciding if you&#39;re the right fit. Mews is an ambitious, high-pressure environment of continuous learning and high standards. Success here requires resilience, adaptability and a willingness to solve difficult problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A few things that define how we work:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High autonomy means high responsibility. People are expected to take ownership and drive outcomes. There isn’t a detailed playbook for everything, and that’s part of what makes the work challenging – and rewarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Change is constant. We’re growing quickly and adapting as we scale. Teams, processes and priorities continue to evolve, and only people who stay curious and agile will thrive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We’re remote-first, not relationship-free. Flexibility is core to how we work, but strong relationships still matter. Our teams are global, so we need expert collaborators and communicators to help us move forward together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI is an integral part of our processes. It’s not here to steal people’s jobs, but to amplify efficiency and productivity. We’re motivated to proactively use the technology to seek out better ways of working and share our findings with the rest of the company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If there&#39;s anything we can do to support you during the application process, let us know.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We don&#39;t discriminate on the basis of race, religion, colour, nationality, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, disability or any other protected characteristic.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;One final thing: don&#39;t hold back. If you don&#39;t meet 100% of the criteria in this job description but you&#39;re certain you could make a big impact, apply. Everyone should have equal access to opportunities, and we&#39;re committed to providing an inclusive experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If Mews sounds like the kind of environment where you&#39;d thrive, we&#39;d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/mewssystems/senior-account-executive-uki-419611","tags":["Commercial"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1792443313},{"slug":"computational-chemist-gn-at-chemistry-ai-venture-london-148656","company_name":"atlantic.vc","title":"Computational Chemist (gn) @ Chemistry AI Venture, London","description":"<p><em>This an Atlantic portfolio venture. <br></em></p><p><strong>About the Venture</strong></p><p>This early-stage venture is building a discovery engine for chemistry, comprising a platform for running end-to-end simulations of chemical reaction systems, and a world model + agent stack that uses the simulation platform to discover new chemistry.</p><p>Their goal is to build backend scientific data infrastructure to meet the demands of AI systems that can truly accelerate and automate the discovery layer of chemistry.<br><br>Both founders hold PhDs in Chemistry from the University of Oxford, and the venture has already secured pre-seed funding. They are now building out their founding team.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>The Role</strong></p><ul><li><p>As a Computational Chemist, you will play a central role in shaping the scientific foundations of the venture's technology, helping develop the computational methods and workflows that underpin its end-to-end chemical reaction simulation platform.</p></li><li><p>You’ll work closely with researchers and engineers to integrate state-of-the-art computational chemistry methods with machine learning approaches, driving progress towards the venture's strategic and scientific objectives.</p></li><li><p>You’ll take ownership of developing, validating and optimising the computational chemistry components of the platform, with a particular focus on reaction mechanisms, reaction kinetics, molecular dynamics and the modelling of complex chemical environments.</p></li><li><p>You will design, implement and refine scalable scientific workflows for generating, processing and analysing chemical reaction data, improving the accuracy, reliability and computational efficiency of simulations.</p></li><li><p>Beyond your core scientific responsibilities, the team is looking for someone who can contribute to strategic research decisions, bring strong independent scientific judgement, and help shape the interdisciplinary research culture of the company at an early stage.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>What You'll Work On</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Foundation models for chemical reactivity:</strong> The team is building and training foundation models for chemical reactivity with a variety of data modalities. You'll help curate this foundational data corpus by developing cheminformatics and computational chemistry workflows for generating data from combinatorial enumeration, as well as robust data filtering, clustering and validation routines.</p></li><li><p><strong>Computational methods:</strong> The team is working on efficient computational methods from which foundational data is generated and the platform is validated. You'll be responsible for developing protocols for estimating solvation and entropy factors in chemical reaction steps. This involves keeping up to date with published literature for ideas and inspiration.</p></li><li><p><strong>Generative models:</strong> The venture is expanding its foundational data corpus beyond combinatorial workflows. You'll help design, validate and benchmark the generative model architectures that accomplish this.</p></li><li><p><strong>Chemical reaction simulation:</strong> The team is building out an end-to-end chemical reaction simulation platform. You'll be involved in designing the architecture and assembling the platform, as well as developing benchmarks and validation protocols against computational and experimental methods.</p></li><li><p><strong>World models and agents:</strong> The venture will be developing an agent + world model stack that operates on the simulation platform. You'll be responsible for formulating the action space in which the world model is trained and the agent explores new chemical reaction space.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p><strong>What They're Looking For</strong></p><p>The team is looking for someone who enjoys being given a blank canvas and the chance to create something spectacular with it. In particular, someone who brings:</p><ul class="ul1"><li><p>A PhD in Computational Chemistry, Machine Learning, or a related field.</p></li><li><p>Intellectual curiosity: Someone who enjoys venturing outside their comfort zone, exploring new ideas and applying their knowledge and experience to unfamiliar domains.</p></li><li><p>An entrepreneurial mindset: Someone who thrives in an early-stage environment, enjoys building things from scratch and is excited to grow beyond the traditional boundaries of their role.</p></li><li><p>Independent thinking and scientific judgement: Someone who can take ownership of complex challenges, contribute new ideas and help shape the scientific direction of the venture.</p></li><li><p>A collaborative approach: Someone who can build strong relationships across the team and actively contribute to shaping and nurturing the company culture as it grows.</p></li><li><p>An instinct for building great working environments: Someone who understands the importance of the right tools, systems and ways of working to help themselves and the wider team do their best work.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/atlanticvc/computational-chemist-gn-at-chemistry-ai-venture-london-148656","tags":["Portfolio Company"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"London, England, United Kingdom","created_at":1792443087},{"slug":"uk-managing-director-london-144323","company_name":"Se3","title":"UK Managing Director","description":"<h2><strong>Join SE3 Labs as UK Managing Director</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build SE3 in the UK from the ground up, and turn trusted relationships with UK defence customers into trials and contracts.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About SE3</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">SE3 Labs builds spatial intelligence and autonomy software for unmanned systems. We combine 3D computer vision, state estimation and AI to help autonomous platforms perceive their surroundings, know where they are and operate when GPS and other sensors become unreliable. Defence is a core application of our work today.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are growing to a team of 100+ people. Join at a stage where you can shape our <strong>UK team</strong>, being our 1st hire in the UK and building the team and being a pivotal figure of SE3's international growth.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As UK Managing Director, you'll build and lead SE3's UK operation, reporting directly to our CEO. You'll develop government customers and partnerships, hire a small local team and work closely with our engineering team in Germany to bring SE3's technology to UK customers. You'll take responsibility for the UK business and shape it as it grows.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What You'll Work On</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>UK Operation:</strong> Build and lead SE3's UK operation and take responsibility for its results.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Customers &amp; Partnerships:</strong> Develop UK government customers and partners, and build long-term trust with them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Trials to Contracts:</strong> Turn relationships and opportunities into trials and contracts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Local Team:</strong> Hire and lead a small UK team, including field engineers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Engineering Link:</strong> Work closely with our engineering team in Germany to bring SE3's technology to UK customers.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Your Profile</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You take ownership of outcomes and remove obstacles without waiting for direction. You turn discussions into clear decisions and decisions into deliverables, and you hold yourself and your team to a consistently high standard.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You know the UK defence market and have relevant customer and procurement relationships.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You bring relevant commercial and industry experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can recruit and lead a small team and operate independently.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're comfortable with the pace, uncertainty and responsibility of an early-stage company.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You speak fluent English and are based in the UK. Given the nature of SE3's work in the defence sector, candidates must be eligible to work on defence-related projects and, where required, obtain the relevant security clearance.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Especially Valued Bonus Skills</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A military career followed by industry or startup experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with UK defence procurement and innovation programmes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with autonomous systems or UAVs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">German language skills.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Perks &amp; Benefits</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Real Ownership:</strong> Participate in SE3's growth through our employee participation programme</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work Environment to Excel at:</strong> Find a high-quality and modern toolset, flat hierarchy and a skilled, driven team which will push the limits together with you</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI-boosted workplace:</strong> We empower every employee with best-in-class AI tools and agents, giving you unlimited access to the latest advancements and a true productivity edge</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team Offsites:</strong> We go on 2 company retreats per year, our last ones were in Italy and Greece</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Our Process</strong></h2><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Intro Call (30 min):</strong> Let's get to know each other.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Case Study (90 min):</strong> We work through a realistic UK market or partnership scenario together.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Leadership Interview (1 hr):</strong> We dive into your UK defence relationships, the deals you have closed and how you build a team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team Dinner / Lunch:</strong> Meet the team and see whether it is a strong fit on both sides.</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Equal Opportunity</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">SE3 is an equal-opportunity employer committed to building a diverse and inclusive team. All qualified candidates will be considered for employment without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, or any other characteristic protected under applicable law.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/se3/uk-managing-director-london-144323","tags":["CEO Office"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"United Kingdom","created_at":1792442417},{"slug":"account-executive-healthcare-communications-london-459981","company_name":"Hanover","title":"Account Executive | Healthcare Communications | London","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hanover is an award-winning communications consultancy that advises enterprises, institutions, and individuals on building recognition and enhancing reputation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;From our offices across Europe and the Middle East, we adopt an integrated approach that connects the dots across channels, audiences and issues.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our collective of smart, curious people think differently and live by a shared mission, purpose, vision, and values. These shape how we work, not just with our colleagues, but with clients and partners too.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to ‘rewire communications for impact’ and harness its transformative power to advocate, trailblaze and make a difference.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We do this by igniting and empowering the potential of every individual within our company, recognising that each person is a unique spark, capable of creating extraordinary impact. We believe that by nurturing and harnessing the collective brilliance of our people, we can drive innovation, foster an uncommon work culture, and make a positive difference to society.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Embracing the complete range of skills and services across the communications spectrum without constraint, we create the best outcomes for our clients and deliver world-class work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly motivated and skilled Account Executive to join our Healthcare Communications team, joining a team of experts in product PR, patient advocacy, crisis management, disease awareness, corporate communications and media relations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Account Executive provides high-quality public relations services to Hanover’s existing healthcare clients, together with timely research and administrative support for new business activity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Account Executive is also responsible for supporting media outreach, providing administrative support for client meetings, and establishing demonstrably credible working relationships with clients, where appropriate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Primary Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay abreast of the media, with the goal of identifying opportunities for coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft high quality materials for client review&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain relevant records of target stakeholder and audience groups relevant to your clients and sectors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver specifically assigned areas of each discrete/new project to agreed timescales, on budget and to a high quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct value-add research and produce high quality draft intelligence reports for existing clients and sector specific new business meetings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft client meeting agendas and effective action notes arising from internal account meetings and sector specific new business meetings, together with efficient maintenance of new business databases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute towards selected new business pitches as part of the wider team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in a relevant PR and communications position from either a public relations consultancy or in-house communications team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good knowledge and understanding of healthcare communications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communications skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and highly organised&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective time management and strong organisational skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience of working collaboratively as part of a team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable interest in media, news and current affairs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to a competitive salary, your core benefits package will include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus potential linked to recruitment, new business and long service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days’ annual leave (plus bank holidays)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private healthcare and dental insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A company pension plan, including 5% employer contribution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll also have access to a wide range of opportunities and initiatives, including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working policies, plus eligibility to apply for a sabbatical after 2 years’ service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Summer Fridays finish (3pm) – early Friday finish the rest of the year (4pm)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The Hanover Academy, which incorporates training, coaching, mentoring and reverse-mentoring opportunities to support personal development and career progression across all levels, with a generous training budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;International secondments as well as the opportunity to collaborate with all offices across the AVENIR GLOBAL’s network&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A wellbeing programme, featuring (but not limited to) pre- and post-maternity leave coaching, a working parents’ group, subsidised gym membership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our Culture Club, with a robust social calendar all year round and CSR activity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diversity, Equity and Inclusion Statement +&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hanover Communications is an equal opportunities employer, committed to creating and ensuring a fair, inclusive, and diverse work environment where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity. We believe that equality and diversity are essential to high performance and a thriving culture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We maintain a strict no-tolerance stance against any form of discrimination and harassment, ensuring all individuals are treated equitably, irrespective of their race, ethnicity, religion, beliefs, age, sex, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, marital or pregnancy status, genetic background, or any other attribute safeguarded under our company policies or federal, state or local laws and legislation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We want to ensure that our hiring process is accessible. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application process, please send an email to &lt;a ---------- with the nature of your request.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are committed to transparency about how we collect and use your data, including ensuring we comply with legal obligations relating to data protection. You can view our data privacy policy&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://hanovercomms.com/recruitment-privacy-policy&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hanover is part of AVENIR GLOBAL’s powerhouse of specialist communications consultancies across EMEA and North America. Collectively we rank among the top 15 largest communication firms in the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Find out more about &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hanovercomms.com/about-us/&quot;&gt;Hanover&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hanovercomms.com/careers/&quot;&gt;working for us&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/hanover/account-executive-healthcare-communications-london-459981","tags":["Hanover"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1792432522},{"slug":"senior-field-account-executive-belfast-404036","company_name":"Lightspeedhq","title":"Senior Field Account Executive","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Hi there! Thanks for stopping by 👋</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are you actively looking for a new opportunity? Or just checking the market? Well… you might just be in the right place!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lightspeed is looking for a motivated <strong>Senior Field Account Executive</strong> to join our founding Northern Irish Hospitality team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Based in Belfast, you’ll be responsible for building strong relationships across Northern Ireland, supporting hospitality businesses in finding the right solutions, and guiding them through their entire journey with Lightspeed - delivering the full value of the Lightspeed ecosystem, ensuring our partners achieve sustainable growth from the initial discovery through to long-term advocacy.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>What you will be doing:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and maintain an advanced understanding of the Belfast and wider Northern Irish hospitality landscape to spot proactively trends and opportunities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leverage market research and insights to shape effective territory sales plans.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage a mixture of complex and high-velocity sales cycles from discovery and solution design through sophisticated contract negotiations and high-touch implementation handovers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Consistently outperform monthly MRR targets by applying an entrepreneurial mindset to territory management, focusing on high-LTV (Long Term Value) accounts and portfolio expansion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Guide clients from needs analysis and solution design through proposals, contract agreements, and seamless onboarding.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver high-impact presentations and live demonstrations that translate Lightspeed’s technical capabilities into clear business outcomes for owners and operators.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain a rigorous, high-integrity Salesforce pipeline; managing your own workload and updating the team accordingly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Spearhead outbound initiatives and represent the brand at premier industry events to cultivate a high-quality pipeline and build long-term leads.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you need to bring:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ years of high-performance experience in Field or Outbound sales, with a track record of navigating complex, solution-based sales within the technology, SaaS, or hospitality ecosystems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A deep understanding of the hospitality industry, including key segments and operational considerations is ideal</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advanced in sales development best practice - building pipelines, territory planning, and driving new business with strong organisational ability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated success in consistently exceeding aggressive MRR targets and significantly contributing to regional market-share expansion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficient in using Salesforce or similar CRM systems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A self-starting, agile mindset with the ability to operate autonomously in a high-growth, fast-paced environment.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What's in it for you?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Come live the Lightspeed Experience…</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Genuine career growth opportunities based on performance within a company that's continuously expanding</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with highly skilled people who are as passionate about sales &amp; marketing  as you are</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An environment that encourages initiatives and leadership</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work in a team big enough for growth but lean enough to make a real impact</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fun activities with your teammates &amp; social events throughout the year</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Opportunity to learn, expand your skill set, forge wonderful relationships and make your mark within the diverse and inclusive Lightspeed culture, a true Canadian tech success story</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">… and enjoy a range of benefits that’ll keep you happy and healthy:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lightspeed equity scheme (we are all owners)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible Paid Time Off - providing you the freedom to take time off however you like</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Private Medical Insurance and cash health plan for optical, dental and more.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Health &amp; Wellness Credit- expense up to 400 GBP per year towards your gym membership, yoga classes, a new bike or whatever else you do for your health </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mental Health Support through the LifeWorks and Modern Health Apps- whether it is meditation, coaching or counseling you need - each employee gets access to this platform </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Time off to volunteer and give back to your community</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Transit / parking benefit - for when you need to travel to the Belfast office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A variety of drinks &amp; snacks in our offices in London </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>To all recruitment agencies: Lightspeed does not accept unsolicited agency resumes. If we have not directly engaged your company in writing to supply candidates for a specific vacancy, Lightspeed will not be responsible for any fees related to unsolicited resumes.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Lightspeed is a proud equal opportunity employer and we are committed to creating an inclusive and barrier-free workplace. Lightspeed welcomes and encourages applications from people with disabilities. Accommodations are available on request for candidates taking part in all aspects of the selection process.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Where to from here?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Obviously, this has to be mutually beneficial: we want you to step into a role you love, and we want to offer you a place you’re proud to come to every day. For a glimpse into our world check out our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.lightspeedhq.com/careers/">career page here</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lightspeed is building communities through commerce, and we need people from all backgrounds and lived experiences to do that. We were founded in 2005, in Montreal’s gay village and our original members were all part of the LGBTQ+ community. The ethos of our business has been about inclusion from the very beginning, and we strive to provide a workplace where everyone belongs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Who we are:</strong> </h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Powering the businesses that are the backbone of the global economy, Lightspeed's one-stop commerce platform helps merchants innovate to simplify, scale, and provide exceptional customer experiences. Our cloud commerce solution transforms and unifies online and physical operations, multichannel sales, expansion to new locations, global payments, financial solutions, and connection to supplier networks.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in Montréal, Canada in 2005, Lightspeed is dual-listed on the New York Stock Exchange (NYSE: LSPD) and Toronto Stock Exchange (TSX: LSPD). With teams across North America, Europe, and Asia Pacific, the company serves retail, hospitality, and golf businesses in over 100 countries.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lightspeed handles your information in accordance with our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="c-link" href="https://www.lightspeedhq.com/legal/applicant-privacy-statement/">Applicant Privacy Statement</a>.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/lightspeedhq/senior-field-account-executive-belfast-404036","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Belfast","created_at":1792431619},{"slug":"account-executive-london-29480","company_name":"Light Inc","title":"Account Executive","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Retire the ERP.<br /></strong><br />Light exists to replace factory-era ERPs with software that feels alive. Our Smart Financial Platform gives modern, global companies superpowers—automated accounting, real-time reporting, and financial flows that move at the speed of the business.<br /><br />We build with our customers, ship fast, and obsess over craft. In a short time, Light has gone from idea to the operating core for leading companies like Lovable, Legora, and Keyshot. People don’t just use Light—they enjoy it.<br /><br />We’re an early team defining a new software category. Think engineers who love debits and credits, designers who care about reconciliation states, and operators who treat finance as a product. If you’re excited to modernize how the world runs money—one workflow at a time—you’re in the right place.<br /><br />Backed by world-class investors and advised by industry titans, we’re building category-defining products with the freedom to ship ambitiously and own outcomes.<br />Come help us make Light the global default for next-gen finance.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Account Executive role:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leading sales cycles for Light as an SFP, managing deals from $30K to $200K+ and consistently hitting revenue targets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Building relationships with C-suite executives and key decision makers, understanding their business needs and showing how our SFP solution helps.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Creating account plans and working closely with technical teams to develop solutions for target industries like asset-light, multinational companies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Running effective customer meetings and negotiations, handling complex deals from first contact through contract signing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Owning the AE to BDR relationship to generate pipeline as a team.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><br />How you fit into the team:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your main mission is to help prospective customers see the light. Aside from being based in-office in London or New York, this role requires you to be hungry, have an understanding of finance tools and knowledge of sales. We have a clear ICP defined with a leadlist.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a GTM role with the responsibility of sales and closing pipeline. You'll work with a small and stellar team with a deep understanding of the market who has done this before.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><br />Your qualifications:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3-6 years of closing experience and acing pipeline - preferably within ERPs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Your Personality</em>: Your exceptional interpersonal skills, energy and sense of ownership make you stand out.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Thriving in a Fast-Paced Environment: </em>You thrive in a fast-paced, high-growth, and rapidly changing environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Attention to Detail: </em>Your attention to detail, outstanding communication skills (phone, listening, and writing), set you up for success.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Self-Driven:</em> Self-driven and ambitious, you have the desire to grow with Light.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Entrepreneurial Spirit: </em>Your entrepreneurial spirit and experience with a strong growth mindset align perfectly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Comfort in Quota-Carrying Environment:</em> You are ambitious, self-motivated, and comfortable working in a quota-carrying environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical experience using AI or emerging technology tools to improve productivity, insight, or decision-making, with the ability to apply first-principles thinking to new problems.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><br />Bonus points:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're CPA and have a few years of experience within Big4, accounting or the CFO suite.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sales Tools Familiarity: You have prior experience using Sales Automation/Prospecting Tools (e.g., Amplemarket, Salesloft, Outreach) and CRM (Hubspot).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Startup Experience: You've worked at a fast-growing startup.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cold Calling Pro: You ace cold calling and relationship building. Wanna really get on our radar? Find our number, call and pitch us.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><br />A few tips to stand out</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Show us who you are through your application and don't limit yourself to a resume. Try not to be generic.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have numbers to show so you can measure impact? Even better!</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Most people can say they wanna work in a startup, but why this one? What are your expectations and what do you specifically wanna learn from us?</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><br />The good stuff</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In addition to being part of a great team and working in a really fun and innovative environment, we offer:<br />💸 A competitive salary + potential stock options<br />🏝 25 days of annual leave + public holidays in the country where you are based.<br />🥳 Regular socials and company off-sites<br />🚀 A huge opportunity for career growth as you'll help shape a market-defining product.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><br />The famous last words</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working at Light means you're embarking on an exciting journey to reshape the future of multinational financial operations. Our cheat-code is that we've built something like this before - and are now doing it again, only better. Our goal is to make global finance effortless and empower companies to make informed decisions.<br /><br />🚀 Join the rocket ship while it's taking off 🚀</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/light-inc/account-executive-london-29480","tags":["GTM"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792431617},{"slug":"staff-software-engineer-data-enrichment-platform-london-united-kingdom-26859","company_name":"Wayve","title":"Staff Software Engineer, Data Enrichment Platform","description":"<div><div style="left:0px;width:100%;height:0px;position:relative;padding-bottom:56.25%"><iframe src="https://embedded-media.ashbyhq.com/embed/c3dedbb7-82c2-4668-a1bf-b53c8f870af0/8c1bb54c-6e60-48b5-8dbb-5631ddd06204" style="top:0px;left:0px;width:100%;height:100%;position:absolute;border:0px" allowfullscreen="true" scrolling="no" allow="encrypted-media *; picture-in-picture *;" sandbox="allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-presentation"></iframe></div></div><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Before the detail, here's the challenge you'd help us solve.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We build the embodied intelligence that moves real vehicles safely, and the ecosystem a billion machines will run on in the future. Very few people in AI can say this. Every role here, whatever the team, plugs into that.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Here’s what this particular role covers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🛠️ About our Data Enrichment Platform Team</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our Enrichment Orchestration team builds the platform that enables Wayve’s teams to deploy, run, evaluate and continually improve machine-learning models. Processing petabytes of driving data across large GPU fleets, the team creates dependable, self-service capabilities that help model engineers understand model performance, improve quality and reduce operational effort and cost.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As our Staff Software Engineer, you’ll own the platform’s technical vision and long-term direction. You’ll combine hands-on engineering with cross-team technical leadership, shaping how model engineering, infrastructure, compute and data capabilities come together to accelerate model development.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🧠 Your day-to-day</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the technical vision and architecture for the end-to-end Data Enrichment Platform, translating user needs into a clear technical direction.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead the design, development and operation of backend services, APIs, model-execution workflows, versioned outputs, annotation capabilities and dataset catalogues.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make architectural decisions for petabyte-scale data and large GPU fleets, addressing data locality, scheduling, capacity, backpressure, failure recovery, observability and cost.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Evaluate when to build, buy, reuse, integrate, consolidate or replace technologies as Wayve’s needs and the technology landscape evolve.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish clear technical boundaries and ownership across model engineering, AI Platform, infrastructure, compute, storage and data teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Remain hands-on while leading cross-team delivery, mentoring senior engineers and raising standards for maintainable, tested and observable software.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive adoption of reusable, self-service capabilities so teams can onboard and operate workflows independently.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define measurable service levels and success metrics covering reliability, throughput, cost, automation and adoption.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🧩 What you’ll be working on</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A scalable platform for large-scale inference, automated evaluation, model monitoring, active learning and retraining.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Self-service backend services and APIs that enable dozens of model engineers to deploy and operate repeatable workflows independently.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reproducible dataset selection, versioned outputs, annotation workflows and dataset catalogues with clear metadata, provenance and lineage.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reliable model-execution workflows operating across petabytes of driving data and large GPU fleets, scaling towards thousands of GPUs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitoring and operational tooling that make model quality, platform reliability, throughput, cost, runtime and workflow status visible.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The foundations for continuous evaluation, drift detection and automated model-improvement loops across robotics and computer-vision workloads.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Architectural improvements that reduce inference costs, duplicate compute and manual operational effort.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🙌 You should apply if</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have owned the long-term technical direction of a complex, multi-system platform or capability and can demonstrate the measurable outcomes of your decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have strong production software-engineering experience in Python, building maintainable, tested and observable backend services, APIs and data-processing systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have deep experience designing and operating large-scale distributed systems for data-intensive or compute-intensive workloads.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have a track record of turning internal platforms into widely adopted, reliable and usable self-service products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You bring excellent architecture and technology judgement, balancing immediate delivery needs with long-term platform direction.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You remain hands-on while leading delivery across organisational boundaries, influencing technical decisions and aligning teams around clear ownership and shared outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You communicate complex ideas clearly and have experience mentoring senior engineers and strengthening the technical capabilities of those around you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with workflow orchestration, batch inference, ML platforms, model deployment or registries would be an advantage. Relevant technologies include Flyte, Airflow, Dagster, Argo, Spark, Databricks, Ray, Kubernetes and GPU infrastructure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with annotation or dataset-catalogue platforms, including provenance, versioning, lineage and quality control, would also be valuable.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with production robotics or computer-vision platforms—including annotation, inference, evaluation and model monitoring—is particularly desirable. Computer-vision research expertise is not required.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🌱 <strong>Not ticking every box? That’s totally okay!</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you’re passionate about autonomy and the impact you could make at Wayve, we encourage you to apply even if you don’t meet every requirement.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>More about Wayve</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🚀 Wayve is building the leading AI platform for autonomous driving. We are pioneering an end-to-end AI approach that enables vehicles to learn directly from real-world experience, developing the ability to adapt, generalise and improve at scale. Instead of relying on hand-coded rules or pre-mapped environments, our AI Driver learns to drive by understanding the world around it. The result is technology that navigates complex urban environments with intelligence, precision and natural flow, unlocking meaningful advances in both safety and efficiency. We believe autonomy represents a once-in-a-generation transformation in how people and goods move, comparable to the shift from horses to cars, and from human-driven vehicles to intelligent machines.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our ambition is to make autonomy universal. Wayve’s mapless and hardware-agnostic AI platform integrates with global OEM partners, enabling continuous software evolution and unlocking advanced levels of automation from L2+ through to L4 as our core AI model scales. In a race increasingly defined by intelligence and real-world learning, Wayve is taking a distinct approach, building a generalisable driving intelligence that can power any vehicle, anywhere. By combining embodied AI with scalable deployment, we are creating technology that can be shaped to each OEM brand and driver experience, accelerating the transition to a safer, more intelligent future of mobility.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How we work 💻 — Locations &amp; Flexible Working</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is based in London. Our main hubs are in London, Sunnyvale, Yokohama, Herzliya, Vancouver and Leonberg. We operate a hybrid working model that combines in-person collaboration in our dedicated office spaces with focused time working remotely. This gives our teams the connection and energy of working together, alongside the flexibility to do their best work in a way that fits their lives.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🔍 The Interview Process</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our process is clear and respectful of your time.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Initial call / Talent Partner screen</strong> (30 mins)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competency interviews:</strong> Python coding (60 mins), System design (60 mins)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Deep Dive Interviews:</strong> Technical Leadership, Hiring Manager interview (45 mins)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Final interview:</strong> Mission, values and Staff-level calibration (45 mins)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’ll always explain the format and work around your availability.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What’s in it for you (location dependent)</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">💰 Salaries benchmarked against the market annually</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">📈 Meaningful equity, sharing in the ownership and long-term success of Wayve</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">✈️ Relocation support and visa sponsorship where applicable</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">✅ Hybrid working, core hours and the chance to work hands-on in vehicle workshops and labs</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">📚 Learning and development budgets with support for training, conferences and growth</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🩺 Comprehensive benefits including health insurance, dental, enhanced maternity and paternity leave, retirement or pension where applicable, access to therapists, wellbeing partnerships, team socials and more</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">A quick, honest note before you apply.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Wayve is not a mature, fully-structured place with the playbook already written. Much of how we work is still being written, and if you join, you’ll help write it. That suits people who want real ownership more than people who need a settled structure from day one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If that sounds like the kind of problem you want to spend your time on, we’d really like to hear from you.<br /><br />At Wayve we're committed to creating a diverse, fair and respectful culture that is inclusive of everyone based on their unique skills and perspectives, and regardless of sex, race, religion or belief, ethnic or national origin, disability, age, citizenship, marital, domestic or civil partnership status, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status, pregnancy or related condition (including breastfeeding) or any other basis as protected by applicable law.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For more information visit <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://wayve.ai/careers/">Careers at Wayve.</a> To learn more about what drives us, visit <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://wayve.ai/careers/">Values at Wayve</a><br /><br />DISCLAIMER: We will not ask about marriage or pregnancy, care responsibilities or disabilities in any of our job adverts or interviews. However, we do look to capture information about care responsibilities, and disabilities among other diversity information as part of an optional DEI Monitoring form to help us identify areas of improvement in our hiring process and ensure that the process is inclusive and non-discriminatory.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/wayve/staff-software-engineer-data-enrichment-platform-london-united-kingdom-26859","tags":["Simulation","Evaluation","Validation"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London, United Kingdom","created_at":1792431617},{"slug":"senior-data-remediation-project-manager-london-259943","company_name":"Delta Capita","title":"Senior Data Remediation Project Manager","description":"<p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Role - Senior Data Remediation Project Manager</span></strong></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Location - London (Hybrid)</span></strong></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Employment Type - 6 months FTC</span></strong></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Joining - Immediate</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">About the Role:</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#121317">Delta Capita is seeking an experienced Senior Data Remediation Project Manager to lead a high-profile regulatory and customer remediation programme within the financial services sector. The successful candidate will be responsible for driving complex data remediation initiatives, coordinating multiple delivery workstreams, and ensuring the successful execution of large-scale remediation activities impacting customer data, operational processes, and technology landscapes.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#121317">This is a highly visible role requiring exceptional stakeholder management capabilities, strong programme governance experience, and a deep understanding of data, technology, and regulatory remediation environments.</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Key Responsibilities:</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Lead the delivery of a large-scale data remediation programme within a regulated financial services environment.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Consolidate multiple data-related workstream plans into a single integrated delivery roadmap, ensuring clear dependencies, milestones, risks, and governance are maintained.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Drive execution across business, data, technology, operations, and change teams to ensure delivery objectives are met.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Engage and influence senior stakeholders, including Executive leadership, Programme Sponsors, Risk, Compliance, Technology, and Operations teams.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Assess and manage data remediation impacts across systems, data architecture, operating models, controls, and manual processes.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Provide strong programme governance, tracking delivery progress, risks, issues, and remediation plans.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Identify opportunities to leverage AI and emerging technologies to improve remediation effectiveness, customer outcomes, and operational efficiency.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Collaborate with technical teams to understand data lineage, data quality issues, system dependencies, and remediation approaches.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Ensure remediation activities are aligned with regulatory expectations, governance standards, and customer outcome requirements.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Support decision-making through robust reporting, stakeholder communications, and programme documentation.<br><br></span></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Required Experience:</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Proven experience leading large-scale data remediation or regulatory remediation programmes within financial services.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Strong project or programme management background with experience delivering complex, multi-workstream initiatives.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Demonstrated ability to manage senior stakeholders and operate effectively within highly visible and regulated environments.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Strong understanding of data remediation methodologies, data quality management, and data governance principles.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Experience working across business, technology, data, and operational teams.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Good understanding of technology architecture, system landscapes, data flows, and remediation impacts.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Ability to build and manage integrated delivery plans across multiple parallel workstreams.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Experience managing programme risks, dependencies, governance forums, and regulatory scrutiny.</span></p> <br> <p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Desirable Experience:</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Experience delivering customer remediation programmes within banking, lending, or retail financial services organisations.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Knowledge of regulatory remediation, customer data management, conduct risk, or operational risk frameworks.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Experience working on large-scale customer contact and claims remediation programmes, including PPI, complaints remediation, redress, or similar customer outcome initiatives.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Understanding of AI use cases, automation opportunities, and advanced analytics within remediation and operational environments.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Exposure to data lineage, data governance, and enterprise data management programmes.<br><br></span></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Key Skills:</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Data Remediation</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Regulatory Remediation</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Programme &amp; Project Management</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Senior Stakeholder Management</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Data Governance &amp; Data Quality</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Delivery Planning &amp; Execution</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Risk &amp; Issue Management</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Financial Services Transformation</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• AI &amp; Innovation</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Technology &amp; Data Architecture Awareness</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Customer Remediation Programmes</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Change Management<br><br></span></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Why Join Delta Capita?</span></strong></p><p><span st