pan></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#eeeff4">•&nbsp;&nbsp; Zet moderne tooling in: AI-personalisatie, marketing automation, tracking, testing, analytics.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#eeeff4">•&nbsp;&nbsp; Werk met leadership aan prioritering, rapportage en roadmap-invloed.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong><span style="color:#eeeff4">Waarom is deze rol interessant voor jou?</span></strong></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#eeeff4">Er is veel te doen en je krijgt veel vrijheid én verantwoordelijkheid. Je maakt diepe impact en je mening wordt serieus genomen. Jouw data inzichten en suggesties vormen de basis voor belangrijke beslissingen en keuze die Snelstart gaat maken in de toekomst. Je zit én aan de knoppen én je bepaalt mede de richting voor verdere groei van de organisatie o.a. mbt tot klantinzichten. Daarnaast kun je experimenteren, testen, AI inzetten, optimaliseren en nauw samenwerken met product, marketing automation, marketing director en het MT.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#eeeff4">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong><span style="color:#eeeff4">Wat biedt Snelstart</span></strong></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#eeeff4">•&nbsp;&nbsp; Brutosalaris €4.800 – €7.000 (40 u/pw), afhankelijk van ervaring.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#eeeff4">•&nbsp;&nbsp; 30 vakantiedagen (o.b.v. 40 uur), maandelijks vakantiegeld en pensioenbijdrage.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#eeeff4">•&nbsp;&nbsp; Hybride werken, modern benefits-pakket, laptop en ergonomische werkplek (zit-sta).</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#eeeff4">•&nbsp;&nbsp; Toegang tot sportschool met bedrijfskorting.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#eeeff4">•&nbsp;&nbsp; Cultuur die data, snelheid en creativiteit omarmt; ruimte en budget voor tooling/experimenten.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#eeeff4">•&nbsp;&nbsp; Directe invloed op product, strategie en roadmap; doorgroeimogelijkheden in een schaalbare omgeving.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#eeeff4">•&nbsp;&nbsp; Een betrokken team met 200+ collega’s.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong><span style="color:#eeeff4">Spreekt dit jou aan?</span></strong><span style="color:#0A0A0B">&nbsp; </span>Neem contact op met Sound People via Sven Fremeijer (<a rel="noopener" target="_blank" ---------- of via 0631932830</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Wat is de procedure?</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">Na een succesvolle telefonische kennismaking volgt een face to face gesprek met Sven Fremeijer. Als we beiden voldoende aanleiding zien om verder te gaan stelt Sound je voor bij SnelStart. Daar volgen 2 gesprekrondes.</p><p class="MsoNormal">De eerste gespreksronde wordt gezamenlijk gevoerd door de directeur commercie en product en HR. De tweede ronde zal plaatsvinden met de directeur commercie en product en een externe adviseur. Daarna volgt een arbeidsvoorwaarden gesprek.</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Slotopmerking</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">Deze functie is bedoeld voor een daadkrachtige verbinder die marketing discipline met pragmatisme combineert. Als jij de marketing van SnelStart wilt professionaliseren en de organisatie wilt helpen naar een voorspelbare, succesvolle ‘marketingmachine’, dan horen we graag van je!</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p class="MsoNormal"><strong><span style="color:#EEEFF4">Jouw profiel</span></strong></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#EEEFF4">Ervaring en competenties</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#EEEFF4">•&nbsp;&nbsp; Hbo werk- en denkniveau.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#EEEFF4">•&nbsp;&nbsp; 7+ jaar in growth/performance marketing of vergelijkbare data-gedreven SaaS-rol.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#EEEFF4">•&nbsp;&nbsp; Sterk in strategie én executie; van visie naar vandaag nog live experimenten.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#EEEFF4">•&nbsp;&nbsp; Analytisch: hypotheses, statistiek, funnel metrics, cohort analyses, CAC, LTV, incrementality.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#EEEFF4">•&nbsp;&nbsp; Ervaring met A/B-testing, experiment design, CRO en gedragspsychologie.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#EEEFF4">•&nbsp;&nbsp; Ervaren in samenwerking met Product, Design en Data; comfortabel in technisch productteam.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#EEEFF4">•&nbsp;&nbsp; Bekend met GA4, HubSpot, Mixpanel/Amplitude, Looker/Power BI, Segment/Stitch, AI-tooling.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#EEEFF4">•&nbsp;&nbsp; Creatief, schaal- en impactgericht, pragmatisch, eigenaarschap, hoog tempo.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#EEEFF4">•&nbsp;&nbsp; Kwaliteitsgericht in de breedste zin.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#EEEFF4">Motivatie; je optimaliseert wordt blij van groei. En wordt blij van resultaat en je vindt de marketing puzzel leuk en enthousiasmeert je collega’s voor jouw vak en de impact die je maakt.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="color:#EEEFF4">Persoonlijk: je gedreven en betrokken, oprecht en geeft je mening graag. Je deelt en geeft inzichten en werkt graag samen omdat het dan beter wordt. Je kan omgaan met feedback. &nbsp;Je neemt graag verantwoordelijkheid en neemt de regie voor jouw werk</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/sound-people-bv/succevol-ingevuld-senior-growth-marketeer-at-snelstart-amersfoort-344931","tags":[],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Amersfoort, Utrecht, Nederland","created_at":1792344676},{"slug":"senior-information-security-officer-amsterdam-478762","company_name":"Testendouble","title":"Senior Information Security Officer","description":"&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role in Our Story:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ACT is strengthening its data, technology and AI capabilities as we build a more integrated digital platform alongside our core environmental commodities trading and market-making business. This transformation is commercially driven, enabling us to scale, deepen client relationships and support increasingly complex and digital markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Senior Information Security Officer, you will own ACT’s enterprise information security strategy and governance at Group level, spanning our core operations, emerging digital businesses and client-facing technology platforms. You will define the security risk appetite, lead our response to an evolving threat landscape, and ensure security and resilience are embedded by design as our technology landscape develops.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working across business and technology leadership, you will translate commercial ambition into a pragmatic and scalable security posture that protects our systems and data while maintaining the trust of clients, counterparties and regulators. In essence, your role involves:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategy &amp;amp; Governance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Group-wide information security strategy and roadmap across ACT’s core market-making business and digital and client-facing platforms, aligned with business goals and industry frameworks such as ISO 27001 and NIST CSF. Define and maintain ACT’s cyber risk appetite.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and lead security governance, including policies, standards and control frameworks, with clear accountability across the Group. Report on security posture and material incidents to executive leadership and, where relevant, the Board.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client Platforms &amp;amp; Secure-by-Design&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embed security-by-design into new products and client platforms, partnering with Data, Architecture and Commercial teams to ensure emerging digital capabilities are secure from inception, while acting as a credible security voice to clients and counterparties.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee application, product and SaaS security, embedding security throughout the software development lifecycle for internal and client-facing platforms, and assessing third-party services handling ACT and counterparty data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Risk &amp;amp; Resilience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead enterprise security risk management, including risk assessments, vulnerability management and third-party/supply-chain risk, driving timely mitigation across core and digital environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct incident preparedness and response, coordinating detection, containment, eradication and recovery, while continuously strengthening incident and crisis-management plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Infrastructure &amp;amp; Emerging Technology&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Secure ACT’s cloud and infrastructure through Zero-Trust-aligned controls, including identity and access management, segmentation and encryption, across a hybrid and multi-platform environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Govern emerging technology and AI security, extending security oversight to AI and data platforms, including model and data-exposure risks and AI-enabled threats, as ACT expands its use of AI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance &amp;amp; Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure regulatory and compliance alignment, including GDPR, DORA and relevant sector obligations, advising the business on required adaptations and coordinating audits and certifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the security function and strengthen security culture across the Group, developing the team, raising security awareness, and acting as ACT’s primary authority and trusted advisor on cyber security to executives and business leaders, working alongside existing teams and capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;665&quot; data-end=&quot;786&quot; data-is-last-node=&quot;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To be successful in this role, we are looking for candidates with the following qualifications and attributes:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Bachelor’s degree in Information Security, Computer Science or a related field. A relevant Master’s degree is an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10–15 years of progressive experience in information security and cybersecurity, including at least 5 years in a senior security role, with ownership of enterprise security strategy, governance and risk management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Broad security leadership experience across incident response, cloud and infrastructure security, product/application security and regulatory compliance. Experience securing client-facing platforms or digital products is highly valuable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience within trading, financial services, commodities or another data-intensive and regulated environment is highly advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of security frameworks and standards, including ISO/IEC 27001, NIST Cybersecurity Framework and CIS Controls, with practical experience implementing them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding of data protection, regulatory and compliance requirements, including GDPR, DORA and standards such as SOC 2.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional certifications such as CISSP, CISM or CISA, or equivalent, are highly desirable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, communication and stakeholder-management skills, with the ability to translate complex security risks into clear business implications and advise technical teams, executives, business stakeholders and clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you meet these criteria and are ready to contribute your expertise to a dynamic and challenging environment, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/testendouble/senior-information-security-officer-amsterdam-478762","tags":["IT"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1792335329},{"slug":"senior-software-developer-c-net-data-analysis-tricht-219852","company_name":"Intero Integrity Services","title":"Senior software developer (C# / .NET, Data Analysis)","description":"<p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Senior software developer (C# / .NET, Data Analysis)</strong><br>Build the software that turns ultrasonic inspection data into safety-critical pipeline decisions worldwide, and lift the team around you.<br><br><strong>Location: </strong>Utrecht region (head office in Tricht, Gelderland)</p><p><br><strong>About Intero Integrity</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">Intero Integrity is an internationally operating specialist in the inspection, maintenance and emission monitoring of pipelines and industrial assets. We develop our inspection technology entirely in-house: from ultrasonic measurement systems and FPGA signal processing to the software our analysts use to interpret hundreds of kilometres of pipeline data.</p><p class="MsoNormal">The inspection results our software produces are used for safety-critical decisions about the integrity of pipelines and industrial installations such as heat exchangers. Reliability and correctness are therefore not a nice-to-have, but an absolute requirement.</p><p class="MsoNormal">We operate across Europe, North America and the Middle East. Our software products sit at the heart of that work: they are used every day by our data analysis organisation around the world. Whatever you build here has a direct, global impact.<br><br></p><p><strong>The opportunity</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">This is a role for a senior engineer who enjoys both sides of the craft: building excellent software, and helping people around you get better. You will work hands-on on the C#/.NET software behind our data analysis, turning large volumes of ultrasonic inspection data into reliable insights that our organisation uses worldwide.</p><p class="MsoNormal">What makes it attractive is the mix. You mentor and guide our internal developers, setting an example in how we design, review and test. At the same time you work side by side with our external development partners. Learning from them, challenging them and making sure the work meets a high bar. You'll grow as an engineer and as a mentor, often in the same week.</p><p class="MsoNormal">Because our data is used for safety-critical decisions, a strong sense of software quality runs through the role: it shapes how you design, how you review and where you set the standard for the team. If you value knowledge transfer and a healthy engineering culture as much as writing good code, you will feel at home here.</p><p><strong><br>What you will do</strong></p><p><strong>Hands-on software development</strong></p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; You design, build and maintain C# applications for the analysis and reporting of inspection data</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; You work with large volumes of ultrasonic signal data and binary data streams</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; You build web applications and REST APIs on the ASP.NET platform</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; You contribute to bringing machine learning / Human-in-the-Loop capabilities into the data analysis workflow</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; You work with cloud-native services, preferably on Azure</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; You contribute to test strategies at functional, integration and system level, with an eye for the safety-critical use of the software</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; You work closely with hardware engineers, test engineers and domain specialists (UT inspection)<br></p><p><strong>Mentorship &amp; working with partners</strong></p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; You mentor and coach our internal developers and help them grow their technical skills</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; You lead by example in code reviews, pairing and knowledge sharing</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; You work side by side with external development partners, challenging their choices and making sure the work meets a high standard</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; You help establish and document engineering standards: coding guidelines, review processes, testing strategies and release policy</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; You make sure design decisions and domain knowledge are documented and transferable, so the team can operate independently</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; You help shape a development culture where quality and continuous improvement are the norm</p><p><strong><br>What you bring</strong></p><p><strong>Technical expertise</strong></p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Extensive experience with C# and the .NET platform</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Solid knowledge of software architecture, design principles and design patterns</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Experience building web applications and REST APIs (ASP.NET)</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Experience writing maintainable, testable, high-quality software</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Experience with automated testing and CI/CD</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; The ability to mentor others and lift the level of a team</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Good communication skills and the ability to clearly substantiate technical choices</p><p><strong><br>A plus</strong></p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Experience with cloud development, preferably Azure</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Experience with machine learning and/or image recognition, and operationalising ML in production</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Affinity with signal processing, measurement data and data streams, preferably in an industrial or technical context</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Experience with WPF and complex desktop applications</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Experience in a domain where software quality and reliability have direct impact (industrial automation, medical software, measurement &amp; inspection or similar)<br></p><p><strong>When do we see you as a senior?</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">For us, seniority goes beyond years of experience or technical skill. We are looking for someone who understands that technical choices affect the product, the organisation and our customers, and who actively takes responsibility for that.</p><p class="MsoNormal">You:</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Form an independent view on architecture and technology</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Think critically about requirements, assumptions and existing ways of working</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Take responsibility for quality, also outside your own code, and recognise that in a safety-critical domain the bar is higher</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Consciously build team knowledge: you document, explain and help colleagues grow</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Are comfortable in an environment where not everything is fixed yet, and know how to bring structure to it</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Actively contribute to knowledge sharing and continuous improvement within the team</p><p><strong><br>What we offer</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">A senior role with real influence on our software products and how we build them, the chance to mentor and grow a team, and the variety of working alongside experienced external partners, in a domain where technology genuinely matters.</p><p><br><strong>Salary &amp; terms of employment</strong></p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Gross monthly salary between € 5.328,- and € 6.715,- based on a 40-hour week, depending on knowledge and experience</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Year-end bonus, dependent on company results</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 25 holiday days per year</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Hybrid working (3 days per week at the office in Tricht as standard) and flexible working hours</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Collective pension scheme, with Intero contributing 50% of the premium</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Laptop and phone provided</p><p><strong><br>Working environment</strong></p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Technically challenging problems at the intersection of software, hardware and data</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Collaboration with experienced specialists across a range of technical disciplines</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Free fruit at work, access to the Intero Gym, company fitness options and a bike leasing scheme</p><p class="MsoListParagraph">•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; An international, technically driven working environment with plenty of room for ownership and initiative</p><p><strong><br>Ready to build with us?</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">Do you want to write excellent software, help a team grow around you and work alongside strong external partners? Then we would like to meet you.<br></p><p class="MsoNormal">Send your application and CV or LinkedIn profile to <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" ---------- <br>Questions about this vacancy? Get in touch with our Corporate Recruiter Veroniek Smits at the same address.<br><br>Please note that for this role we do not work with recruitment agencies, and we're unable to accept unsolicited candidate submissions or related fees.</p><p class="MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/intero-integrity-services/senior-software-developer-c-net-data-analysis-tricht-219852","tags":["Competence Center"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Tricht, Gelderland, Netherlands","created_at":1792333901},{"slug":"remote-senior-integrity-engineer-tricht-72924","company_name":"Intero Integrity Services","title":"Senior Integrity Engineer","description":"<p><strong>Senior Integrity Engineer</strong></p><p><strong>Europe | Remote (hybrid near an Intero office) | 32-40 hours<br><br></strong></p><p><em>An inspection shows a client what is wrong. You show them what to do about it.<br><br></em></p><p>Are you the integrity engineer people turn to when the inspection data is in and a decision has to be made? Do you enjoy combining fracture mechanics, corrosion growth and sound engineering judgment into advice an operator can actually act on? Then we would like to meet you. We are growing our Integrity team and are looking for our first Senior Integrity Engineer based in Europe.<br><br></p><p><strong>About Intero</strong></p><p>Intero Integrity Services helps pipeline operators and industrial companies keep their assets safe, compliant and running. With our own in-line inspection technology (including MFL and UT) we inspect pipelines and installations all over the world and tell clients exactly what condition their assets are in. Headquartered in Tricht, the Netherlands, we have over 40 years of experience and 650+ professionals from 25+ nationalities.<br>Learn more about our Inspection service line in this video: <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wRWFOOAl92M">Intero - The Power of Integrity</a>.<br><br></p><p><strong>Your team</strong></p><p>You join a close-knit Integrity team of five, including you: a Principal Integrity Engineer and Team Lead in Vancouver, an Integrity Engineer in Mexico City and two Junior Integrity Engineers in Toronto and Calgary. The team is part of our Data Analysis (DA) department.</p><p>Together the team delivers integrity reports for clients around the globe. You will be in daily contact with your teammates. The atmosphere is informal, communication is clear and transparent, and the pace follows the workload: some weeks are calm, others are full on. As the first team member in Europe, you strengthen our coverage of European time zones and clients.<br><br></p><p><strong>Why this role matters</strong></p><p>An inspection delivers a list of findings. For our clients, especially in highly regulated markets, a list of problems without a solution is not enough. That is where you come in. The Integrity team turns inspection results into a complete solution package: assessments, remaining life, and clear recommendations that help operators make well-founded decisions about the continued operation of their systems. In this role you raise the quality and consistency of that package, review the work of junior engineers, and help develop the tools and methods the team relies on.<br><br></p><p><strong>What your week looks like</strong></p><p>Part of your week goes to performing integrity assessments on pipelines, piping, heaters and boilers. The other part goes to supporting business development, developing methods and giving technical support. From day one you will work on Corrosion Growth (CG) reports and Fitness-for-Service (FFS) assessments.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Perform Level 1 and Level 2 FFS assessments and advanced Corrosion Growth Analysis (CGA); review or prepare Level 3 FFS assessments where projects require it.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Review the work of junior engineers, such as Run Comparison reports, dent strain and bending strain analyses, against the applicable codes and standards.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Act as the technical point of contact for project managers and clients on structural integrity questions, and support proposals and client-facing technical activities.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Align recommendations with local and national regulations, and build knowledge of codes and standards across jurisdictions.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Validate and help develop our in-house engineering tools, and write Python or VBA scripts to automate evaluations based on MFL and UT inspection data.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Set up and maintain internal procedures, technical questionnaires and quality checklists so every deliverable meets client and internal standards.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Manage several projects at the same time, and flag risks and priorities early.<br><br></p><p><strong>What you bring<br><br></strong></p><p><strong>Must-haves</strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; A degree in Mechanical and/or Materials (or Metallurgical) Engineering, ideally a combination of both. A Master's degree is a strong plus.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; At least 5 years of relevant experience in the structural integrity of pressurised equipment, preferably pipelines, including independently performing and reviewing FFS assessments and remaining life calculations.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Strong working knowledge of fracture mechanics and corrosion and fatigue damage mechanisms.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Working knowledge of API 579 / ASME FFS-1, API 530, ASME B31G, DNV-RP-F101, API 1183, ASME VIII Div. 2 and ASME PCC-2, and of the international regulations for pipeline and pressure equipment integrity.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Experience with risk assessments and turning results into clear, actionable recommendations.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Strong mathematics and statistics, including probabilistic methods.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Programming skills to solve engineering problems, preferably in Python, VBA or MATLAB.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Mid to advanced-level training in integrity assessment methods.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; You write clear, professional technical reports and explain complex topics to both technical and non-technical audiences.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; You work independently with minimal supervision, keep your agreements, and are flexible with working hours to collaborate with colleagues in Canada and Mexico.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; You are curious, proactive and a team player who suggests improvements to help the team work better and avoid rework.<br><br></p><p><strong>Nice-to-haves</strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Hands-on experience with finite element analysis (FEA), preferably ABAQUS.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Experience with creep assessment of boilers and heaters.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Exposure to Level 3 FFS assessments.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Experience with pipeline ILI data analysis (MFL/UT).</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Experience with client-facing technical activities or proposals.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Experience in highly regulated industries.<br><br></p><p><strong>Why Intero</strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <strong>Work that makes a difference.</strong> Your recommendations directly determine whether critical pipelines and installations can keep operating safely.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <strong>Variety.</strong> Pipelines, piping, heaters and boilers; FFS Level 1 to 3, corrosion growth, dent strain and more, for clients all over the world.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <strong>Real influence.</strong> You help shape the team's methods, procedures and in-house tools, and see your ideas put into practice.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <strong>International team, flexible set-up.</strong> Daily collaboration with colleagues in Canada and Mexico, remote working from Europe, and once or twice a year a visit to our HQ in Tricht.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <strong>Growth.</strong> Within one to three years you can take on a larger share of Run Comparison and FFS reviews and expand into dent strain analysis.<strong><br><br>What we offer</strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; A contract for 32-40 hours per week.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; A competitive salary and benefits package, tailored to the country you're based in. Because pay and conditions vary by location, we'll discuss the details with you personally during the process.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Remote working from Europe, or hybrid if you live near one of our offices with available space.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Flexible start of the day between 6:00 and 10:00, with occasional early or late meetings to overlap with our North American team.</p><p><br><strong>Application process</strong></p><p>1. Introductory interview with our recruiter.<br>2. Technical interview with our Principal Integrity Engineer and Team Lead.<br>3. Final interview with Manager and Business Director.<br>4. Job offer.<br><br></p><p>We would like the new colleague to start as soon as possible. Interested? Apply via the button below with your CV and a short motivation. For questions, please contact Veroniek Smits, our Corporate Recruiter, at <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" ---------- do not work with recruitment agencies for this vacancy. Unsolicited CVs from agencies will not be considered.</em></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/intero-integrity-services/remote-senior-integrity-engineer-tricht-72924","tags":["ISP","Remote"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Remote job","created_at":1792333901},{"slug":"teamleider-warehouse-geodis-venlo-302828","company_name":"GEODIS Benelux","title":"Teamleider Warehouse GEODIS Venlo","description":"<p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Ben jij onze nieuwe Teamleider Warehouse?</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">Voor onze locatie in Venlo zijn wij op zoek naar een gedreven Teamleider Warehouse. Heb jij een passie voor logistiek, weet jij teams te motiveren en zorg jij voor een efficiënt verloop van het warehouseproces? Dan zijn wij op zoek naar jou!</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Jouw rol</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">Als Teamleider Warehouse ben je verantwoordelijk voor het organiseren van een effectieve en efficiënte goederenstroom, conform de vastgestelde kwaliteitsnormen en klantplanning. Je zorgt voor een optimaal werkklimaat en creëert ruimte v