 a culture that’s as ambitious as it is authentic. We hold ourselves to high standards, thrive on solving the unexpected, and push boundaries together. But we also know how to enjoy the ride. Our culture is a unique blend of curiosity, team spirit, and a touch of unconventional charm. It’s fast-paced, fun, and grounded in a sober sense of purpose and perspective. Whether we’re deep in design reviews or sharing laughs over lunch, we’re building something meaningful together. At Qualinx, you’re not just contributing to a ground-breaking technology, you’re helping shape a team that’s redefining what it means to work in deep tech.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p><strong>Role</strong> <strong>Overview</strong></p><p>As a Senior&nbsp;System-Level Designer, you'll play a pivotal role in designing the digital baseband part of our cutting-edge GNSS/IoT chip. This role is for those who enjoy challenges and wish to contribute to the development of technology that powers GNSS L1/L5 receivers and BLE/Lora/NB-IoT transceivers.</p><p>As a <strong>Senior Communication System Engineer</strong>, you will help shape the future of our next-generation products. You will be responsible for the design and implementation of advanced communication systems, contributing to both innovation and performance optimization.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Design and implement communication systems with a focus on bandwidth, latency, reliability, and power efficiency.</p></li><li><p><strong>Develop innovative algorithms and solutions to address challenging system-level problems.</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Analyze standard requirements (e.g., BLE, LTE) and benchmark competitor performance to guide strategic design decisions.</strong></p></li><li><p>Collaborate with cross-functional teams including hardware, software, and network engineers to ensure seamless system integration.</p></li><l