ng Digital, Analog and RF components. This role requires hands-on experience in debugging, analyzing, and characterizing SoCs through automated test setups.</p><p class="MsoNormal">Key responsibilities will include:&nbsp;</p><ul><li><p>Collaborating closely with the design teams, firmware, and software teams to define digital test requirements and validation plans.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Developing and executing comprehensive test plans to validate all digital functionalities.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Working on SoC-level validation and bring-up, managing tests from component-level through to full system operation.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Creating Python/C scripts to automate tests and collect measurements using automated setups with digital test equipment.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Collecting, organizing, and analyzing data to verify performance across various conditions for different samples.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Utilizing tools like Python for scripting and data handling to automate processes and enhance analysis.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Debugging and troubleshooting issues that arise during testing, including hardware, firmware, and digital interface issues, and collaborating with design, applications, and software teams to implement solutions.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Documenting test procedures, validation results, and specifications for internal reference and compliance.&nbsp;</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Requirements:</strong>&nbsp;</p><p class="MsoNormal">The ideal candidate for this Digital Validation Engineer role is detail-oriented, proactive, and has a can-do attitude, with the following qualifications:&nbsp;</p><ul><li><p>BSc or MSc in Electrical Engineering, Embedded Systems, or a related field.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Strong knowledge of digital circuits, including memory and MCU architecture and digital interfaces, with experience in low-power IoT systems.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Hands-on experience with bus protocols (AHB, APB) and peripheral interfaces (SPI, I2C, UART).&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Working knowledge of FPGA systems for pre-silicon debugging, especially Zynq processors.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Proficiency in firmware debugging and real-time troubleshooting using debugging tools and creating mini-fw to test the HW</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Experience with automated test setups and conducting concurrent lab tests on multiple products.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Hands-on experience with lab equipment, such as oscilloscopes, logic analyzers, digital multimeters, signal generators, and programmable power supplies.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Proficiency in Python programming for automation and data analysis; familiarity with tools like Excel, database management, and version control software (e.g., Git).&nbsp;</p></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal">Bonus Points:&nbsp;</p><ul><li><p>Knowledge of GNSS technologies for precise location-based IoT applications&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Experience in Power, Voltage, and Temperature (PVT) characterization and expertise in analog hardware testing.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>What's in it for you?</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">At Qualinx, we believe that great work starts with a great environment, pioneering technology and a fun dynamic market to address. Here’s what you can expect when you join our team:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Ownership and Impact</strong>: We offer employee equity, giving you the opportunity to share in the success you help create.</p></li><li><p><strong>Well-being Matters</strong>: Your physical and mental health are important to us. We provide access to wellness resources, including company discounts and a free mental healthcare platform.</p></li><li><p><strong>Global Talent, Local Support</strong>: If you're relocating from abroad, 