ase of production test solutions for Qualinx products.</p></li><li><p>Support in developing and debugging ATE test programs for wafer sort and final test.</p></li><li><p>Support silicon characterization, correlation, and production qualification activities.</p></li><li><p>Analyze test results and production data to identify issues and opportunities for yield improvement.</p></li><li><p>Work with Design and Product Engineering teams to investigate test failures and support root cause analysis.</p></li><li><p>Contribute to test time optimization and test coverage improvements.</p></li><li><p>Support OSAT and manufacturing partners during product bring-up and production ramp.</p></li><li><p>Assist in implementing and validating digital test methodologies, including SCAN, MBIST, JTAG, and Flash testing.</p></li><li><p>Develop automation scripts and tools to improve test efficiency and data analysis.</p></li><li><p>Maintain test documentation and support continuous improvement of test processes.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul><li><p>Bachelor's degree in Electrical Engineering, Electronics Engineering, Semiconductor Engineering, or a related field.</p></li><li><p>Minimum five years of experience in semiconductor test engineering, product engineering, or a related role.</p></li><li><p>Semiconductor test development and production test flow experience.</p></li><li><p>Experience with semiconductor testing at wafer sort and/or package level.</p></li><li><p>Experience with embedded digital interfaces such as SPI, I2C, UART, SWD, and JTAG.</p></li><li><p>Understanding of digital test methodologies, including SCAN, MBIST, JTAG/Boundary Scan, IDDQ and Flash Memory Testing</p></li><li><p>Experience with ATE platforms or test development environments such as NI and Teradyne IG-XL.</p></li><li><p>Programming or scripting experience in Python, C/C++, MATLAB, or similar languages.</p></li><li><p>Un