nce into clear growth recommendations for country managers and leadership.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Set analytics standards, documentation, and best practices, support and improve our MCP and data connector ecosystem, and challenge misleading metrics so decisions rest on sound data.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You'll Bring</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- 3+ years of experience in Marketing Analytics, Web Analytics, or Growth Analytics, ideally within D2C e-commerce, with hands-on knowledge of GTM, GA4, e-commerce data layers, pixels, server-side tracking, UTMs, and conversion APIs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- High proficiency in SQL and experience working with cloud data warehouses and multiple marketing, CRM, and e-commerce data sources.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Solid understanding of attribution, incrementality, cohort analysis, funnel analysis, CAC, ROAS, MER, contribution margin, and payback.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- A strong statistical mindset with practical experience designing A/B tests, geo-lift tests, holdout tests, or conversion lift studies, and the communication skills to turn analytical topics into clear guidance for marketing and leadership.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Bonus: experience with AI-assisted analytics, API connectors, automated reporting, or marketing data infrastructure.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we offer</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>💼 Compensation</strong> — Competitive salary · Company pension plan · Capped overtime, fully paid</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🚀 Growth and Career Development</strong> — You will take real ownership from the start with direct impact on key business outcomes, work with an international team across Europe, and follow fast-track opportunities to grow into senior leadership roles as PERGOLUX scales.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>⏰ Time 