 Zusammenarbeit mit erstklassigen Cybersecurity-Expert:innen in unserem internationalen CERT-Team.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Über Eye Security</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Eye Security bietet Unternehmen in Europa Cybersicherheit mit integrierten Cyberversicherungslösungen. Unser Team vereint Fachleute mit Erfahrung in den Bereichen Nachrichtendienst, Militär, Technologie und Beratung. Sie alle verbindet eine gemeinsame Mission: Cybersicherheit auf Enterprise-Niveau für jedes Unternehmen zugänglich zu machen – nicht nur für die Großen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Eye Security wurde 2020 in Den Haag gegründet und vereint Managed Detection and Response, ein rund um die Uhr von Menschen betriebenes Security Operations Center (SOC), schnelle Incident Response und eine eigene Cyberversicherung auf einer einzigen Plattform. Das Unternehmen betreut Organisationen in den Niederlanden, Belgien und Deutschland und baut seine Plattform sowie den Marktzugang in ganz Europa aus.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Eye Security wird von Bessemer Venture Partners, J.P. Morgan Growth Equity Partners und TIN Capital unterstützt. Zuletzt nahm das Unternehmen in einer von Sofina angeführten Series-C-Finanzierungsrunde 60 Millionen Euro auf.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/eye-security/senior-carrier-and-product-management-berlin-183446","tags":["Business"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Germany","created_at":1792453223},{"slug":"senior-carrier-and-product-management-berlin-466220","company_name":"Eye Security","title":"Senior Carrier and Product Management","description":"<h2>The role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll bring together cyber insurance, product development and carrier management. In this pivotal role, you’ll oversee Eye Security’s insurance portfolio and MGA partnerships, developing scalable solutions for our European markets.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2>What you’ll do</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product management</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop our cyber insurance products in Germany, the Netherlands, Austria and other markets, closely integrating them with our Cyber Guard and incident response services. Coordinate external partners where needed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor market, carrier and broker trends, and adapt our products and policy wordings accordingly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the underwriting team and our customers with legal and insurance-related questions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify compliance risks across all markets at an early stage and implement solutions that comply with the laws and regulations of each jurisdiction.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive the introduction of a modular product concept and scale processes through automation.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Carrier management</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead carrier management from a legal and strategic perspective. Negotiate and oversee MGA agreements in the EU and UK, and manage capacity for SMEs and large risks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build a stable, long-term and diversified carrier base that best supports our business model.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Oversee all MGA agreements, coordinate renewals, and build a claims management function that aligns our profitability goals with carriers’ requirements.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2>What you’ll bring</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong legal knowledge of cyber insurance in Germany, the Netherlands or another EU country. A legal qualification as a lawyer or equivalent legal expertise is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Several years of experience with cyber products and policy wordings in underwriting and/or claims handling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An understanding of cyber compliance and regulatory requirements, with practical experience in incident response and prevention solutions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An entrepreneurial mindset, a structured and detail-oriented approach, and the motivation to build and scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to work independently, communicate with confidence and follow through—and to bring others along with you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confidence negotiating with customers and partners, resilience, and a strong sense of ownership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency in English and either German or Dutch.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2>What we offer</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A pivotal role at one of Europe’s fastest-growing cybersecurity scale-ups.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The opportunity to shape an innovative cybersecurity product line that brings effective cybersecurity and cyber insurance together on a global scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An attractive compensation package, including a bonus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible working hours to support a healthy work–life balance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A car allowance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your choice of equipment: a MacBook or Dell laptop, and an iPhone or Android smartphone.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Active support for your personal and professional development.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The opportunity to work with outstanding cybersecurity experts in our international CERT team.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2>About Eye Security</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Eye Security provides businesses across Europe with cybersecurity and integrated cyber insurance solutions. Our team brings together professionals with backgrounds in intelligence, the military, technology and consulting. They share one mission: to make enterprise-grade cybersecurity accessible to every business—not just the largest ones.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in The Hague in 2020, Eye Security brings together Managed Detection and Response, a human-led Security Operations Center (SOC) operating around the clock, rapid incident response and its own cyber insurance on a single platform. The company serves organizations in the Netherlands, Belgium and Germany, and is expanding its platform and market reach across Europe.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Eye Security is backed by Bessemer Venture Partners, J.P. Morgan Growth Equity Partners and TIN Capital. Most recently, the company raised €60 million in a Series C funding round led by Sofina.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/eye-security/senior-carrier-and-product-management-berlin-466220","tags":["Business"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Germany","created_at":1792453223},{"slug":"remote-senior-events-manager-emea-19628","company_name":"Camunda","title":"Senior Events Manager- EMEA","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Camunda is <strong>the enterprise platform for agentic orchestration</strong>, enabling organizations to coordinate <strong>AI agents, people, and systems </strong>across complex, end-to-end business processes. With built-