ms of the European debate on autonomy and AI in defence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Senior Engagements:</strong> Lead SE3's most significant political and press engagements as a senior voice of the company.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team Building:</strong> Build, lead and develop the government affairs and communications team as the function scales.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Your Profile</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You take ownership of outcomes and remove obstacles without waiting for direction. You turn discussions into clear decisions and decisions into deliverables, and you hold yourself and your team to a consistently high standard.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You hold a degree in political science, international relations, security studies, communications, public policy or an adjacent discipline. A postgraduate qualification is welcome.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You bring significant senior experience in government affairs, political or strategic communications, or in a ministry, parliament or comparable institution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have built and led a function or team, and you have owned senior stakeholder relationships.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You speak native-level German and have full professional fluency in English, written and spoken. Given the nature of SE3's work in the defence sector, candidates must be eligible to work on defence-related projects and, where required, obtain the relevant security clearance.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Especially Valued Bonus Skills</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An established network in the Bundestag, the Federal Ministry of Defence or European institutions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in defence, security or technology policy.</p></li>