&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;MinIO is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and an affirmative action employer. We review applications for employment without regard to their race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, age, veteran status, genetic information, physical or mental disability, medical condition, marital status, or any other basis prohibited by law.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/minio/remote-commercial-account-executive-ny-182931","tags":["Sales - Commercial"],"job_types":[],"location":"Remote","created_at":1792432519},{"slug":"senior-software-engineer-hamburg-151369","company_name":"Fender","title":"Senior Software Engineer","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Software Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fender Musical Instruments Corporation&lt;/strong&gt; is a world-famous brand with offices across the globe. Fender was born in Southern California and has built a worldwide influence beyond the studio and the stage. A Fender is more than an instrument; it’s a cultural symbol that resonates globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Software Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to join our software team in Hamburg, where we build the technology that powers the next generation of music production tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will own key components of our cross-platform applications, which integrate tightly with other Fender hardware and software products. You will lead the design and implementation of complex features, contribute to architectural decisions, mentor fellow developers, and help drive continuous improvement of our tools and processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Functions:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement, and maintain core features in C++ across platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to both firmware-level and desktop/mobile platform development to deliver seamless user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clean, efficient, and maintainable code in C++ and participate in code reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with team members to refine requirements for software development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to improving development workflows, tools, and practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or similar education&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive professional experience designing, developing, and maintaining complex, production-grade software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong object-oriented C++ programming skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with a cross-platform software framework such as Qt or JUCE&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with software development tools (Visual Studio, XCode, Git, Jira / Confluence)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent German and English language skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid analytical and problem-solving skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently and as part of a team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in music production and audio technology, as well as knowledge of music production software and software instruments is a benefit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Fender Musical Instruments:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fender Musical Instruments Corporation (FMIC) is one of the world’s leading musical instrument manufacturers, marketers and distributors, whose portfolio of brands includes Fender®, Squier®, PreSonus®, Gretsch®, Jackson®, EVH®, Charvel®, Bigsby®, and Groove Tubes®, among others. For more information, visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.fender.com/&quot;&gt;www.fender.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/fender/senior-software-engineer-hamburg-151369","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":[],"location":"Hamburg","created_at":1792432519},{"slug":"associate-product-manager-salesforce-6-7-months-maternity-cover-all-genders-berlin-135462","company_name":"Lightspeedhq","title":"Associate Product Manager, Salesforce (6-7 months Maternity Cover)  (all genders)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hi there! Thanks for stopping by 👋</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are you actively looking for a new opportunity? Or just checking the market? Well… you might just be in the right place!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for an <strong>Associate Product Manager, Salesforce (6-7 months Maternity Cover)</strong> to join our Global Information Systems Team. You will be responsible for leveraging best practices, understanding internal customer needs, translating them into clear, actionable direction and working hand-in-hand with development as the voice of the business.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"> <strong>What you’ll be doing:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Building trusted relationships and managing stakeholders;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Product roadmapping &amp; feature prioritization;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understanding and documenting business processes, requirements, scenarios, pain points;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Facilitating in developing new business processes and identifying areas for optimization;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Analyze and propose new solutions to improve business performance;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translating business requirements into instructions for technical teams to execute, and clarifying any issues throughout the development process;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Managing the agile development process, including sprint and release planning, user acceptance testing, and other related ceremonies;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Change management, including the development of training materials, communication plans, launch schedules;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cross-functional collaboration with various product &amp; technology teams, corporate data, Go-To-Market;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to the overall management and development of the IS Product Management Practice, by continuously working to establish best practices and improve ways of working.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you need to bring:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re a team of 100+ people located all over the globe (Canada, USA, EMEA, APAC). Our team is responsible for ensuring everyone across the organization has the tools and systems in place to effectively do their jobs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a candidate who has experience with the following:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">1-2 years of demonstrated Product Management, Project Management and/or Business Analysis experience in SaaS implementations;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An impressive ability to translate between business and technical stakeholders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Intermediate knowledge of standard Salesforce features;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven success managing complex projects across multiple functional groups;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Usage of Agile Methodologies such as scrum;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven ability to drive decisions, positively influence other team members, and thrive in an entrepreneurial environment;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong organizational skills with a demonstrated ability to pivot and reprioritize across multiple projects;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated abilities in leading design workshops, proposing solutions and building corresponding artifacts;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Salesforce and Scrum Master certification preferred.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We know that people are more than what’s on their CV. If you’re unsure that you have the right profile for the role... hit the ‘Apply’ button and give it a try!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What’s in it for you?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Come live the Lightspeed experience…</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to do your job in a truly flexible environment;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Genuine career opportunities in a company that’s creating new jobs everyday;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work in a team big enough for growth but lean enough to make a real impact.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">… and enjoy a range of benefits that’ll keep you happy, healthy and (not) hungry:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Health &amp; Wellness Credit- expense up to 400 EUR per year towards your gym membership, yoga classes, a new bike or whatever else you do for your health</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mental Health Support through the Modern Health App- whether it is meditation, coaching or counseling you need - each employee gets access to this platform</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">People Experience - Our PX benefit allows you to work from pretty much anywhere in the world for 60 days a year</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Time off to volunteer and give back to your community</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>To all recruitment agencies: Lightspeed does not accept unsolicited agency resumes. If we have not directly engaged your company in writing to supply candidates for a specific vacancy, Lightspeed will not be responsible for any fees related to unsolicited resumes.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Lightspeed is a proud equal opportunity employer and we are committed to creating an inclusive and barrier-free workplace. Lightspeed welcomes and encourages applications from people with disabilities. Accommodations are available on request for candidates taking part in all aspects of the selection process.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Where to from here?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Obviously, this has to be mutually beneficial: we want you to step into a role you love, and we want to offer you a place you’re proud to come to every day. For a glimpse into our world check out our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.lightspeedhq.com/careers/">career page here</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lightspeed is building communities through commerce, and we need people from all backgrounds and lived experiences to do that. We were founded in 2005, in Montreal’s gay village and our original members were all part of the LGBTQ+ community. The ethos of our business has been about inclusion from the very beginning, and we strive to provide a workplace where everyone belongs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Who we are:</strong> </h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Powering the businesses that are the backbone of the global economy, Lightspeed's one-stop commerce platform helps merchants innovate to simplify, scale, and provide exceptional customer experiences. Our cloud commerce solution transforms and unifies online and physical operations, multichannel sales, expansion to new locations, global payments, financial solutions, and connection to supplier networks.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in Montréal, Canada in 2005, Lightspeed is dual-listed on the New York Stock Exchange (NYSE: LSPD) and Toronto Stock Exchange (TSX: LSPD). With teams across North America, Europe, and Asia Pacific, the company serves retail, hospitality, and golf businesses in over 100 countries.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lightspeed handles your information in accordance with our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="c-link" href="https://www.lightspeedhq.com/legal/applicant-privacy-statement/">Applicant Privacy Statement</a>.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/lightspeedhq/associate-product-manager-salesforce-6-7-months-maternity-cover-all-genders-berlin-135462","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1792431619},{"slug":"product-manager-berlin-360655","company_name":"Augustus","title":"Product Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Few people get to build a bank from scratch. Even fewer get to build one at a moment when banking itself is being reinvented.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />The Dollar is the best product in the history of the world - there is infinite global demand. But International Fintechs and non-US banks are left with two unsatisfying options to access it: Either they build on legacy clearing banks that are slow and unreliable, or they interface with middleware providers that don’t move and hold the dollars directly, but themselves rely on underlying legacy banks. Augustus collapses this stack by combining two things: A real, national bank charter (in organization), and Marble, our proprietary core banking system, built around intelligence, made of code.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />We are a group of operators, unicorn early employees, ex-founders and people who walked away from degrees because they believe this is an industry and career defining opportunity. We are backed with more than $200M from Peter Thiel's Valar Ventures, Tiger Global, Hummingbird, QED, Creandum, and the founders of Nubank, Ramp, Deel, Circle, Fluidstack, Fuse, and n8n.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />We are regulated in Europe and live with Euro and Stablecoin clearing today. Now, we are building the US team from the ground up, while continuing to grow rapidly in Europe.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>The Role</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">You own Banking Experience: the accounts at the center of customer's relationship with the bank, and the  API and dashboards they use to manage them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In this role you’re responsible for redefining what beautiful software in banking looks like. You'll define account structures that give customers powerful building blocks for their products, and craft intuitive interfaces grounded in a deep understanding of their use cases and workflows.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You report to Will, Head of Product, and work closely with Simon, our CTO. You're expected to operate with full autonomy on your team's roadmap, collaborating with design and engineering.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Your First Six Months</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Months 1-2:</strong> Take over day-to-day ownership of the Banking Experience team - the roadmap, the ways of working, the hard decisions. Establish yourself with customers and how they use our accounts. You define and ship your first project.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Months 3-4:</strong> Execution mode. You're unblocking engineering daily, making hard prioritization calls, and shipping your roadmap to customers. You're proactively raising the bar across accounts, API, and dashboard by feeding what you learn from customers into the product.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Months 5-6:</strong> You're working with live customers on the products you've built. Deposits and number of account holders are scaling. You've moved from execution to platform mode - evolving the roadmap based on what our customers are building on top of Augustus.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Who Will Thrive At Augustus</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe that throwing smart people with high agency at big problems produces the best outcomes. We’re building a modern correspondent bank, and we win by having a better team. The people who succeed here share the following traits:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>American Dream:</strong> You’d rather shoot for gold than settle for mediocrity. You pick the harder goal and stay optimistic when the odds are against you. If it feels easy, we aimed too low.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Live Player:</strong> You don’t need permission. You rebuild what’s broken without being asked, challenge how things are done, and move before the perfect moment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ever to Excel:</strong> You can’t accept good enough and you take your work personally. When it matters, you do what it takes and keep raising the bar for yourself and your team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Genuine:</strong> You play for the company, not your title or turf. Low ego, low drama, no politics. You say it straight, also upwards and always assume good intent.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>This role is for you if:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You want to spend time with customers to intimately understand and then innovate on their workflows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re a structured and relentless problem solver.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You combine first-principles thinking with deep domain knowledge to make complex processes simple.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have taste and care deeply about the quality of what you build.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You leverage AI to push the boundaries of what a PM can do.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re excited about building a programmable bank and helping shape what that means.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Hard Requirements</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience end-to-end owning and building banking, fintech, or developer platform products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical enough to spar on architectural decisions with engineers - you're comfortable in API design discussions, not just UI reviews.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have experience with control planes, dashboards, or console products at infrastructure, finance, or developer tools companies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have strong opinions on information architecture and how to organize complex products so they feel simple</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable in customer-facing roles - you've pitched, demoed, and closed early adopters yourself.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Based in New York or Berlin, or willing to relocate.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Pay transparency</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Compensation packages at Augustus include base salary, equity, and benefits. New hire offers are made based on a candidate's experience, expertise and geographic location. The annual US base salary range for this role is $180,000-$230,000 + equity.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What We Offer</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Career Growth:</strong> You will be given more responsibility and pushed to grow faster than ever before.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Network:</strong> Your peers are brilliant, highly motivated people. These people will be foundational in your future opportunities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Real Participation:</strong> Employees are shareholders. You will think and act like an owner.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Perks &amp; Benefits:</strong> Relocation support, visa support, the latest Apple gear (MacBook + AirPods), lunch benefit, gym benefit, a beautiful office in the heart of the city, 4x on-/offsites per year, and an annual development budget.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Additional to the global benefits above, we offer localized benefits such as comprehensive medical, dental, and vision insurance and a 401(k) retirement plan for our US team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Augustus is committed to creating an inclusive environment where people from all backgrounds can thrive and where different viewpoints and experiences are valued and respected. Augustus will consider all applications for employment without regard to race, ethnicity, national origin, religious beliefs, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, neurodiversity, disability, age, parental or veteran status.</em></p><hr><p>Compensation: €90K – €120K • Offers Equity</p><ul><li> • €90K – €120K • Offers Equity</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/augustus/product-manager-berlin-360655","tags":["Product"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1792431618},{"slug":"chief-operating-officer-magdeburg-349323","company_name":"DRIVAR®","title":"Chief Operating Officer","description":"<h2>Deine ersten Monate als Chief Operating Officer bei DRIVAR®</h2><p>Du übernimmst die operative Führung unseres globalen Internet-Marktplatzes für Sportwagen, Oldtimer und Luxusautos von unserem wunderschön an der Elbe gelegenen Hauptsitz in Magdeburg au