tructional-designer-berlin-468777","company_name":"Bots and People Product GmbH","title":"AI Expert & Instructional Designer","description":"<h2><strong>About us</strong></h2><p>Bots & People designs and delivers enterprise AI upskilling programmes for large organisations across Europe, including Daimler Truck, Deutsche Telekom, Siemens Energy and Audi. The company has trained more than 80000 employees across over 30 enterprise clients.</p><h2><strong>The role</strong></h2><p>This role involves both designing enterprise learning programmes and delivering them as the expert in the room.</p><p>It is a senior individual contributor role requiring independent professional judgement across programme architecture, client consultancy and live delivery.</p><h3><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h3><p><strong>Facilitation</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Deliver live training, workshops, hackathons and coaching sessions for enterprise audiences</strong>, from small leadership groups to sessions with up to 100 participants, <strong>in German and in English</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Facilitate our signature formats</strong>, and adapt them live to the room</p></li><li><p><strong>Handle technical questions on AI tooling in the moment</strong>, at a level that holds up with technical participants</p></li><li><p><strong>Run dry-runs and debriefs, and feed what you learn in delivery back into the design</strong></p></li></ul><p><strong>Learning design</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Design blended learning programmes</strong> and multi-month learning journeys for enterprise clients: impact goals, learning objectives, module structure, session sequencing and learning transfer tasks</p></li><li><p>Decide the pedagogical approach, format and instructional method for each engagement, based on the client’s maturity, audience and business goals</p></li><li><p><strong>Develop course content, exercises, facilitator guides and learner materials</strong>, and keep the existing course library current as the AI landscape moves</p></li></ul><p><strong>Client work and AI expertise</strong></p><ul><li><p>Lead scoping and diagnostic conversations with L&D leads, heads of function and senior stakeholders, and challenge the brief where it won’t achieve the stated outcome</p></li><li><p><strong>Contribute to proposals and pre-sales conversations</strong>: scoping, feasibility, effort estimation</p></li><li><p><strong>Maintain current, hands-on expertise across the generative AI landscape</strong>, with particular depth in the Microsoft ecosystem, including Copilot, M365 and Power Platform (but not exclusively)</p></li><li><p><strong>Act as a reference point on learning design and AI capability</strong> for our freelance trainers, including onboarding and reviewing their sessions</p></li></ul><h3><strong>What you bring</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Several years of <strong>instructional design or L&D experience</strong> in which you owned programme architecture end to end, ideally for corporate audiences</p></li><li><p><strong>Proven experience facilitating live training for enterprise audiences</strong>, including senior and technical participants</p></li><li><p><strong>Practitioner-level expertise with generative AI tools</strong>: you build, troubleshoot and teach with them, not just follow the news</p></li><li><p>The ability to <strong>make complex technical material accessible to non-technical audiences</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Experience with large enterprise clients</strong> and their stakeholder environments</p></li><li><p><strong>German at completely fluent level (C2).</strong> You will design and facilitate in German for German clients</p></li><li><p><strong>English at C1 or above.</strong> Our company language is English: team communication, internal documentation and all interviews are in English, and you will facilitate in English too</p></li><li><p>Based in Germany</p></li><li><p>An advantage: working knowledge of the Microsoft ecosystem (Copilot, M365, Power Platform)</p></li></ul><p><strong>What we offer</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Fully remote work within Germany</strong>, with occasional travel for client delivery and team meetings</p></li><li><p>Quarterly team on-sites</p></li><li><p>30 vacation days per year</p></li><li><p>Urban Sports membership</p></li><li><p>A small, fast team where what you build is used by thousands of learners within week</p></li></ul><p><strong>All interviews are in English.</strong> We aim to complete the process within 4 weeks of your application.</p><h3><strong>Apply</strong></h3><p>Send us your CV and, if you have one, an example of a learning programme or session you designed/facilitated. A long cover letter is not needed; <strong>a few lines on why this role is interesting to you are.</strong></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/bots-and-people-product-gmbh/ai-expert-instructional-designer-berlin-468777","tags":["Remote","Training","Development"],"job_types":["Permanent employment (unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag)","professional / experienced"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1792422083},{"slug":"senior-product-manager-parental-leave-cover-fixed-term-12-months-berlin-chemnitz-sachsen-dresden-sachsen-217327","company_name":"Staffbase","title":"Senior Product Manager - Parental Leave Cover (Fixed-Term, 12 Months)","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Staffbase&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We inspire people to achieve great things together. Our mission is to help organizations unlock the power of inspirational communication with the first &lt;strong&gt;AI-native Employee Experience Platform&lt;/strong&gt;. Our&lt;strong&gt; industry-leading and award-winning agentic AI communications channels&lt;/strong&gt; - intranet, employee app and email solutions - create engaging experiences that connect and empower employees.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Headquartered in Chemnitz, Germany and New York City, with offices in Berlin, London, Sydney, Tokyo, Prague, and Minneapolis–St. Paul, our diverse team of 550+ employees supports 1,500+ customers—reaching over 14 million employees—in transforming their employee experience.&lt;br&gt;We are proud to be a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Unicorn&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;company—privately valued at over $1 billion—demonstrating strong growth, innovation, and lasting impact in our industry. Together, we’re shaping the future of workplace communication.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;At Staffbase, we&#39;re moving beyond communication into a new frontier: helping millions of frontline and deskless employees not just&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;find&lt;/em&gt; information, but actually &lt;em&gt;get things done&lt;/em&gt;. The Actions team owns that execution layer - the bridge between employees, Staffbase AI, and the real operational work happening in stores, warehouses, hospitals, and in the field.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;Our biggest bet right now is &lt;strong&gt;Tasks&lt;/strong&gt; - the product that lets an enterprise&#39;s HQ push operational standards to thousands of locations and see them executed on the ground, driven by a major new partnership. Around it sits a portfolio of agentic actions, forms, and HR workflows that make Staffbase a place where work happens, not just where it&#39;s announced.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Product Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to seize this moment. This is a&lt;strong&gt; 12-month fixed-term role&lt;/strong&gt; - and we mean that as a feature. It&#39;s a rare chance to make an outsized, visible impact on Staffbase&#39;s expansion into operational territory, with senior leadership attention and real revenue behind it, without signing up for the long corporate haul. If you&#39;re a builder who loves 0-to-1 energy and wants to point it at a concrete, high-stakes problem for a year, this is for you.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;You&#39;re a commercially-minded generalist, comfortable in ambiguity, fast-moving, and able to hold the whole picture - customer, business case, and build - in your head at once.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
