 word ‘Pleo’ actually means ‘more than you’d expect’, and living by that mantra has been the secret to our success over the last 10 years.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Now, we’re at a pivotal moment in our journey; every move we make has a direct impact on our 40,000+ customers, our business, and our collective success. We need people who take pride in uncovering customer needs, who turn complex problems into simple solutions, challenge the way things are done (respectfully), and always aim high. With great ambitions driving us forward, we can’t say we’ve got this whole thing figured out. And frankly, that’s half the fun! What we can say is that we’re a driven, progressive, and, importantly, a kind bunch of 850+ people from over 100 nationalities, all committed to delivering the future of business spending, together.</p><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">In this role, you will play a central part in assessing, questioning, and enhancing how customers experience Pleo. Drawing on deep regulatory knowledge, you will lead Consumer Duty initiatives, actively spot potential customer harm, examine what drives customer journeys, and ensure targeted remediation creates lasting, positive impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll need sharp analytical skills and the confidence to influence stakeholders, translating data and MI into decisive action. You will construct and manage dashboards and reporting mechanisms that illuminate emerging patterns, vulnerable customer risks, and key concerns, offering executive leadership clear visibility into operational gaps and necessary solutions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your contribution goes well beyond producing MI. You will conduct QA across complex complaint handling and sensitive customer interactions, manage Ombudsman cases, and speak up when evidence shows outcomes aren't meeting expectations. Collaborating across teams, you'll turn data-driven insights into practical improvements, drive projects to completion, and evaluate whether changes deliver real results for our users.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're seeking someone who views Consumer Duty as a powerful driver of business improvement rather than a routine compliance exercise. You'll bring together technical understanding, rigorous analysis, and constructive challenge to investigate root causes, align key partners, deliver change, and prove that customer experiences are continuously getting better.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Who you’ll be working with and reporting to </strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll work closely with teams across Customer Support, Complaints, Compliance, Risk, Operations, Product, Data, Technology, and other business functions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The role will have broad exposure across the organisation, particularly when customer outcome risks or Consumer Duty-related remediation require cross-functional action.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll also work closely with senior stakeholders through Consumer Duty governance and reporting, helping translate detailed analysis into clear insights, risks, recommendations, and actions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll be doing</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Consumer Duty Specialist, you will:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Turn data into customer outcome insight</strong>: Build and own MI, dashboards, KPIs, and reporting that give the business a clear view of customer outcomes, trends, risks, and emerging areas of concern.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own Consumer Duty reporting</strong>: Produce monthly and quarterly Consumer Duty reporting, turning complex data into a clear story for senior leadership and Board-level audiences. You'll go beyond showing <em>what</em> happened to explain <em>why it matters</em> and <em>what we should do about it</em>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Identify customer harm</strong>: Use complaints, QA findings, customer feedback, vulnerable customer data, Ombudsman cases, and MI to identify potential customer harm, emerging risks, and systemic issues.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Challenge the business</strong>: Where the evidence suggests customers aren't receiving good outcomes, you'll be expected to ask difficult questions, challenge assumptions, and ensure the issue is properly understood and addressed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Drive remediation and change</strong>: Work with stakeholders across the business to agree remediation plans, establish clear owners and timelines, and help drive Consumer Duty-related projects and improvements through to completion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Provide complaints QA</strong>: Conduct weekly quality reviews of complaints handled by the Complaints Manager, using findings to identify quality issues, customer risks, and wider trends.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Manage Ombudsman activity</strong>: Act as the primary operational contact with the UK Ombudsman, managing referred complaints, responses, remedies, compensation, invoices, and related communications.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Leverage AI and smart automation</strong>: Spot opportunities to apply automated tools and AI to scale and streamline Consumer Duty analytics, monitoring, and workflows. You will feel empowered to test emerging tech and eliminate repetitive manual work, maintaining proper critical evaluation and human governance whenever compliance risks or customer impacts are involved.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you bring</strong> </h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll thrive in this role if you have:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong Consumer Duty knowledge</strong>: You understand the principles of Consumer Duty and how they translate into practical customer outcomes, particularly across complaints, customer support, vulnerable customers, and customer journeys.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong data and MI experience</strong>: You know how to take complex data, build meaningful dashboards and reporting, and identify the insights that actually matter. You're comfortable working with data rather than simply consuming reports created by others.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A customer outcome mindset</strong>: You're naturally curious about how customers are experiencing the business and are able to connect data, customer feedback, complaints, and operational activity to real customer outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong analytical and problem-solving skills</strong>: You can spot trends, anomalies, and patterns, investigate root causes, and determine whether an issue is isolated or potentially systemic.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The confidence to challenge</strong>: You're comfortable questioning decisions, processes, and assumptions when the evidence suggests customers may be experiencing poor outcomes. You can challenge constructively and build relationships at the same time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A bias towards action</strong>: You don't believe reporting is the end of the process. You want to understand what needs to change, bring people together, and help make it happen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Project and remediation experience</strong>: You're comfortable managing actions, timelines, dependencies, stakeholders, and risks across cross-functional projects, particularly where there is a regulatory, customer, or operational outcome to deliver.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>An AI and automation mindset</strong>: You're naturally curious about how AI and automation can make processes more efficient, improve analysis, and free up time for higher-value work. You look for sensible opportunities to automate repetitive tasks and use AI to augment your thinking, while maintaining appropriate human oversight, critical judgement, and accountability — particularly where customer outcomes or regulatory decisions are involved.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Why is this role a good fit for you</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is a good fit for you if:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You love using data to uncover things that others might not see.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You want your analysis to drive real change, rather than sit in a report or dashboard.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You enjoy asking <em>"why?"</em> and getting to the root cause of customer problems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're comfortable challenging the business when the evidence tells you something isn't working.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is not a good fit for you if:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You prefer to produce reporting without being involved in what happens afterwards.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're uncomfortable challenging stakeholders or having difficult conversations when customer outcomes aren't where they should be.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You prefer working within a narrow functional remit rather than across multiple teams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>How you’ll develop in this role </strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">In your first 6 months at Pleo, you'll:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build a deep understanding of our customer outcome data, existing Consumer Duty MI, complaints, vulnerable customer journeys, and current areas of risk.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take ownership of key Consumer Duty dashboards and reporting, developing a clear view of the metrics and insights that matter most.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish strong relationships with stakeholders across Customer Support, Complaints, Compliance, Risk, Operations, Product, Data, and Technology.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead the analysis behind Consumer Duty reporting and help shape how customer outcomes are presented to senior stakeholders and the Board.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Over time, you'll have the opportunity to shape how Pleo measures, understands, and improves customer outcomes, helping move Consumer Duty from a regulatory obligation into a genuine driver of better customer experiences and better business decisions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Show me the benefits!</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your own Pleo card (no more out-of-pocket spending!)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lunch is on us for your work days - enjoy catered meals or receive a lunch allowance based on your local office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comprehensive private healthcare - depending on your location, coverage options include Vitality, Alan or Médis</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer 25 days of holiday + your public holidays</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">For our Team, we offer both hybrid and fully remote working options</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Option to purchase 5 additional days of holiday through a salary sacrifice</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We use MyndUp to give our employees access to free mental health and well-being support with great success so far</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Paid parental leave - we want to make sure that we're supportive of families and help you feel that you don't have to compromise your family due to work</p></li></ul><h2><strong><br />The interview process</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We want to ensure you are set-up for success and understand what will be expected of you. If your application is successful, our interview process is as follows:</p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Intro call: A 30-minute chat with our Talent Partner to discuss the role and your background.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Meet the Hiring Manager: 1hr going through role in more depth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pleo Challenge: A case study were you talk us through how you'd solve a work appropriate challenge.</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Transparency is important to us so we also wanted to share some insights about what we’re looking for in applications to ensure you can set yourself up for success!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Last time we advertised this role, we received a really high volume of applications but could only select so many. Some of the key reasons why previous candidates didn’t make it past the application screening stage include:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">CV writing and content: we receive a lot of CVs, and many of them are AI-generated. We love seeing people leverage AI—it’s a big focus for us internally too—but without human intervention, these CVs can sometimes become generic and fail to show a candidate in the best light. What we're really looking for is the specific details of real impact that only you know from your previous experience. A top tip from us is to use the “Achieved X, as measured by Y, by doing Z” formula (credit: Laszlo Bock, ~2014) to give a really clear picture of what you’ve worked on. A final note: including links to your previous companies' websites is a huge help and allows us to truly understand your background!</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Application care: every single application we receive is reviewed by a human (yes, hundreds of them) because we believe that candidates' efforts should be matched by an equal level of human care. This means that we expect a similar level of attention put into your application. Read and answer the application questions carefully, they make a huge difference in our decision-making process.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Profile to role fit: highlight most important aspects of the role, points that might get misunderstood, any specific industry requirements etc.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>About your application</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>English first.</strong> Since it's our company language, please submit your application in English. You’ll be using it a lot if you join us.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A fair look for everyone.</strong> Our talent team reads every single application to ensure the process is fair. To keep things running smoothly, we only accept applications through our system—our support team can’t pass on calls or emails.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Diversity drives us.</strong> We can only reach our goals if our team reflects the world around us. That starts with you hitting apply, even if you don't tick every single box. We encourage people from all backgrounds and experiences to join us.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Interview at your best.</strong> We want you to feel comfortable throughout the process. If you have any accessibility requirements or need a specific format, email ----- We’ll design a process that works for you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your data is safe.</strong> When you apply, we process your personal data as a data processor. For more information on how Pleo processes personal data, read our Privacy Policy <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="in-cell-link" href="https://www.pleo.io/en/legal"><u>here</u></a>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Applying for multiple roles?</strong> Nothing is stopping you, and we assess every role independently. However, we do look for alignment, so make sure you can explain why your interest and experience are right for each specific role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Reapplying.</strong> If you’re applying for the same role again, please wait six months from your last decision before hitting submit.</p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/pleo/senior-consumer-duty-specialist-london-121450","tags":["Legal"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792410016},{"slug":"web-engineer-intern-london-436997","company_name":"Epicgames","title":"Web Engineer Intern","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;WHAT MAKES US EPIC?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At the core of Epic’s success are talented, passionate people. Epic prides itself on creating a collaborative, welcoming, and creative environment. Whether it’s building award-winning games or crafting engine technology that enables others to make visually stunning interactive experiences, we’re always innovating.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Being Epic means being a part of a team that continually strives to do right by our community and users. We’re constantly innovating to raise the bar of engine and game development.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;ENGINEERING - EPIC GAMES SERVICES&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Driving the plug-in power behind Unreal Engine 5. We bridge connections for licensees and our own internal game teams to online services. This allows games like Fortnite to utilize a combination of platform online services as well as Epic’s own online services to build cross-platform online features. Login, parties, voice chat, matchmaking, purchasing, cloud storage, and analytics are just a few examples of online features that our Online Game Services team helps games utilize.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;WEB ENGINEER INTERN&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Web Engineer Intern to join the Tools &amp;amp; Portals team within Epic Online Services. Tools &amp;amp; Portals builds the software, platforms, and digital experiences that enable Epic’s internal teams, player support operations, players, and external developers to work with and access Epic services more effectively. You will contribute to production systems across the full stack while gaining hands-on experience with modern web development, backend services, cloud infrastructure, and AI-assisted software development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you will&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build full-stack features using React, Next.js, TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS with guidance from the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Contribute to development of backend services and APIs using Next.js, NestJS, and Node.js&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Learn and apply development practices for production infrastructure including AWS, Kubernetes, containers, and CI/CD pipelines&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Write, test, review, and deploy production code alongside experienced engineers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Learn and apply AI-assisted software development workflows throughout the software development lifecycle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Contribute to internal tools and developer-facing platforms used across Epic Games&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Interest in full-stack web development and learning modern engineering technologies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Some familiarity with JavaScript, TypeScript, React, or similar web technologies through coursework, projects, or previous experience&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Eagerness to learn, ask questions, and contribute to solving well-defined engineering problems&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Willingness to explore new technologies and codebases, seek support when needed, and incorporate feedback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Ability to work effectively with guidance, communicate questions and blockers, and incorporate feedback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Strong collaboration skills and willingness to work closely with engineers, product partners, external teams, and stakeholders&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Understanding of defined requirements and willingness to ask clarifying questions when needed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Strong communication and collaboration skills, including sharing progress and incorporating feedback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Interest in using AI tools and AI-assisted workflows as part of software development&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This internship has a flexible start date in 2027. Recruitment will be ongoing until teams find an ideal match. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the posting location for the duration of the internship. For more information about Epic’s Early Career Program, visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.epicgames.com/site/en-US/earlycareers&quot;&gt;epicgames.com/earlycareers&lt;/a&gt;. This is going to be Epic!&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;ABOUT US&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Epic Games​ ​is a leading interactive entertainment company. For over 30 years we&#39;ve been making award-winning games and engine technology that empowers others to make visually stunning games and 3D content that bring environments to life like never before. Epic&#39;s award-winning Unreal Engine technology not only provides game developers the ability to build high-fidelity, interactive experiences for PC, console, mobile, and VR, it is also a tool being embraced by content creators across a variety of industries such as media and entertainment, automotive, and architectural design. As we continue to build our Engine technology and develop remarkable games, we strive to build teams of world-class talent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Like what you hear? Come be a part of something Epic!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Epic Games deeply values diverse teams and an inclusive work culture, and we are proud to be an Equal Opportunity employer. Learn more about our Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Policy &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.epicgames.com/site/en-US/eeo-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note to Recruitment Agencies: &lt;/strong&gt;Epic does not accept any unsolicited resumes or approaches from any unauthorized third party (including recruitment or placement agencies) (i.e., a third party with whom we do not have a negotiated and validly executed agreement). We will not pay any fees to any unauthorized third party. Further details on these matters can be found &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.epicgames.com/note-to-recruitment-agencies&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/epicgames/web-engineer-intern-london-436997","tags":["Engineering Specialist"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1792400113},{"slug":"senior-engagement-manager-london-435445","company_name":"Legora","title":"Senior Engagement Manager","description":"<h2>About Us</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Legora is redefining how legal work gets done. Not built for lawyers, built with them. We work alongside the world’s best legal teams, who expect excellence, precision, and speed, and we hold ourselves to the same bar.<br /><br />Our AI-native workspace lets legal professionals move faster, think more clearly, and operate with sharper precision. By analysing thousands of documents in minutes and powering end-to-end workflows, we cut through complexity, teams can focus on what matters: judgment, strategy, and outcomes.<br /><br />2,100+ customers across 80+ countries trust us, including Cleary Gottlieb, Goodwin, Linklaters, White &amp; Case, Dentons, and Barclays. We’ve scaled to<strong> $200M+ in ARR</strong>, with teams across Europe, North America and APAC, and continue to expand through acquisitions including Qura, Walter AI, Graceview, Cadastral, and Wexler.<br /><br />We partner with world-class performers: including Aaron Judge and the New York Yankees, Ludvig Åberg (and his caddie), and campaigns featuring Jude Law.<br /><br />Joining Legora means three things.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We <strong>lean in: </strong>ownership over titles, outcomes over intentions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We <strong>fight for excellence:</strong> high standards, direct, ego-free feedback.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We<strong> grow together:</strong> as a team and with our customers.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mission before ego. Everyone contributes. No one coasts.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you’re driven by impact, pace, and raising the bar. This is the place.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />The way legal work gets done is changing, and Engagement is at the centre of that transformation. We're looking for an experienced Engagement Manager to own Legora's global relationship with one of the Big 4, one of our most significant partnerships, and to fundamentally change the way that firm works with Legora.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a role for someone who has led change inside large, complex organisations and knows that real transformation is designed and managed. You will own the adoption and long-term success of this client globally: building the relationships, defining the outcomes and serving as the trusted adviser and orchestrator who turns Legora into an embedded part of how their teams operate.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Global means global. You will set the strategy for how the firm adopts Legora worldwide, and Engagement Managers in other regions will run their local programmes against the direction and decisions you set. Day to day, you will be the point of contact for the firm's UK and Ireland practice from our London office, and you will travel regularly to other<br />member firms in the network to build those relationships and land the programme on the ground. Expect to be travelling around 25% of the time.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At the heart of the role is designing the client's adoption playbook and delivering a multi-year change-management programme that transforms how they work. You will build the roadmap, sequence initiatives from initial rollout through firm-wide scaled adoption, define measurable outcomes and ROI and evolve the programme as new AI capabilities and use cases emerge.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be critical as we continue to build a best-in-class adoption programme at Legora, helping the client realise measurable ROI, expand successful use cases and transform the way their teams work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You'll Do</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />You'll own the global relationship end to end, leading the post-sale experience across every member firm we work with. Specifically, you will:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />● Set the global adoption strategy for the account and lead its execution across regions. Engagement Managers in other markets will deliver their local programmes against the strategy and decisions you set, and you will be accountable for coherence and outcomes globally.<br />● Act as the primary point of contact for the firm's UK and Ireland practice, while travelling frequently to other member firms to build senior relationships and support local delivery in person.<br />● Design the client's adoption playbook: the tailored change-management approach, stakeholder map and target outcomes for how the firm adopts Legora and transforms the way it works.<br />● Execute against that playbook, sequencing initiatives from initial rollout to enterprise-wide scaled adoption and adapting as the client's needs and Legora's capabilities evolve.<br />● Act as a strategic adviser who deeply understands the client's goals and legal and professional services workflows, surfaces high-impact opportunities and guides teams towards maximum value from Legora.<br />● Drive sustained value through a structured operating cadence: success plans, enablement, stakeholder check-ins, training and value reviews.<br />● Orchestrate engagement from cross-functional teams to accelerate client success (GTM, Product, Legal Engineering, Engineering, Marketing, Support), maintaining end-to-end account context and coordination globally.<br />● Partner with GTM on key commercial moments to ensure seamless transitions, continuity and exceptional customer experience, and to identify and realise expansion opportunities across the account.<br />● Translate customer feedback into action by collaborating closely with Product, Engineering and Marketing to inform roadmap, positioning and enablement.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>What You Bring</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />You care deeply about customer outcomes and you know that transformation has to be designed and led. You're proactive, strategic and comfortable steering demanding, senior stakeholders through significant change. You take pride in being the reason customers adopt, grow and succeed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We're looking for:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />● 5+ years experience in management consulting, legal, LegalTech or customer success in an AI-native B2B vertical.<br />● Extensive experience working with or inside a Big 4 firm is highly desirable, we want someone who already understands how these firms are structured, how decisions get made and how change actually lands across member firms.<br />● A consulting or transformation background, with a demonstrated track record of designing and delivering change-management programmes inside large, complex organisations.<br />● Experience building tailored transformation roadmaps and adoption plans and steering them to measurable outcomes.<br />● A track record of driving adoption, retention and satisfaction with enterprise clients and senior stakeholders.<br />● Experience leading through influence rather than direct authority. You will set the direction that colleagues in other regions deliver against, so you need to be able to bring people with you.<br />● Experience working with legal, compliance or other regulated and complex industries or the ability to learn a complex domain exceptionally fast.<br />● Strong programme and project management skills; you keep multi-workstream initiatives moving and your clients confident.<br />● Excellent communication skills — written, verbal and interpersonal. You can lead boardroom conversations with legal and professional services leaders and roll up your sleeves with hands-on teams.<br />● High EQ: you know when to listen, when to advise and when to act.<br />● A love of fast-paced, early-stage environments where you help build the playbook, not just follow it.<br />● Fluency with metrics and driven by data, customer health and outcomes over process.<br />● Willingness to travel internationally around 25% of the time.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Legora is an Equal Opportunity Employer</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Legora, we believe great teams are built on diversity of thought and experience. We’re proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to creating an inclusive, high-performance culture where everyone can do their best work. We welcome people of all backgrounds and don’t discriminate based on race, color, religion, national origin, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/legora/senior-engagement-manager-london-435445","tags":["Engagement"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792399214},{"slug":"programme-manager-trade-moorgate-323347","company_name":"Checkatrade","title":"Programme Manager (Trade)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Powering Great Work</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We started as the place to find a trusted trade. Now, as we shape the future of home improvement, we're building the tech to transform that landscape for everyone - better products, smarter data, AI where it actually helps - so trades can spend less time on admin and consumers can find someone they trust, first time. That's Powering Great Work, and it's why every team here exists:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🔧 Trades spend less time on admin and more on winning work and growing their business</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🏠 Homeowners get a trusted trade, first time, every time</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🚀 We get to build products that change homes and lives across the country</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Programme Manager (Trade) in Retention, you'll turn strategy into delivery that actually sticks. You won't manage the teams, but you'll shape how they work, what they work on, and whether the initiatives our Head of Operations is driving make it into everyday practice. You'll sit across the whole of Trade Lifecycle, working with Finance, Product, Engineering, Sales and CRM so the right things get built, rolled out and embedded, not just kicked off.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The job, unfiltered:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the delivery of Trade Lifecycle's most critical initiatives end to end, from scoping and planning through to execution and review.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead tooling and systems changes across Retention, Credit Control and Trade Support: define requirements, manage timelines and make sure the teams can use the new systems well.</p></li><li><p sty