p für deine tägliche Arbeit wird dir zur Verfügung gestellt.</p></li></ul><h2>Deine ersten Monate bei p4b</h2><p>In den ersten Wochen machst du dich mit unserer Systemlandschaft und den internen Abläufen vertraut. Du übernimmst schrittweise die Betreuung erster Applikationen und unterstützt das Team bei laufenden Projekten. So wächst du schnell in deine neue Rolle hinein und gestaltest unsere IT aktiv mit.</p><p></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/p4b/system-application-engineer-80-100-bern-93730","tags":["System and Network Administration"],"job_types":["Unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag","berufserfahren"],"location":"Bern","created_at":1792351860},{"slug":"performance-marketing-manager-zurich-429805","company_name":"Aepsy","title":"Performance Marketing Manager","description":"<h2>Why we do what we do</h2><p>The mind is our window to the world. It can paint everything outside in grey or in bright colors. Whoever finds access to that window can change their perspective every day, and psychological hurdles can become chances to grow. Happiness spreads from one person to the next and across a whole society, like a quiet revolution, one mind at a time.</p><h2>Who we are</h2><p>Our mission inspires us and challenges us. Our skills, thoughts and ideas go into a product that reaches thousands of people, and that brings responsibility with it. The work asks for passion, integrity and the courage to try things no one has tried before.</p><p>A team full of people who are crazy enough to think they can change the world they live in. Yes, we are a hardworking team, but not for us alone, not for money or personal fame, but for the people we serve at the center of our efforts: Our team, clients, psychologists on our platform and supporters across the country.</p><h2>Why this role exists</h2><p>Aepsy serves three audiences, each with its own timeline. Clients need support now. Psychologists are building their practice. Employers are deciding whether to unlock access for their whole team.</p><p>This role leads performance marketing for all three: how people find Aepsy, what actually works, and what the numbers suggest we do next.</p><p>Marketing at Aepsy is a small, focused team, and every role has a clear place in it. The Creative Marketing Lead owns copy and shapes the campaigns. The Art Director builds the visual language. The Growth Performance Architect owns the measurement architecture. You work closely with all three, bringing campaigns to the right people through the right channels, finding out what worked, and helping the team decide what to keep, change or stop.</p><h2>Performance with principles</h2><p>Our values shape how we advertise. Privacy is non-negotiable. Anyone visiting a mental health platform deserves the highest level of privacy and data security. That means no urgency or fear in our messages, no before-and-after claims, and no targeting or retargeting based on health data or other sensitive personal information.</p><p>Sometimes this makes a number harder to reach. It also builds trust that lasts, and that trust is why people choose Aepsy. If strong performance combined with strong principles sounds like the challenge you’ve been looking for, we’d love to hear from you.</p><h2>What you’ll do</h2><ul><li><p><strong>Own performance across all funnels.</strong> Clients may decide within days. Employers take longer and involve several people. Together with the colleagues closest to each audience, you define what success means for each one.</p></li><li><p><strong>Run paid media end to end on Meta, Google, TikTok and LinkedIn. </strong>That covers structure, bidding, audiences, creative rotation, and both awareness and conversion, plus the judgement to know which of the two you’re working on.</p></li><li><p><strong>Read the numbers and get more out of them. </strong>The Growth Performance Architect builds the measurement setup with you. You turn it into insights the team can act on.</p></li><li><p><strong>Turn patterns into decisions.</strong> Why do people who considered Aepsy drop off before deciding? Does the response to a creative suggest it should run weekly rather than monthly? Answering questions like these is the core of the role.</p></li><li><p><strong>Shape how people find support. </strong>Search is changing fast, and new ways of discovering things are emerging. You’ll help decide how people find Aepsy when they need it most.</p></li><li><p><strong>Help build the team’s marketing rhythm.</strong> You’ll set up the flow for campaigns, newsletters and more, from first idea to delivery, so the whole team can rely on it.</p></li></ul><h2>What you bring</h2><ul><li><p>Three to four years in performance marketing, including campaigns you’ve run end to end and at least one that didn’t go as planned and taught you something.</p></li><li><p>A data-driven mindset with a real feel for brand and content.</p></li><li><p>Confidence running Meta and Google on your own, and experience with TikTok or LinkedIn for reaching HR leads and psychologists. Bring the channels you’ve found work best.</p></li><li><p>Judgement that weighs data together with values. The field is sensitive, Switzerland is a small multilingual market, and the mission matters.</p></li><li><p>Fluent (Swiss) German and English. Aepsy works in four languages, German is the largest market, and most partners and HR leads communicate in German.</p></li><li><p>A habit of noticing a step that repeats and improving it, using AI in your daily work.</p></li></ul><h3>Strongly preferred</h3><ul><li><p>SEO and GEO basics, and curiosity about how AI search engines choose which sources to cite.</p></li><li><p>Lifecycle marketing experience: segmentation, triggers and deliverability.</p></li><li><p>Experience at an organisation with strong convictions, and enjoyment of doing great work within clear principles.</p></li></ul><h2>What we offer</h2><ul><li><p><strong>Work that matters.</strong> Every campaign you improve helps someone find support a little sooner. Your skills serve something bigger than a conversion rate.</p></li><li><p><strong>A team that has your back.</strong> The Creative Marketing Lead, Art Director, Growth Performance Architect and Head of Marketing are each strong in their field. You’ll never have to face a number alone.</p></li><li><p><strong>A strong foundation.</strong> You’ll build on a product people trust, a network of qualified psychologists, partnerships with employers and insurers, and values clear enough to make hard decisions easier.</p></li><li><p><strong>Room to shape things. </strong>There are three audiences, several funnels, a content area being rebuilt, and a search landscape that AI is changing. Your ideas will have impact, and you’ll see it.</p></li><li><p><strong>A short line to decisions.</strong> You’ll report directly to the Head of Marketing and have access to leadership strategy.</p></li><li><p><strong>Modern tools</strong>, including AI, and the freedom to use them well.</p></li><li><p><strong>Time to recharge</strong>: five weeks of holiday and a mental health benefit (of course).</p></li></ul><h2>Together with us</h2><p>We’re a young, ambitious team with diverse backgrounds and beliefs. We love conversations about the big picture and about the small details. We believe in what we do and work hard for a slightly better world. We’re also friends, parents, partners, stand-up comedians, yoga beginners and Zen monks who enjoy life.</p><p>Sleep on it. Read it again. Then take a deep breath and send us:</p><ul><li><p>Your <strong>CV</strong> and a <strong>personal cover letter</strong>. We read every letter carefully, so tell us what motivates you, why this mission matters to you, and why this role, right now.</p></li><li><p><strong>Whatever shows your thinking best</strong>. A short note is enough. One campaign you can explain well is worth more than a full portfolio.</p></li></ul><p>In our conversation we’ll be curious about two things: a number that proved you wrong, and something you decided to stop doing.</p><p>PS: Please skip the generic, AI-generated cover letter. A few honest lines in your own words mean much more to us. The time you save is better spent in the sun, on a walk in the forest or with a friend. Life is too beautiful for impersonal cover letters :)</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/aepsy/performance-marketing-manager-zurich-429805","tags":["Marketing Manager"],"job_types":["Indefinite contract (unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag)","manager"],"location":"Zürich","created_at":1792351860},{"slug":"working-student-software-engineering-zurich-476563","company_name":"NAIRON","title":"Working Student Software Engineering","description":"<h2>Intro</h2><p><em>For this position we are looking for </em><strong><em>students or recent graduates in Zürich</em></strong><em>, working hybrid at the ETH Student Project House (SPH) and remotely.</em></p><p>Nairon GmbH is a Swiss startup building AI voice agents that answer and make phone calls for businesses. Our platform runs real-time conversations over the phone and on the web, connected to our customers' telephony and business tools. We value clear communication, thoughtful engineering, and a collaborative approach to problem-solving. Join us as we continue to develop tools that make a difference.</p><p>We are looking for a Working Student (30–60%) who wants to work on real production systems next to their studies.  We are flexible on the duration of the employment.</p><h2>Tasks</h2><p>As a Working Student at Nairon GmbH, you will work with our team on one or more of these areas, depending on your interests and skills:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Voice AI:</strong> turn-taking, latency measurements, LLM prompting and tool calls, and evaluating speech models (STT and TTS).</p></li><li><p><strong>Voice model training:</strong> training foundational speech models (TTS and STT) on GPUs: data collection and preparation, training runs, fine-tuning for German and Swiss-German voices, and evaluation.</p></li><li><p><strong>Realtime backend:</strong> <em>Python</em> services around our <em>LiveKit</em>-based media platform, messaging and integrations with customer systems.</p></li><li><p><strong>Web and mobile:</strong> features in our <em>Next.js / React / TypeScript</em> web application and our <em>Expo / React Native</em> app.</p></li><li><p><strong>Platform:</strong> <em>Docker</em>, <em>Kubernetes</em>, monitoring and the tooling that keeps our services running.</p></li><li><p><strong>Commercial and tech sales:</strong> preparing demos and pilot agents, answering customers' technical questions, market and competitor research, and supporting offers and partner conversations.</p></li><li><p>Building test calls, benchmarks and small internal tools, and writing down what you learn.</p></li></ul><h2>Requirements</h2><p><strong>Experience:</strong></p><p>Currently enrolled at ETH Zürich or another university or Fachhochschule, or graduated recently, in computer science, electrical engineering, data science, business and engineering (e.g. MTEC, Wirtschaftsingenieurwesen) or a related field. First project or work experience is a plus, not a must.</p><p><strong>Technical Skills:</strong></p><p>Required:</p><ul><li><p>Programming in <em>Python</em> or <em>TypeScript</em>; for the engineering areas, good fundamentals in Git, APIs and debugging.</p></li><li><p>For commercial work: a solid technical understanding and the ability to explain technology to customers.</p></li></ul><p>Nice to have:</p><ul><li><p>Experience with LLMs, speech or audio processing, or machine learning.</p></li><li><p>Deep learning with <em>PyTorch</em>, training on GPUs, or a related thesis or research project.</p></li><li><p><em>Next.js</em>, <em>React</em> or mobile development.</p></li><li><p><em>Docker</em>, Linux or cloud platforms.</p></li><li><p>Interest in sales, business development or startups.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Communication:</strong></p><p><strong><em>English proficiency is essential</em></strong><em>, both written and spoken, as it is the working language for all positions.</em></p><p>German is a plus, and important for customer-facing work.</p><p><strong>Soft Skills:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Curious, quick to learn and able to work independently.</p></li><li><p>Reliable with the hours you commit to, next to your studies.</p></li></ul><h2>Benefits</h2><ul><li><p><strong>Flexible Work Setup:</strong> Hybrid: work at the ETH Student Project House in Zürich and remotely, around your study schedule.</p></li><li><p><strong>Equipment Provided:</strong> Company laptop provided.</p></li><li><p><strong>Collaborative Environment:</strong> Join a small, agile team where your contributions go into production.</p></li><li><p><strong>Growth Opportunities:</strong> Real experience in AI voice technology and in building a startup, with the possibility of a thesis topic or a full-time role in engineering or sales after your studies.</p></li></ul><h2>Closing</h2><p>If you want to build AI that talks on real phone lines while you study, we'd love to hear from you. Please tell us which areas interest you most, technical or commercial, and how many hours per week you can work.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/nairon/working-student-software-engineering-zurich-476563","tags":["Software Development"],"job_types":["Fixed-term contract (befristeter arbeitsvertrag)","professional / experienced"],"location":"Zürich","created_at":1792351858},{"slug":"senior-network-firewall-engineer-check-point-baden-271506","company_name":"Coopers Group AG","title":"Senior Network & Firewall Engineer (Check Point)","description":"<p>................</p><p>For our client in<strong> Zurich</strong>, we are looking for an <strong>Senior Network & Firewall Engineer (Check Point)</strong></p><p><strong>In this project</strong>, you will take on a key role in managing, securing, and optimizing a highly complex, business-critical network infrastructure within a <strong>Software as a Service (SaaS) environment serving multiple financial institutions</strong>. You will ensure the stability, security, and performance of enterprise network and firewall environments, with a particular focus on <strong>Check Point technologies, advanced networking, and high availability</strong>. Working closely with infrastructure, cloud, and security teams, you will contribute to the continuous improvement of secure and reliable network solutions.</p><p><strong>Your Tasks:</strong></p><ul><li>Administration, configuration, maintenance, and troubleshooting of <strong>Check Point Next Generation Firewalls (NGFW)</strong></li><li>Management of <strong>Check Point Security Management, SmartConsole, Security Gateways</strong>, and firewall policies</li><li>Configuration and optimization of <strong>NAT, VPN connectivity, firewall rules, and network segmentation</strong></li><li>Operation and continuous improvement of complex <strong>enterprise network infrastructures</strong> in a business-critical SaaS environment</li><li>Analysis and resolution of advanced network issues involving <strong>TCP/IP, BGP, OSPF, VLANs, routing, and switching</strong></li><li>Implementation and maintenance of <strong>high-availability solutions</strong>, including Check Point ClusterXL</li><li>Execution of firewall upgrades, migrations, patching, and security hardening activities</li><li>Ensuring secure connectivity and network isolation across multiple customer environments</li><li>Troubleshooting of network performance, availability, and connectivity issues</li><li>Participation in <strong>incident management, root cause analysis, and change management</strong> processes</li><li>Collaboration with infrastructure, cloud, security, and application teams on network optimization and modernization initiatives</li></ul><p> </p><p><strong>Your Profile:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Professional experience</strong> in Network Engineering, Network Security, or Firewall Administration</li><li>Extensive hands-on experience with <strong>Check Point Firewalls</strong>, including configuration, administration, policy management, and troubleshooting</li><li>Strong expertise in <strong>enterprise networking, routing, switching, and network security</strong></li><li>In-depth knowledge of <strong>TCP/IP, BGP, OSPF, VLANs, NAT, IPsec VPNs, and network segmentation</strong></li><li>Proven experience working with <strong>large-scale, complex network infrastructures</strong></li><li>Experience supporting <strong>high-availability, security-critical production environments</strong></li><li>Good understanding of <strong>multi-tenant environments</strong>, secure customer connectivity, and network isolation</li><li>Experience in <strong>banking, financial services, FinTech, or enterprise SaaS environments</strong> is highly desirable</li><li>Knowledge of <strong>Check Point VSX, Multi-Domain Security Management (MDSM), and ClusterXL</strong> is an advantage</li><li><strong>Check Point certifications (CCSA/CCSE)</strong> are an advantage</li><li>Experience with <strong>cloud networking (AWS/Azure)</strong> and network automation tools such as Python, Ansible, or Terraform is a plus</li><li>Strong analytical and troubleshooting skills with a structured, independent, and solution-oriented approach</li><li>Excellent communication skills and ability to collaborate with cross-functional technical teams</li><li><strong>Fluent English skills</strong> are required, German language skills are an advantage</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/coopers-group-ag/senior-network-firewall-engineer-check-point-baden-271506","tags":["Remote","Software Development"],"job_types":["Befristeter arbeitsvertrag","contract"],"location":"Baden","created_at":1792351858},{"slug":"team-member-opportunity-attendant-world-economic-forum-annual-meeting-2027-davos-87244","company_name":"Spool AG","title":"Team Member Opportunity (Attendant) - World Economic Forum Annual Meeting 2027","description":"<p>We are seeking motivated individuals to join our team for the prestigious World Economic Forum (WEF) Annual Meeting 2027 in Davos. This is a unique opportunity to be part of a global event that shapes the world's economic and political landscape.</p><p><strong>Event Details:</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Date: January 18.01. - 22.01.2027</strong><br>depending on the team: arrival 14th or 16th January 2027</p></li><li><p>Location: Davos, Switzerland</p></li><li><p><strong>Important:</strong> Application evenings on <strong>2nd November</strong>, <strong>13th November</strong> or <strong>23rd November</strong> (Zurich), and <strong>17th November</strong> (Lausanne)</p></li></ul><p>Attendance at one of the application evenings is <strong>mandatory and must take place in person</strong>. Unfortunately, online participation is not possible.</p><h2>Tasks</h2><ul><li><p>Badge issuance at registration desks</p></li><li><p>Access control at lounges and sessions</p></li><li><p>Assisting in the congress center and surrounding hotels</p></li></ul><h2>Requirements</h2><ul><li><p>Minimum age of 18 years</p></li><li><p>Valid work permit for Switzerland</p></li><li><p>Excellent English language skills (C1 level or higher)</p></li><li><p>Available for the entire duration: <strong>minimum 16. - 22.01.2027</strong></p></li><li><p>Maintaining a professional and courteous demeanor at all times</p></li><li><p>Discreet, committed, and able to work