ypes":["Full Time"],"location":"Delft","created_at":1792215634},{"slug":"real-world-data-associate-amsterdam-493816","company_name":"Mytomorrows","title":"Real-World Data Associate","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About myTomorrows</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">myTomorrows is a global health tech company dedicated to breaking down barriers for patients seeking treatment options.   </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We strive to enable earlier and better treatment access by bridging the gap between those searching for possible options, and the companies who develop them. We work closely with patients, healthcare professionals, trial sites, patient advocacy groups, and BioPharma – connecting key stakeholders in the drug development ecosystem.   </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’ve developed a cutting-edge AI-powered technology platform that simplifies and streamlines access to drugs in development. To support our users and clients, we have a range of industry-expert specialized teams ready to help. Our services include clinical trial patient recruitment, Expanded Access Program management and Real-World Data collection.   </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With a global footprint spanning 134 countries, to date we’ve supported over 17,000 patients, 3,000 physicians and 350 sites, earning the trust of 60+ BioPharma companies. In October 2025, we closed a €25M investment with Avego Healthcare Capital to fuel our global ambitions and scale the business.  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join us in shaping the future of treatment access - making tomorrow’s therapies accessible for people who need them today. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The opportunity: Real-World Data Associate </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Real-World Data Associate at myTomorrows, you will support the design and execution of real-world data collection within Expanded Access Programs and other non-interventional studies. Working closely with the Real-World Data team, you will help keep communication with clients, physicians and site staff running smoothly, carry out data validation and quality-control tasks, and contribute to the documentation that supports consistent, high-quality RWD delivery. This is a great opportunity to build hands-on experience in real-world data within a purpose-driven, fast-growing company.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Given that most of our team is located in the Netherlands, we only consider candidates for this position who live within commuting distance to our office in Amsterdam.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll do in this role: </strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the design and day-to-day execution of RWD collection within Expanded Access Programs and other non-interventional studies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assist in maintaining communication with clients, physicians and site staff about data collection and data management.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help monitor RWD collection and completion, flagging data discrepancies or missing data for follow-up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Perform basic data validation, cleaning and quality-control tasks in electronic data capture systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Follow relevant regulatory requirements, internal procedures and ICH-GCP principles in all RWD study activities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the preparation and maintenance of SOPs, templates and study documentation for RWD projects.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Share observations and ideas that could improve data collection, workflows and supporting tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work under the guidance of more senior team members, collaborating closely with colleagues across the team and other relevant functions.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you bring to the table:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A bachelor’s degree in Life Sciences, Pharmacy, biomedical sciences or another relevant scientific field.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">0–2 years of experience in Data Management or Clinical Research (e.g. an internship, traineeship or first role).</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong organizational and multitasking skills, with the ability to manage priorities and follow through on commitments.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with, or a strong interest in learning, electronic data capture systems and structured clinical or real-world data.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A basic understanding of ICH-GCP guidelines, or the motivation to develop it quickly.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Close attention to detail and a proactive, solution-oriented mindset.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Eagerness to learn and the ability to contribute positively to a collaborative team environment.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What Success looks like in the first 6 months:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Data completion and quality metrics for your assigned programs are consistently on target.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re contributing ideas and improvements to RWD processes and documentation, helping to raise the bar for data excellence at myTomorrows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re recognized as a reliable partner by both internal teams and external collaborators, someone who ensures the integrity of real-world data to advance patient access</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we offer:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Serve a purposeful mission: helping patients gain access to potentially lifesaving treatments.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">International work environment, scale-up energy and a flat organization.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive salary, annual performance bonus and equity.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Great career-development opportunities in a growing company.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Learning and development budget, alongside internal knowledge-sharing sessions.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Attractive pension plan, with the full premium covered by us.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hybrid work model (2 days in office).</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Policies to support working parents.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Healthy lunch at the office.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Unlimited access to professional guidance by certified psychologists via OpenUp.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An additional holiday for Liberation Day on 5 May.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Equal opportunities</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">myTomorrows is an Equal Opportunity Employer and, beyond upholding discrimination-free practices, we are committed to cultivating a workplace where difference and diversity are protected and celebrated. The best work comes from our best selves, and we go to great lengths in supporting our team members to be just that. </p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/mytomorrows/real-world-data-associate-amsterdam-493816","tags":["Expanded Access"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam HQ","created_at":1792215634},{"slug":"production-engineer-amsterdam-384813","company_name":"Monumental","title":"Production Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Monumental is automating on-site construction with robotics and software. Our mission is to make construction software-defined and autonomous - a future where beautiful, bespoke buildings go up in a single day, with minimal labour.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're a growing team of engineers, operators and technicians from companies like Palantir, Qualcomm, Dyson, Shopify, Tesla, Meta and Google DeepMind. It's still the early days of building the company, and this is a chance to make an outsized impact on a problem that matters. From day one, you’ll be working with an experienced founding team, backed by a $32M Series B led by Khosla Ventures and Plural.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monumental is based in the city centre of Amsterdam, in a beautiful facility with an fully equipped workshop and robot testing floor. We build the whole stack in-house - hardware and software, we're explicitly not a hybrid or remote-first company - you can't build robots or walls from home, so we're onsite five days a week.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Read more on why we believe you should spend your time working on construction, and learn about <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.monumental.co/our-vision/">our vision </a>and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.monumental.co/about/">company</a>. You might enjoy <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2-Q2F0Fcx4A">Based in Europe’s film on how we’re fixing Europe’s housing shortage</a>, or <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DOo8n19XEns">this video by Andreas Klinger of what our office looks like</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monumental are already deploying robots into the real world at scale, building beautiful, bespoke homes. Our robots are on sites across the Netherlands and the UK and will be in the US within a year. Every deployment teaches us something about our hardware; you’ll push our R&amp;D fleet to become one ready for large-series production: you'll own taking us from tens of robots a year to hundreds, and then thousands. You'll also keep that growing fleet deployable, and making design changes yourself to improve reliability and serviceability.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scaling a fleet means solving whatever is in the way: limited space, no clear production process, lead times we can't live with and modules that don't survive the harsh conditions of a construction site. You’ll be expected to wear many hats; we’re looking for people who are genuinely excited to lead these efforts.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our robots are built from modules at every level of maturity, so expect to work with the hardware R&amp;D team at early stages of development to validate R&amp;D designs as fast as we can. In parallel, you'll be in the workshop determining how we assemble them: the processes, the fixtures, the production space itself, getting the very best out of our Amsterdam facilities.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For more context on building hardware at Monumental, read Niall’s Substack: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://open.substack.com/pub/buildmonumental/p/i-quit-my-job-and-moved-country-to?r=68ngjs&amp;utm_campaign=post-expanded-share&amp;utm_medium=post%20viewer">I quit my job and moved country to make robots that will fix Europe’s housing crisis.</a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bottom line, you'll own increasing our quarterly production from 30 sets of robot systems to 100 within a year. This is a challenge. You'll be building the production capabilities at Monumental rather than inheriting them, and you'll do it alongside engineers and technicians who care a great deal about getting this right.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take prototypes through to production-ready modules. Find and address design flaws, validate improvements, and push these modules to production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assembling modules, understand the friction slowing production, and address issues yourself along with the hardware team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop fixtures, jigs and light automation solutions to support module assembly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Find production processes that bring minimal value when done in-house. Work with external suppliers to outsource them, while maintaining production quality.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Produce drawings, assembly instructions and quality checks to make sure our modules are integrated together and our robots are brought up with no errors.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we're looking for</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Industry experience, ideally in a VC-backed start-up, transitioning products from prototype to production</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on, analytical mindset: skilled at building assemblies, running studies, analysing data, solving production and quality issues, and collaborating with technicians to implement and validate improvements</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency in mechanical assembly (press fits, fastener selection, harness, etc.)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong knowledge of GD&amp;T and producing 3D and 2D drawings</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience creating structured process documentation (work instructions, SOPs, quality checklists)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Good communication skills in English, both written and spoken</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice-to-haves</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">BSc in Mechanical, Electrical, Manufacturing or Industrial Engineering, or equivalent</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with robotics or complex electromechanical systems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with ERP tools (Odoo or similar)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why Monumental?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Joining Monumental means being at the forefront of a movement aimed at making significant strides in the construction industry. Here, your work has the potential to impact not just the company but the future of how we build. If you're driven by innovation, eager to tackle complex challenges, and ready to make a tangible difference, we want to hear from you.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">For open applications (where you don’t see an exact role match), please reach out to us at: ----- - share with us the most interesting or challenging project you’ve worked on, why you want to join and your CV or portfolio.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Unfortunately we do not currently support internships.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you don’t meet all the qualifications here but are excited about Monumental and feel you’d still be able to help us solve difficult problems, do get in touch. We welcome generalists who focus on outcomes and are eager to learn on the job.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/monumental/production-engineer-amsterdam-384813","tags":["Hardware Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1792215633},{"slug":"group-product-manager-amsterdam-138407","company_name":"Prosus","title":"Group Product Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who We Are</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've ordered dinner through Just Eat Takeaway. You've bought and sold on OLX. You've paid with PayU. Chances are, you've already used a Prosus company today.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are Prosus, a global technology company powering some of the world's leading lifestyle ecommerce businesses. Every day, billions of people across India, Latin America, Europe and beyond use our products and services to buy, sell, pay, connect and discover.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our AI-driven ecosystem spans 100+ companies across ecommerce, food delivery, fintech and experiences, serving billions of consumers worldwide. AI powers how we operate and innovate, with more than 60,000 active AI agents helping our teams build, scale and move faster. Through our investment team, we also back the founders and technologies shaping the future: From robotics and autonomous systems to synthetic biology and frontier AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Guided by our five values <strong>Innovation, Results, People, Impact, and Entrepreneurship,</strong> culture is our competitive advantage. We thrive with experimentation; we build, we test, we learn, we iterate.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join us in shaping the future of technology at global scale.</p><h2><strong>The Problem You'll Solve</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prosus is building an AI-first future across a global portfolio that spans food delivery, e-commerce, fintech, and education. We invest over $100 million annually in AI, run 800+ models in production, and have deployed Toqan — our internal platform for building, testing, and deploying GenAI and agentic workflows — across the organisation. The scale of ambition is real; the challenge now is focus, coherence, and velocity.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Group Product Manager for our AI Platform, you will own the multi-year product strategy for the platform that underpins every AI initiative across Prosus. This means defining and sequencing the roadmap for agent infrastructure, evaluation frameworks, model deployment pipelines, and the shared capabilities that internal teams — from applied science to application engineering — rely on to build and ship AI products. You will balance long-term platform investments against the immediate, high-impact needs of teams across the portfolio who are racing to deliver.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will lead and mentor a team of product managers, instilling product discipline and building the PM talent pipeline that scales with the platform. You will partner closely with engineering and applied science leadership to shape the technical strategy — making the hard trade-offs between model performance, latency, cost, and reliability that determine what we can promise the business.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">And you will be the connective tissue: the person who turns ambiguous, fast-moving business needs into clear requirements, who aligns stakeholders across functions and geographies, and who ensures that what we build is not just technically impressive but adopted, trusted, and measurably impactful.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Who You Are</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are a senior product leader who has lived through the messy reality of building platform products for internal teams — and loved it. You measure your success not by features shipped but by the velocity and quality of the teams who build on top of your platform.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are deeply technical. You can engage substantively with engineering and applied science teams on model lifecycle, MLOps, evaluation frameworks, and infrastructure trade-offs — not as a bystander, but as a thought partner. You understand agentic architectures, LLM capabilities and limitations, and the operational realities of running AI in production at scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are a people leader. You have managed and mentored product managers, and you take genuine pride in their growth. You set strategic direction, coordinate overlapping roadmaps into a coherent plan, and create the clarity that lets your team operate with autonomy and purpose.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You thrive in ambiguity. You have worked in fast-paced, high-scale environments where priorities shift and the path forward is not always clear. You do not wait for perfect information — you run rapid experiments, test hypotheses, and let data and user feedback guide the next step.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are a communicator. You can simplify complex technical concepts for executive leadership one hour and dig into detailed requirements with an engineering team the next. You build trust across functions and geographies, and you are as comfortable pushing back as you are building consensus.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are customer-obsessed — even when your customers are internal teams. You connect frequently with the people who use your platform, validate solutions through product discovery, and treat adoption as a first-class metric.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What You Bring</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">8+ years in product management, with at least 3–5 years in formal people-management roles leading a team of product managers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated success owning platform-level or infrastructure products used by internal teams — ideally including AI/ML platform capabilities, MLOps tooling, or developer-facing services.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with generative AI, LLMs, and the model lifecycle (training, fine-tuning, evaluation, deployment, and monitoring) in production environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track record of defining and executing multi-year product strategies in fast-moving, high-scale environments.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical Depth</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to engage substantively with engineering and applied science teams on architectural decisions, infrastructure trade-offs, and AI system design.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with agentic workflows, agent frameworks, and the operational patterns that make AI agents reliable at scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong data-driven decision-making: comfortable with analytics tooling, A/B testing, defining and tracking KPIs, and using metrics to measure adoption, accuracy, latency, and ROI.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with modern product and engineering tooling (e.g., Databricks, Jira, Confluence, Figma) and agile methodologies.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Leadership &amp; Influence</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven ability to mentor and grow product managers, instilling PM best practices and building talent pipelines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stakeholder management across functions and geographies — aligning engineering, applied science, business teams, and executive leadership around a shared roadmap.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A bias toward ownership: you take accountability for outcomes, protect your engineers' focus, and course-correct execution without waiting to be asked.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Mindset</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Customer-first: you translate needs into technical requirements, push back when scope dilutes value, and advocate relentlessly for the people who use your platform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort with ambiguity: you structure complex problems, propose pilots to validate direction, and create clarity for new and evolving teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI intuition: you stay current on models, frameworks, and evaluation methods — not as a researcher, but with the hands-on curiosity of a builder.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why Prosus?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Prosus, your colleagues include 60,000 AI agents… and your job is to figure out what that actually means. We're one of the largest operators of agentic AI on the planet, inside a $100B+ portfolio across 100+ companies and two billion people. The humans here own what AI can't do alone: judgment, creativity, and the call on what gets built next.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Own the impact. Work the ecosystem. Earn your growth. Build with backing.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Curious about our perks and benefits? Take a look </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://prosusbenefits.com/"><em><u>at this page</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our Diversity &amp; Inclusion Commitment</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We respect the dignity and human rights of individuals and communities wherever we operate in the world. Building an inclusive workplace where everyone feels welcome and can thrive is critical for us. We provide access to education, which helps everyone understand the important role they play and the positive impact they can have.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Want to know more about life at Prosus? Explore our </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.prosus.com/the-prosus-way"><em>culture and values</em></a><em>.</em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/prosus/group-product-manager-amsterdam-138407","tags":["AI & ML"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1792204835},{"slug":"project-manager-mid-alkmaar-106567","company_name":"Wearebeyondsports","title":"Project Manager (mid)","description":"<h1>Project Manager</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location:</strong> Alkmaar, Netherlands<br /><strong>Working Arrangement:</strong> 5 Days Onsite, Alkmaar Office</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Join Our Team as a Project Manager at Beyond Sports</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you’re someone who thrives on bringing people, technology, and clients together, enjoys taking ownership of projects from start to finish, and gets energy from delivering high-quality digital products, this could be the perfect opportunity for you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Beyond Sports, you’ll work on innovative consumer-facing products and experiences within the sports world, collaborating with multidisciplinary teams to turn ideas and client requirements into successful deliveries.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What Your Day Will Look Like</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Project Manager within the Beyond Sports Delivery Team, you’ll be responsible for the end-to-end delivery of consumer-facing software projects, including websites, mobile applications, data visualizations, and other digital sports experiences.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll take ownership of scoping, planning, budgeting, and project delivery, while making sure projects stay on track and meet the quality our clients and users expect. You’ll work closely with our Design, Engineering, and QA teams, facilitating collaboration and ensuring everyone has the clarity they need to deliver successfully.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll also be a key point of contact for our external clients. From translating customer requirements and feedback into clear scopes, functional requirements, and user stories to managing expectations, risks, and project progress, you’ll make sure communication stays clear throughout the entire project lifecycle.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">When our products go live, you’ll be there too, acting as a central point of communication and helping coordinate and escalate where necessary during live events.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What We Value</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Beyond Sports, we value people who take ownership, communicate clearly, and are comfortable working in a fast-paced and collaborative environment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Project Manager, you’ll need to be proactive and organised, while also being able to adapt your approach depending on the project, client, and team you’re working with. You should be comfortable managing several projects at once and confident bringing together different perspectives to keep everyone moving towards the same goal.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for someone who understands the world of technology and software development and can comfortably translate between technical and non-technical stakeholders. Experience working with data-driven products or projects is particularly valuable for this role.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">While this role is based in Alkmaar, Netherlands, we believe in the power of in-person collaboration, so we expect you to be available for <strong>32–40 hours per week in the office</strong>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Skills and Experience</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You don’t need to tick every box, but here’s what we’re looking for:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience managing <strong>software </strong>or <strong>digital </strong>projects from start to finish, ideally including consumer-facing products such as websites, mobile applications, or data visualization products</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with project scoping, planning, budgeting, and resource coordination</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of software development processes and working with multidisciplinary teams across Design, Engineering, and QA</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience translating customer requirements and feedback into clear scopes, functional requirements, and user stories</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong client and stakeholder management skills, with the confidence to act as the main point of contact throughout project delivery</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication skills and the ability to communicate effectively with both technical and non-technical stakeholders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience managing project risks, issues, reporting, documentation, and delivery progress</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously while maintaining quality and attention to detail</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A proactive and solution-oriented approach to problem-solving</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong collaboration and facilitation skills, with the ability to bring teams and stakeholders together around decisions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The confidence to negotiate, manage expectations, and resolve conflicts professionally when needed</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with project management and delivery tools such as <strong>Azure DevOps</strong> and <strong>Jira</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with modern AI tools such as Copilot and Claude</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A good understanding of data or data-driven products is strongly preferred</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with tools such as <strong>Figma </strong>and <strong>Trello</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working within the sports, media, broadcast, or technology industry</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience supporting the delivery of live products or events</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience identifying and implementing improvements to delivery processes and ways of working</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Ready to Make an Impact?</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you’re ready to take ownership of exciting digital projects, work directly with clients, and bring together talented multidisciplinary teams to deliver innovative sports experiences, we’d love to hear from you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Beyond Sports, you won’t just be managing timelines and budgets. You’ll play an important role in turning ideas, technology, and sports data into experiences that reach fans around the world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Why Level Up Your Career at Beyond Sports?</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>High-impact, fast-paced environment:</strong> Manage exciting projects at the intersection of sports, technology, and digital experiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ownership and responsibility:</strong> Take projects from initial scope and planning all the way through to successful delivery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cross-functional collaboration:</strong> Work closely with Design, Engineering, QA, Business Development, and external clients.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Innovation:</strong> Be part of a company building new ways for fans and clients to experience sports.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ongoing learning and development:</strong> Continue developing your project management, technical, and stakeholder management skills in a dynamic environment.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We also offer:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>25 days off per year</strong> – Because we know rest is important for performance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pension program</strong> – Secure your future</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lunch included</strong> – No need to worry about food logistics</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Gym card</strong> – Stay sharp on and off the screen</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Fresh fruit, coffee, and Friday drinks</strong> – Fuel and fun throughout the week</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bi-monthly outings</strong> – Team bonding and relaxation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Office games</strong> – FIFA, chess, and ping-pong breaks</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you're ready to level up your career, apply now and help us deliver the future of sports tech!</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/wearebeyondsports/project-manager-mid-alkmaar-106567","tags":["Beyond Sports"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Alkmaar","created_at":1792204834},{"slug":"indomo-ai-marketing-transformation-internship-amsterdam-48897","company_name":"Ogilvy","title":"InDomo | AI & Marketing Transformation Internship","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Ogilvy &amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ogilvy has been creating impact for brands through iconic, culture-changing, value-driving ideas since the company was founded by David Ogilvy more than 75 years ago. It builds on that rich legacy through Borderless Creativity—innovating at the intersection of intelligence, imagination and influence, with experts across advertising, sports &amp;amp; entertainment, PR &amp;amp; social, consulting, and health collaborating seamlessly across more than 120 offices spanning 90 countries. Ogilvy was named &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ogilvy.com/ideas/ogilvy-brings-home-network-year-2026-cannes-lions-international-festival-creativity&quot;&gt;Network of the Year&lt;/a&gt; at the 2026 Cannes Lions International Festival of Creativity and&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ogilvy.com/ideas/ogilvy-tops-warc-effective-100-creative-100-4th-straight-year&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;e2c78315-ff05-4544-925f-9288319dea2c&quot;&gt;ranks&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;as the #1 global agency network for creative excellence and effectiveness by WARC for the fourth consecutive year, signifying its ability to deliver creative solutions that drive unreasonable impact for clients and communities. Ogilvy is part of WPP, the trusted growth partner for the world&#39;s leading brands. Powered by exceptional talent and our agentic marketing platform WPP Open, WPP unites cutting-edge media intelligence and data solutions, creativity, production, enterprise solutions and expert strategic counsel.&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;For more information, visit &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ogilvy.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;39833259-880d-4fd8-930f-0d84b1c14850&quot;&gt;Ogilvy.com&lt;/a&gt;, and follow us on&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/ogilvy/&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;735e393e-6e8a-4ca8-804a-74f1bd8166b6&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/ogilvy&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;d10960ce-761b-48c5-81d5-0a7c4cc6013a&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/ogilvy/&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;92ffcb70-6ca7-4d9a-88d5-c130e36e6c4f&quot;&gt; Instagram&lt;/a&gt;, and&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.facebook.com/ogilvy/&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;3bd2010d-00a2-401b-8cfb-7e8c24deac52&quot;&gt; Facebook.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About WPP&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. We unite&amp;nbsp;cutting-edge media intelligence and data solutions, world-class creativity, next-generation production, transformative enterprise solutions and expert strategic counsel&amp;nbsp;in a single company –&amp;nbsp;powered by exceptional talent and our agentic marketing platform, WPP Open,&amp;nbsp;to help our clients navigate change, capture opportunity and deliver transformational growth. For more information, visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://wpp.com/&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;7f087527-f491-4cb6-a79d-3b4a67d1ec89&quot;&gt;WPP.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About InDomo&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;InDomo is a WPP company and the trusted transformation partner for multinationals ready to unlock rapid digital business growth. We work shoulder-to-shoulder with marketing leaders to build bespoke, in-house performance marketing capabilities that break down silos, put the consumer at the centre, and drive measurable commercial impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In 2026, our focus has sharpened around AI-powered marketing transformation. We help brands navigate the shift to an AI-driven world by designing new ways of working, deploying intelligent marketing agents, and leveraging WPP Open (WPP’s proprietary AI platform) to deliver breakthrough results. We are scaling our AI practice rapidly and looking for a sharp, motivated intern to join the team and contribute from day one.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a coffee-and-PowerPoint internship. As our AI &amp;amp; Marketing Transformation Intern, you will be embedded in a small, high-impact team working at the intersection of strategy, technology, and execution. You’ll support real client engagements, help build AI-powered solutions, and contribute to shaping how some of the world’s biggest brands adopt AI in their marketing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be given real responsibility, direct access to senior team members, and the opportunity to develop skills that sit at the cutting edge of where marketing is heading. If you’re finishing a Master’s programme and want to hit the ground running in AI-driven marketing transformation, this is the role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;AI Agent Development Support&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in the design, testing, and iteration of custom AI expert agents for enterprise marketing clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help build and refine AI-powered workflows using WPP Open and adjacent tooling, working alongside senior team members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research and experiment with AI tools, techniques, and frameworks (such as prompt engineering, retrieval-augmented generation, and API integrations) to support solution development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document agent performance, capture learnings, and contribute to our internal knowledge base.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Workshops &amp;amp; Client Engagement&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the preparation and delivery of AI Discovery Workshops and transformation sessions for senior marketing leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help develop workshop materials, including diagnostic frameworks, interactive exercises, and output templates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attend and contribute to client meetings, with the opportunity to present specific sections or findings as your confidence grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the delivery of internal training and enablement sessions on AI tools and ways of working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Go-to-Market &amp;amp; Research&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help develop pitch decks, case studies, proposals, and other sales collateral for new business development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct competitive analysis and market research to keep our AI propositions sharp and well-positioned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the packaging and refinement of InDomo’s AI service offerings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Platform &amp;amp; Innovation&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become proficient in WPP Open, exploring new features and capabilities and sharing findings with the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay on top of the rapidly evolving AI and marketing technology landscape, surfacing relevant tools, trends, and opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring fresh thinking. We value your perspective as someone close to the latest academic research and emerging ideas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About You&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Must-Haves&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently pursuing or recently completed a Master’s degree in Marketing, Business, Digital Strategy, Data Science, Computer Science, or a related discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine, demonstrable interest in AI and its application to marketing or business. You’ve explored AI tools beyond the basics and can talk about what you’ve learned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and strategic thinking skills. You can take a complex topic, break it down, and communicate it clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident communicator who is comfortable presenting ideas to a room, whether that’s a team meeting or a client session.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and visual communication. You can structure a compelling deck or write a clear, persuasive brief.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter mentality. You take initiative, work independently when needed, and don’t wait to be told what to do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Available for a full-time, 6-month internship based in Amsterdam.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Strong Pluses&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with AI tools in an academic or personal project context, such as building chatbots, experimenting with LLMs, using AI coding assistants, or working with APIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with concepts like prompt engineering, large language models, retrieval-augmented generation, or agent architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous internship or work experience in marketing, consulting, or a technology-related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with enterprise platforms (e.g., CRM systems, marketing automation tools, or analytics platforms).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Dutch and/or international market dynamics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What We Offer&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of the WPP network, you’ll have access to a world-class professional environment and a comprehensive set of benefits:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real, meaningful work on live client engagements with some of the world’s biggest brands. No busywork.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct mentorship from experienced AI and marketing transformation leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with WPP Open and cutting-edge AI tooling that most people only read about.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A competitive internship compensation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to WPP’s global learning resources and professional development programmes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Light, open-plan office space with roof terrace, on-site bar, and stunning views over central Amsterdam.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role is based at WPP Amsteldok Amsterdam and requires 3–4 days of on-site work, with the flexibility to work remotely 1–2 days a week.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong foundation for a career in one of the fastest-growing areas in marketing. High-performing interns may be considered for permanent roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Ogilvy, our people are at the heart of what we do: a creative agency that sparks game-changing ideas across culture and business through collaboration, integrity, and a celebration of self-expression.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in building powerful teams with purpose - and we relentlessly curate transformative initiatives that make our commitment to fairness, and equity a reality.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our ultimate mission is to leave a positive impact on the world, creating a better future for all, while supporting and uplifting the global communities we serve.&amp;nbsp; This is central to our mantra of Borderless Creativity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Ogilvy is an equal opportunity employer and considers applicants for all positions without discrimination or regard to particular characteristics. We are committed to fostering a culture of respect in which everyone feels they belong and has the same opportunities to progress in their careers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you need any assistance seeking a job opportunity, or if you need reasonable accommodation with the application process, please contact us at ----- Please note that this contact is only for candidates who are requesting accommodation. Emails for other purposes, including application status requests, will not receive a response.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/ogilvy/indomo-ai-marketing-transformation-internship-amsterdam-48897","tags":["Consulting"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1792194924},{"slug":"staff-forward-deployed-engineer-ai-native-software-development-amsterdam-326389","company_name":"jetbrains","title":"Staff Forward Deployed Engineer – AI-Native Software Development","description":"&lt;p&gt;At JetBrains, code is our passion. Ever since we started, back in 2000, we have strived to make the strongest, most effective developer tools on earth. By automating routine checks and corrections, our tools speed up production, freeing developers to grow, discover, and create.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We just unveiled JetBrains Central,&amp;nbsp; a platform for agent-driven software development that connects tools, agents, and infrastructure. It enables automated AI workflows to run, be monitored, and be managed across teams – with clear visibility into results, costs, and performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;JetBrains Central provides three core capabilities:&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Governance and control: &lt;/strong&gt;Policy enforcement, identity and access management, observability, auditability, and cost attribution for agent-driven work. Some of these functionalities are already available via the &lt;a href=&quot;http://console.jetbrains.cloud/&quot;&gt;JetBrains Central Console&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agent execution infrastructure:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Cloud agent runtimes and computation provisioning that allow agents to run reliably across development environments.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agent optimization and context:&lt;/strong&gt; Shared semantic context across repositories and projects, enabling agents to access relevant knowledge, and task routing to the most appropriate models or tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Inside the Professional Services department, we are building a team of Forward Deployed Engineers to help our customers adopt AI-native development with JetBrains Central and enable JetBrains consulting partners to transform their customers’ AI-native software development lifecycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Principal Forward Deployed Engineer, you will work directly with early adopter customers to deploy JetBrains Central platform into complex enterprise environments and help them move from experimental AI usage to governed, scalable AI-native development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will act as a trusted advisor to customer engineering teams and consulting partners, while also mentoring other Forward Deployed Engineers and helping with complex deployments. In this role, you will help establish best practices for enterprise AI adoption and influence how organizations implement AI-driven software development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is often a strong fit for engineers who have previously served as Principal or Staff Engineers, Heads of Engineering, CTOs, or Solutions Architects and who enjoy working directly with customers while staying deeply involved with complex technical systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role combines consulting, architecture, and hands-on engineering. Your work in the field will directly influence how our platform evolves and how enterprises adopt AI-driven development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work directly with the world’s most innovative companies — our client base includes 420 of the Fortune 500 — ensuring they maximize the value of their JetBrains investments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deploy JetBrains Central platform into enterprise development environments, CI/CD systems, and internal developer platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help organizations transition from ad-hoc AI experimentation to governed AI-native development workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement enterprise AI governance, including security policies, access management, and data privacy controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable observability for AI-driven development to help organizations understand their AI usage and its impact on productivity, as well as their code-generation patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design sustainable AI adoption strategies, including usage controls and cost visibility across multiple model providers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate our cloud-based agent execution layer, allowing AI agents to run securely and at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with JetBrains product teams to shape the platform based on real-world deployments and customer feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create delivery frameworks and train JetBrains partners to deliver the desired scope of service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and support other Forward Deployed Engineers, sharing architectural expertise and helping to scale the team’s deployment practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will thrive in this role if you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A consultant at heart who can communicate effectively with both engineers and technical leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to see the whole picture of the software development lifecycle across developer tools, infrastructure, APIs, and cloud systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced at integrating complex software systems into enterprise environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curious about the future of AI agents and AI-native software development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working with early adopters and overcoming ambiguous technical challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Motivated to mentor other engineers and contribute to building a new technical discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in software-related projects, ideally in a customer-facing or consulting environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Java or Python.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or integrating developer platforms, infrastructure systems, or software solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with modern development workflows (CI/CD, developer environments, internal developer platforms, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with customers or technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills and the ability to operate in fast-evolving technical environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability and desire to travel to meet customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;These would be a plus, but are not blockers&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with industry-specific solutions (fintech, telco, retail, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AI/LLM platforms, agent frameworks, or AI-assisted development tools.&lt;br&gt;Experience in solutions engineering, consulting, or forward-deployed engineering roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the JetBrains ecosystem or developer productivity tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;#LI-KP1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We know great ideas can come from anyone, anywhere. That’s why we do our best to create an open and inclusive workplace – one that welcomes everyone regardless of their background, identity, religion, age, accessibility needs, or orientation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;We process the data provided in your job application in accordance with the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.jetbrains.com/legal/docs/privacy/privacy-recruitment/&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/jetbrains/staff-forward-deployed-engineer-ai-native-software-development-amsterdam-326389","tags":["Professional Services"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1792194921},{"slug":"growth-marketer-amsterdam-212924","company_name":"Tebi","title":"Growth Marketer","description":"<h2><strong>About us:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tebi is creating the first Connected Restaurant Management System that makes hospitality flow. In one seamless platform, Tebi embeds sales, reservations, kitchen prep, payments, and all the data that powers it, creating smooth service and intuitive insights.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded by Arnout Schuijff, co-founder of Adyen, and backed by €50 million in funding from Index Ventures &amp; CapitalG, Tebi is built in service of hospitality first. Thousands of restaurants, cafés, bars, and coffee shops across the Netherlands, UK, Italy, Spain, Germany, Denmark and Finland already love running on Tebi.</p><h2><strong>About the role:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Restaurant owners generally aren't on LinkedIn and they don't read e-books. They ask friends, search Google, and more and more often, they ask ChatGPT. We need someone who can find new ways to reach them and get those ideas live quickly.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're hiring a Growth Marketer to build and ship our organic and non-paid growth experiments. This role is for a builder, not a strategist. You'd rather ship a working test today than a polished deck next week. You'll take ideas from the backlog to live, measure them honestly, and double down on what works. Using AI and no-code tools, you'll build pages, tools and campaigns yourself instead of relying on agencies and six-figure budgets.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll report to the Head of Marketing, who sets direction and priorities. You'll work in deep collaboration with our other growth marketers, product marketing and creative teammates, plus embed yourself in the wider org of Sales, Account Management, RevOps, Product, and more.</p><h2><strong>What you'll be doing:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ship growth experiments, fast:</strong> Take ideas from our growth backlog and get them live: landing pages, tools, ads and content. Run plenty of them, keep what works and kill what doesn't.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Get Tebi recommended by AI:</strong> Own our visibility in ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, Gemini and Google's AI Overviews. Create and update content built to be cited, not just published, and track how often we show up compared with competitors.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build tools operators actually use:</strong> Build free tools, calculators and templates for restaurant owners, and scale our programmatic landing pages. Use no-code, AI and vibe coding tools to ship without waiting on engineering.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Run creative campaigns:</strong> Help launch scrappy, unconventional campaigns across markets, from competitive campaigns to guerrilla and partner media, with the support of our Marketing team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Turn word of mouth into a channel:</strong> Test referral and sharing ideas that turn merchant word of mouth into a steady flow of demo requests. Work with our Product Growth team to build the winners into the product.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Keep paid and organic working together:</strong> Support our performance agency with landing pages, creative tests and tracking.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Measure everything:</strong> Keep the experiment log up to date: hypothesis, cost, result and next step. Set up tracking and UTMs properly so we know what actually drove each demo.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How we'll measure success:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experiments shipped each month, and what we learned from them</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demo requests from organic and other non-paid channels</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">How often Tebi appears in AI answers for our category, by market</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demos from free tools, the reservation widget and programmatic pages</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What you’ll bring:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Think like a growth marketer but move like a hacker. You know what drives results and how to build just enough to prove it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ship rather than spec. A working prototype today beats a polished plan next week</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have built and launched things yourself, like pages, tools, automations or campaigns, and can tell us what happened, including what didn't work</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Already use AI to work faster and have a point of view on how it's changing the way people find products</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are hands-on with no-code and AI tools (Framer or Webflow, Zapier or Make, Claude or ChatGPT, Cursor or similar), without being precious about the stack</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are comfortable with data and honest about results, in GA4, HubSpot, Looker or whatever gets the answer</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have creative, sharp ideas and the discipline to ship the unglamorous parts too</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take ownership and don't wait to be told what to do. No task is above or beneath you</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Speak fluent English. Another European language is a plus</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with SEO, and with AEO or getting a brand cited by AI tools</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience marketing to small businesses, or a background in hospitality</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Vibe-coding projects you're proud of</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We don't have a minimum number of years for this role. We care more about how you think and what you've built than how long you've been doing it. If this sounds like you but you don't tick every box, we'd still like to hear from you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Start-up Equity</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive Salary</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lunch Provided in Office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Team building events</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Unlimited time off</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>What is Restaurant Software?</strong> </h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Restaurants and other merchants use various software systems such as Point of Sale (POS), Reservations, Kitchen Display Systems (KDS), Payments, Inventory, Staffing, and the list goes on. These systems all need to speak to each other which they frequently don’t. It’s a mess, and we are fixing it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">From buying a croissant at a cafe to having dinner with friends, it’s a €4 Trillion+ global market and a critical part of everyday life in today's economy.</p><h3>How we use AI at Tebi </h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">We use AI the way our merchants use Tebi, to cut out the friction and get to what matters faster. We believe in a world where AI increases quality, efficiency and speed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Tebi, AI isn't a policy or a checkbox, it's just part of how we work. It helps us write, analyse, build, and improve but doesn’t make the last call. If there's a smarter way to do something, we want to find it.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/tebi/growth-marketer-amsterdam-212924","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1792183219},{"slug":"events-community-manager-amsterdam-496347","company_name":"Tebi","title":"Events & Community Manager","description":"<h2><strong>About us:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tebi is creating the first Connected Restaurant Management System that makes hospitality flow. In one seamless platform, Tebi embeds sales, reservations, kitchen prep, payments, and all the data that powers it, creating smooth service and intuitive insights.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded by Arnout Schuijff, co-founder of Adyen, and backed by €50 million in funding from Index Ventures &amp; CapitalG, Tebi is built in service of hospitality first. Thousands of restaurants, cafés, bars, and coffee shops across the Netherlands, UK, Italy, Spain, Germany, Denmark and Finland already love running on Tebi.</p><h2><strong>About the role:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Restaurant owners trust other restaurant owners. They listen to the chef down the street, their wine supplier and their accountant long before they listen to an ad. That's why our events work. When we launched in Berlin, we hosted a four-hands dinner with two local merchants and a well-known food creator. We believe that’s what builds credibility, trust, and ultimately a warm prospect list.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re hiring an Events &amp; Community Manager to turn that into a program that runs in several markets at the same time. You’ll plan and run our partner and owned events, and find new ways to grow Tebi through the hospitality community in each city, neighbourhood and market. You’ll work closely with our local sales teams so every event and partnership turns into real conversations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on role. One week you'll be hosting a merchant dinner in Milan, the next you'll be setting up a distributor breakfast in Amsterdam. You'll report to the Head of Marketing and work closely with our Marketing team to extend these programs to our channel ecosystem, plus align closely with the General Managers and Account Managers in each market.</p><h2><strong>What you'll be doing:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Run events across markets:</strong> Plan and deliver partner and owned events in 2–3 markets at a time, from intimate merchant dinners and industry breakfasts to city launches. You own the calendar, budget, venues, suppliers, guest lists and the plan for the night.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build the playbook as you go:</strong> Turn each event into templates, checklists and supplier lists, so we can launch a city campaign in weeks, not months. Improve them after every event.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build local partner networks:</strong> Find the people operators already trust: drinks distributors, wholesalers, food creators, hospitality associations, accountants and the advisers who help new venues open. Build partnerships that bring us introductions and referrals, not just logos.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Put our merchants front and center:</strong> Work with our best merchants as hosts and anchors, so prospects hear about Tebi from the people they respect.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Turn connections into pipeline:</strong> Agree with local Sales and Account Management who to involve, how to follow up and who owns what conversations. Track every event in HubSpot from invite to demo to signed merchant.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Grow Tebi through the community:</strong> Find new ways to reach operators through the people and places they already trust, in each city, neighborhood and across borders. Keep guests and partners engaged after events, so one introduction leads to the next.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Open new community channels:</strong> Test new ways to grow through our close-knit industry, such as an affiliate or referral program for partners, sharing useful insights from our merchants, and showing up in the forums and groups where operators talk shop.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Capture the stories:</strong> Work with our creative team and relevant freelancers to turn events and partner moments into social content, case studies and sales material.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How we'll measure success:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Events delivered each quarter across markets, on time and on budget</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demos, pipeline and new merchants from each event and partnership</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Introductions, referrals and leads from partners, affiliates and community channels</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cost per demo compared with our other channels</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What you’ll bring:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have built something people show up for: an event series, a supper club, a community, a program. You can point to what it led to, not just how many people came</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Feel at home in hospitality. You've worked in or around restaurants, bars or food and drink brands, and you're comfortable leading a room full of operators</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are high agency. You own your calendar, your relationships and your results, and you don't wait to be told what to do</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build your own playbook when there isn't one, and you enjoy doing the work as much as planning it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Know the difference between a real community and a guest list</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">See growth opportunities beyond events, and are curious enough to test them</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Can run several markets at once without dropping details, and are happy to travel regularly</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track what you do: comfortable with a CRM (HubSpot a plus), UTMs and simple reporting</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Speak fluent English. Dutch, German, Italian, Spanish or a Nordic language is a plus</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Typically this means 3–5 years in events, community, field marketing or partnerships, but we care more about what you've built than how long you've been doing it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>This role isn't for you if:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'd rather plan the program than run it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You need a fixed playbook and a clear org chart to get going</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're not willing to roll up your sleeves on the night</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Start-up Equity</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive Salary</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lunch Provided in Office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Team building events</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Unlimited time off</p></li></ul><h3><strong>What is Restaurant Software?</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Restaurants and other merchants use various software systems such as Point of Sale (POS), Reservations, Kitchen Display Systems (KDS), Payments, Inventory, Staffing, and the list goes on. These systems all need to speak to each other which they frequently don’t. It’s a mess, and we are fixing it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">From buying a croissant at a cafe to having dinner with friends, it’s a €4 Trillion+ global market and a critical part of everyday life in today's economy.</p><h3>How we use AI at Tebi</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">We use AI the way our merchants use Tebi, to cut out the friction and get to what matters faster. We believe in a world where AI increases quality, efficiency and speed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Tebi, AI isn't a policy or a checkbox, it's just part of how we work. It helps us write, analyse, build, and improve but doesn’t make the last call. If there's a smarter way to do something, we want to find it.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/tebi/events-community-manager-amsterdam-496347","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1792183219},{"slug":"director-product-physical-amsterdam-44643","company_name":"hellofresh","title":"Director, Product (physical) (f/m/x)","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting Relationships&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Primary Manager: &lt;/strong&gt;COO and Co-MD&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Dotted Line: &lt;/strong&gt;CMO and Co-MD&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Direct Reports: &lt;/strong&gt;~10 people spanning Culinary, Product Innovation, Product Strategy, Product Operations, and Product Analytics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Factor is a healthy, ready-to-heat meal delivery service that has built a category-defining business in the US and Canada. Now we&#39;re building &lt;strong&gt;Factor in Europe&lt;/strong&gt; — and although we have strong blueprints from North America, we have the opportunity to leverage the very rich multi-cultural environment in Europe to tailor both our physical and digital products to five different markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As our &lt;strong&gt;Director, Product&lt;/strong&gt;, you will own the full product vision and execution for Factor Europe. You will lead a multi-layered team of ~10 people, sit on the Factor Europe leadership team, and maintain a close dotted-line relationship with our CMO to ensure product and marketing move as one.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a rare kind of role: senior strategic ownership and real infrastructure, with the pace and ambition of an early-stage scale up. If you are a visionary builder who leads with curiosity, earns conviction through data, and holds your team to the same high standard you hold yourself — we&#39;d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Lead and Develop a High-Performance Product Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Build, inspire, and manage a multi-disciplinary team — setting a clear vision, establishing the operating rhythms that allow the team to move fast, and investing in the people who will drive Factor Europe&#39;s next chapter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Own and Challenge the Product Vision&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Define a clear and compelling vision for what Factor&#39;s physical product must become in Europe — grounded in customer insight, commercially rigorous, and differentiated enough to win. Develop a deep, independent point of view on where the North American model translates and where European markets demand something different.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Push the team and the business to think beyond the current roadmap — challenging assumptions, interrogating trade-offs, and ensuring we are always working on the highest-leverage version of the product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Act as the liaison to our global Digital Product team — representing Factor Europe&#39;s priorities in the feature roadmap and collaborating on shared global initiatives that benefit the wider business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Drive Customer Retention and Commercial Performance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Own customer retention levers as your north star. Build a rigorous, evidence-based view of what drives it and rally the team around interventions that move the needle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Make product decisions with full awareness of their P&amp;amp;L implications. Take calculated risks, track outcomes honestly, and move quickly to learn and adjust when bets don&#39;t pay off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Build for Multiple European Markets&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Lead our effort to find product-market fit across five distinct markets — understanding how consumer preferences vary by culture, and building a proposition that resonates locally while scaling efficiently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Share learnings across geographies and partner with peers across the HelloFresh Group to continuously raise the bar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Support new channel strategies, understanding and adapting products for different customer bases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Align Product and Marketing Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Work closely with the brand &amp;amp; marketing team to ensure product roadmap and marketing strategies are fully synchronised — so what we build, how we talk about it, and how we sell it form one coherent proposition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Act as the product voice on the leadership team, articulating a compelling vision for where the product needs to go and why.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;A visionary leader who executes. &lt;/strong&gt;You set a compelling direction, bring your team with you, and roll up your sleeves to make it happen.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Customer-obsessed and analytically rigorous. &lt;/strong&gt;Sharp instincts backed by disciplined discovery. Comfortable querying your own data and stress-testing assumptions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Commercially minded. &lt;/strong&gt;You understand how product decisions flow through to the P&amp;amp;L — and hold yourself accountable to outcomes, not just outputs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;A cross-functional influencer. &lt;/strong&gt;You build trust quickly, drive execution through others, and get the right priorities onto other teams&#39; roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Internationally curious. &lt;/strong&gt;You find the complexity of building for multiple European cultures energising, and you seek out the nuances that matter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;An exceptional communicator. &lt;/strong&gt;You write and present with clarity and conviction — from strategy narratives to leadership updates to product briefs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Food and/or nutrition obsessed!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Experience: &lt;/strong&gt;8–10+ years in Product, Strategy, or a closely related commercial leadership role; 3+ years managing multi-disciplinary teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Technical toolkit: &lt;/strong&gt;Advanced Excel/Google Sheets; AI proficiency and curiosity required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Strong preference for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;○&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Experience in D2C subscription businesses — retention, lifecycle, and recurring revenue models.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;○&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Multi-market European experience and an understanding of how consumer preferences vary across the continent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;○&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Experience in physical products or FMCG, especially food &amp;amp; beverage.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;○&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; A track record of scaling a product in a new market and finding product-market fit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Financial Wellbeing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoy 20% off HelloFresh and 40% off Factor_ subscriptions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access the &quot;Benefits at Work&quot; platform for discounts on brands like Nike, Bol.com, and IKEA.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll receive a HelloFresh laptop, a €250 home office setup budget, and contribute to the Bedrijfspensioenfonds Levensmiddelen pension scheme (2025 rate 27.6%; employer pays 19.64%, employee pays 7.96%).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Health &amp;amp; Wellbeing&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Benefit from discounts on ClassPass and gym memberships via Bedrijfsfitness Nederland, free bootcamp classes (Amsterdam), and free subscriptions to Headspace and OpenUp.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get a 10% discount on additional health insurance at Zilveren Kruis in 2025.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexibility &amp;amp; Work-Life&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work flexibly with our hybrid setup (50% office, 50% remote), plus a €2.40 daily remote work allowance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Receive 24 days of annual leave (pro-rated), plus one additional day per year of service (up to 30 days total).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full reimbursement for 2nd-class public transport to the office, plus €0.23 per km for car and bicycle travel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eligible employees can work from another country for up to 8 weeks per year.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Career &amp;amp; Development&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow with our &quot;Learning Never Stops&quot; mindset: participate in Pantry Staple trainings, access internal/external opportunities, and join our cross-market mentoring program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture &amp;amp; Environment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoy fresh homemade lunches in the office (€3.00/day), weekly &lt;em&gt;vrij-mi-bo&lt;/em&gt; (Friday drinks), quarterly strategy sessions, and team events.&lt;/li&gt;
